hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"29059","(29059) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Jabir, and Ibn Salem, On the authority of Amer, they said: Whoever slanders Ibn al-Mala’an will be flogged."
"29060","(29060) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawoos; Concerning the man who says to the son of the cursed one: O son of the adulterer, he said: He will be flogged eighty times."
"29061","(29061) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever slanders Ibn The cursed one is flogged."
"29062","(29062) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Whoever says to Ibn al-Mula’an: O Ibn al-Hannah, will be flogged. The limit"
"29063","(29063) Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: When it was said to Ibn al-Mala``inah: You are not the son of so-and-so who He cursed your mother. He said: The one who says that to him will be flogged."
"29064","(29064) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever accused Ibn al-Mul``an, Or his mother, flogged."
"29065","(29065) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Dulham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Qadhif Ibn Al-Mala’an is struck."
"29066","(29066) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a person slanders it, the one who slandered it will be flogged."
"29067","(29067) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the mother being under the heat and he slandering her, he said: The hadd shall not strike, nor shall he curse."
"29068","(29068) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer; Concerning the mother being under the heat and he slanders her, he said: There is no punishment for them, nor any cursing."
"29069","(29069) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, Mujahid (H) and Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’abi; Concerning a man with a female slave under him, and he slanders her. They said: There is no curse between them, and there is no punishment upon the one who slanders her."
"29070","(29070) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; Concerning a freed slave, he slanders her. They say: There is no curse between them, and he is flogged."
"29071","(29071) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Does Judaism curse a Muslim? He said: No, not even the free slave, but the slave will be flogged."
"29072","(29072) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Aamir; In the case of a slave woman, she has a free woman, and she brings a child, but he is separated from him. He said: He will be beaten, and there will be no cursing between them. And the child clings to it.\n Amer said, and Al-Hakam: In the heat, there was a mother-in-law, and she brought a child, but he was separated from him, saying: There is no curse between them, and the child will cling to him."
"29073","(29073) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the slave, if he is under a free woman, if he hurls it, he will be flogged, and he shall not be cursed, and if he is free, he will be subjected to a slave. So he squirts it, then he shall not be flogged, nor shall he be cursed. And if there is a slave beneath him who is a slave woman and he slanders her, then he shall not be flogged, nor shall he be cursed. He cursed you"
"29074","(29074) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; There are four people who testified against a man who had divorced his wife three times, but he denied it and admitted that he had cheated on a woman, so he said: There is no punishment. Because he is a quarrel."
"29075","(29075) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, and this is the saying of his leaders; They both said: He will separate them with thirty-two testimony, and he will be stoned with four testimony."
"29076","(29076) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, he said: They reported on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Omar, he said: It differs He testified between them for four or more days, and if he repeats it, he will be stoned."
"29077","(29077) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, he said: They prophesied on the authority of Abraham, he said: He will separate them with evidence. Four, and more than that is stoning."
"29078","(29078) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a man who had witnesses testify that he had divorced his wife three times, but he denied that, and that he had cheated on her? He said: Al-Sha’bi said: The punishment will be avoided because of his denial."
"29079","(29079) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who divorced his wife and had two witnesses testify, then he came to the village where the woman was, and he cheated on her and admitted that He had been married to her, and he denied that he had divorced her, so Ataa said: Their testimony is permissible, and he should separate them, and there is no punishment for him."
"29080","(29080) Abdou told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; That a man divorced his wife three times, then had sexual intercourse with her after that, and Ammar was asked about that? He said: If I am able to do this, I will stone you to death."
"29081","(29081) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ammar; In the same way"
"29082","(29082) Humaid and Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Issa bin Asim, who said: A people set out on a journey. So they passed by a man and went down to him, and he divorced his wife three times, so the people continued on their journey, then they returned and found him with her, so they brought him To Shurayh, and they said: This man divorced his wife three times and we found him with her. He denied it, so he said: Do you bear witness that he is an adulterer? So they repeated the words to him as they had said, and he said: Do you bear witness that he is an adulterer? So they attacked him again, so he separated them, but did not challenge them, but he accepted their testimony."
"29083","(29083) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who says to another man: So-and-so told me that you committed adultery. He said: There is no punishment for him because he added it to someone else."
"29084","(29084) Hushaym told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; That a man said to another man: So-and-so claimed that you were an adulterer. He said: If he brings the clear evidence, otherwise the punishment will be struck."
"29085","(29085) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: Because I disrupt the punishments. It is more beloved to me to have doubts than to establish them in doubts."
"29086","(29086) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father; That Muadh, Abdullah bin Masoud, and Uqba bin Aamer said: If there is suspicion that a punishment has been committed against you, remove it."
"29087","(29087) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab; That a woman committed adultery, and Omar said: I saw that she was praying during the night, and she humbled herself, then she knelt down and prostrated, and then some deceiver of deceit came upon her. So they frowned at her, so Omar sent for her, and she said as Omar said, so he let her go."
"29088","(29088) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say, “Avert punishments from the servants of God.” As much as you can"
"29089","(29089) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Push the limits for every person."
"29090","(29090) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Avert killing and flogging. On behalf of the Muslims as much as you can."
"29091","(29091) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He said: Expel the confessors."
"29092","(29092) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Musa said: I came and I In Yemen, with a woman who became pregnant, so you asked her? She said: What do you ask about a pregnant woman who is married to someone other than her husband? By God, I have never been with a friend, nor have I been with a friend since I converted to Islam, but between us I was sleeping in the courtyard of my house, and by God I did not The only thing that woke me up was a man who danced with me and threw something like a gray hair into my stomach. Then I looked at him, singing. I don’t know who he is among God’s creation. So I wrote about it to Omar, and Omar wrote: And consume me with it, and with people of its people. He said: So we brought it to you at the appointed time, so he said: Similar to anger: Perhaps you have preceded me in something of the matter of women? He said: I said: No, she is with me and some of her people. So he asked her, and she told him as she told me. Then he asked her people. So they praised her better, he said: Then Omar said: A young man who sleeps, as he used to do, so he passed by her, clothed her, and instructed her. Treat her well."
"29093","(29093) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of al-Nazzal ibn Sabara, he said: While we were in Minna with Omar, a huge woman on a donkey was crying. People almost killed her because of the crowding. They say: You committed adultery. When she came to Omar, he said: What makes you cry? The woman may have been forced to say: I was a woman with a heavy head, and God was providing me with the ability to pray the night. So I prayed all night and then went to sleep. By God, nothing woke me up except the man who had put me on his knees. I looked at him and said, “I don’t know who.” He is one of God’s creation, so Omar said: If I killed this, I would fear that fire would be upon the two woods. Then he wrote to the nations: Not a soul should be killed. Without it"
"29094","(29094) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad al-Basri, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: Avert the punishments from the Muslims as much as you can, and if you find a way out for the Muslim, then let him go, for the Imam It is better to make a mistake in pardon than to make a mistake in punishment. (Tirmidhi 1424, Hakim 384)"
"29095","(29095) Abu Bakr bin Ayash and Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever brings an animal, there is no punishment for him. (Abu Dawud 4460)"
"29096","(29096) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Regarding whoever brings an animal, he said: He will be flogged, but his punishment will not reach the level of punishment."
"29097","(29097) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the one who comes to animals, he said: He will be punished."
"29098","(29098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no punishment upon the one who brings an animal, nor upon him. Who threw it away?"
"29099","(29099) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: It is not upon anyone He brought a wild animal."
"29100","(29100) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever commits sexual intercourse with an animal, there is no punishment for him."
"29101","(29101) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; He said: If a man has intercourse with an animal, the punishment will be imposed on him."
"29102","(29102) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Rahbi, on the authority of Ikrimah said: Al-Hassan bin Ali was asked about a man who brought his animal. He said: If he is married, he will be stoned."
"29103","(29103) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Farwa, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin left; He used to carry out the punishment on him."
"29104","(29104) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Who are the animals and the boy being brought to? He said: The punishment is upon him."
"29105","(29105) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man falls on animals, he will be flogged. The punishment is complete, and whoever attacks a woman with animals is subject to the punishment."
"29106","(29106) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Masruq; Concerning the one who comes to animals, he said: When he treats them, he says: They were slaughtered."
"29107","(29107) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, who said: Masruq said: He will be stoned and the stones with which he was stoned will be stoned. And its effect will be removed, meaning in the one who has sex with animals."
"29108","(29108) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Whoever has intercourse with animals, the punishment will be imposed on him."
"29109","(29109) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: Whoever brings an animal that does not stand for it Resurrection"
"29110","(29110) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the one who comes to animals, he said: On him is the lower of the two limits, whether he is guarded or not guarded."
"29111","(29111) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Ismail, on the authority of Dawud ibn Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Kill the one who commits animal and animal damage. \n(Abu Dawud 4459. Hakim 355)"
"29112","(29112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Umayr bin Numayr, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about A female slave was between two men, and one of them had intercourse with her? He said: There is no punishment for him. He is a traitor. Someone will attack him and take it."
"29113","(29113) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning a slave girl who was between two men, and one of them fell upon her and said: He will strike ninety-nine lashes."
"29114","(29114) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdi, on the authority of Shurayh; He averted the punishment from him, and guaranteed it."
"29115","(29115) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the mother, she will be among the partners, and one of them will fall on her. He said: He will be struck by a hundred."
"29116","(29116) Rawad bin Al-Jarrah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul; There was a female servant among three people, and one of them had sexual intercourse with her, and he said: The nearest of the two borders is one hundred, and one third is for him. One-eighth, two-thirds of her dowry, and the value of the child, if any."
"29117","(29117) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will be punished, and he will be attacked."
"29118","(29118) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: We have been informed that Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz came. With a female slave who was between two men, and one of them had intercourse with her, so he consulted Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab about her, and Sa`id ibn Jubair, and Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, and they said: We think that he should be flogged without the punishment, and they evaluated it in value, so he should be given to a partner. Half the value"
"29119","(29119) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus; Concerning a man who has intercourse with a female slave between him and his partner, he said: She shall stand up against him."
"29120","(29120) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a maid who was between two men, and one of them had intercourse with her, and she became pregnant. He said: She should stand up against him."
"29121","(29121) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning the slave girl, who was between two men, and one of them had intercourse with her. He said: He must be punished with pebbles."
"29122","(29122) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He said about a man who had intercourse with a slave girl from among the camels. He said: There is no punishment for him, he has a share in her."
"29123","(29123) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: There is no punishment for him, if he is He has a share in it."
"29124","(29124) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Bukair bin Dawud; That Ali performed the five-part punishment on a man who had intercourse with his female slave."
"29125","(29125) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he has anything in the matter, he will be punished. And she is in charge of him, and likewise in a maidservant between him and a man."
"29126","(29126) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Habib bin Salem; That a man had intercourse with his neighbour’s wife, so his wife went to Al-Nu’man bin Bashir and informed him, and he said: As for me, That is comprehensive news. I narrated it on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If you permit him, I will flog him for a hundred times. If you did not permit him, you would stone him. (Tirmidhi 1452, Ahmad 277)"
"29127","(29127) Ali Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A woman came to Ali and said: My husband had sex with my daughter and said: If you are telling the truth, we will stone you, and if you are lying, we will flog you. Then the people beat you. Until they mixed together, and the woman went away."
"29128","(29128) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Mubarak bin Amara, who said: A woman came to Ali, and she said: Oh, by her, her husband had intercourse with her maid, and he said: If you are truthful, we will stone him. We flog you as a liar."
"29129","(29129) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Omar said: I will not bring a man who has intercourse with his maidservant, his wife. Otherwise I did it and I did it."
"29130","(29130) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; When they were asked about a man having intercourse with his maidservant, his wife, they would recite these verses: {And those who care for their private parts. They guard only their wives, or those whom their faith possesses, for they are not to be blamed."
"29131","(29131) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Salman, who said: I heard Ibrahim, saying: Ta’zir and no punishment."
"29132","(29132) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ma’abad, and Ubaid Banu Hamran, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; He struck him beyond punishment."
"29133","(29133) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Alqamī said: I do not care if I have intercourse with my maidservant, his wife, or his maidservant. Awsaja, a man from the neighborhood."
"29134","(29134) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife’s maid, he said: I do not care whether I come to you or to a maid from the road."
"29135","(29135) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The punishment is upon him."
"29136","(29136) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar said: If I were to bring a man who had sex with His maid, his wife, stoned him."
"29137","(29137) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Nafi’, he said : A slave girl came to Omar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, the raider is having intercourse with me, and his wife is calling on you. He committed adultery, and if I am her, then he has forbidden him from my adultery, and if I am his, then he has forbidden his wife from slandering me, so send to Al-Maghirah, so he said: Do you have intercourse with this slave girl? He said: Yes, he said: From where? He said: And my wife gave it to me. He said: By God, if you do not give it to me, you will not return to your family unless you are stoned. Then, he said: Go to the jealous woman and tell her: If you do not give her to him, we will stone her to her. He said: So they came to her and told her, and she said: Oh, my God, I want my husband to be stoned. God forbid, then they have given her a curse. To him, he said: So he left him."
"29138","(29138) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man came to Ibn Masoud and said: I had a sexual intercourse with Your wife’s maid, and he said: God has covered you, so cover yourself. This reached Ali, and he said: If what the son of Umm did had come to me Abd, I would hit his head with stones."
"29139","(29139) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Haytham bin Badr, on the authority of Harqus, on the authority of Ali; That a man had intercourse with his maid, his wife, so the punishment was averted from him. (Abdul Razzaq 1348)"
"29140","(29140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; He said: There is no punishment for him."
"29141","(29141) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: I fell upon Your neighbour, his wife, and he said: Fear God, and do not repeat it."
"29142","(29142) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Uqba bin Jabbar, on the authority of Abd God said: There is no punishment for him."
"29143","(29143) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aamir bin Matar, On the authority of Abdullah; Concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife’s slave girl. He said: If he forced her to do so, then he is free, and he must pay the same for her mistress. And if she obeyed him, then it is for him, and the same is for her master."
"29144","(29144) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no punishment for him."
"29145","(29145) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salama bin Muhabqq; That a man had intercourse with his maid, his wife, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, averted the punishment from him. (Abu Dawud 4456; Ahmed 467)"
"29146","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:\n(29146) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; A woman got married during her waiting period, so Omar beat her as a punishment without the punishment."
"29147","(29147) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, who said: I said to Sa’id bin al-Musayyab: If he marries her in Did you prepare it intentionally? He said: The punishment will be imposed on her."
"29148","(29148) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Marwan flogged them for forty, then separated them, and Qubaisah bin Dhu’ayb said to him: If only you could flog them lightly, then you could lash them both. Twenty twenty."
"29149","(29149) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a woman. She was married within her waiting period. They said: There is no punishment for her."
"29150","(29150) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: No punishment shall be imposed on the People of the Book regarding drinking wine, nor Adultery"
"29151","(29151) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Not upon the People of the Book. limit"
"29152","(29152) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Raja’, on the authority of Qabisah bin A wolf; That a man had sexual intercourse with his female slave and she had a husband, so Omar bin Al-Khattab beat him with a hundred punishments."
"29153","(29153) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jami’, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, who said: A man was brought to Umar who had intercourse with his female slave and he married her off. So he struck him severely, but he did not reach the extent of his punishment."
"29154","(29154) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man has intercourse with his female slave and she has a husband, then it is He will be flogged for a period of time, whether he is married or not, and if she becomes pregnant, the child will go to bed."
"29155","(29155) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who steals from the treasury? He said: It is cut, and the arbiter said: It is not cut."
"29156","(29156) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim; That a man stole from the treasury, so Saad wrote about it to Omar, so Omar wrote to Saad: He has no severance of it, he has in it. share"
"29157","(29157) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked the arbitrator about a man who steals from the treasury? He said: He does not have to cut it off."
"29158","(29158) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who steals from the spoils, he said: There is no punishment for him, if he has a share in it."
"29159","(29159) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man steals from the spoils, and Something is not cut off, so if it is stolen from her and he has no share in it, it is cut off."
"29160","(29160) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Ubaid bin Al-Abras; That Ali was dividing weapons in the desert, and a man took it while he was looking for it, and a man found it and brought it. Ali, but he did not cut it off and said: There is shirk in it."
"29161","(29161) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Zayd; On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Hadrami, he said: I brought a boy of mine to Omar, and I said: Cut him off. He said: What does he have? I said: Stealing a mirror for my wife is better than sixty dirhams. Omar said: Your servant steals your possessions."
"29162","(29162) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, he said: He came The stronghold of Al-Muzani went to Abdullah, and he said: My servant stole my cloak, so he cut it off? Abdullah said: No, the owner of some of it is in some of it."
"29163","(29163) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Ali said: If my servant steals some of my property, I will not cut him off."
"29164","(29164) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Salim bin Hayyan told us, he said: Sa’id bin Mina told us, he said: It was Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, the wife of Sadaqah Al-Zubair, and she was in a house that no one but him and his female slave could enter. He lost some of his money, so he said to the maid: No one would enter this house except you and me, so whoever took This money? So the maid confessed, and he said to me: O Saeed, go with her and cut off her hand, for if the money was mine it would not be. She has to be cut off."
"29165","(29165) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad, what is the ruling about a man who has intercourse with his mother’s female slave? They said: The punishment is upon him."
"29166","(29166) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no punishment for him."
"29167","(29167) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah; Abu Darda’ brought a woman who had stolen, and he said to her: Peace, has she stolen? Say: No."
"29168","(29168) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of a servant of Abu Masoud, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: A man was brought who had stolen, and he said: Did you steal? Say: I found him. He said: I found him, so let him go."
"29169","(29169) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed bin Abi Aroubi narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil; A thief was brought to Abu Hurairah, and he was a prince at that time, so he said: Did you steal? Did you steal? Say: No, no twice, or three times."
"29170","(29170) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban; That a man had stolen his veil, and it was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Messenger of God, this man had stolen his veil. He said: I don't think he stole it.\n(Abdul Razzaq 1383, Darqutni 102)"
"29171","(29171) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ghalib Abi Al-Dhail, who said: I heard Saba’ Abu Salem, he says: I witnessed Al-Hasan bin Ali, and a man was brought to him who admitted to stealing, and Al-Hasan said to him: Perhaps you have embezzled? So that he might say: No."
"29172","(29172) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, who said: Omar was brought with a thief who had confessed. Then Omar said: I see a man’s hand that is not in the hand of a thief. The man said: By God, I am not a thief. So Omar sent him and did not cut him off."
"29173","(29173) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He used to go on to bring the thief, and he would say: Did you steal? I do not know him except that he named him Abu Bakr and Omar."
"29174","(29174) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Miskin, a man from my family, told me: I witnessed A man and a woman were brought to Ali and they were found in a ruin. Ali said to him: Did you bring it closer? Then Ali’s companions started saying to him: Say: No, and he said: No, so he let him go."
"29175","(29175) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ma’iz bin Malik: Perhaps you kissed, or touched, or had intimate contact. (Ahmad 255. Bukhari 6824)"
"29176","(29176) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no cutting of fruit, nor of increasing it. (Ahmad 463. Malik 839)"
"29177","(29177) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: There is no Any of the animals are cut to accommodate the larvae, but none of the fruits are cut to accommodate the green ones."
"29178","(29178) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Sa`id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is not in any of the fruits. Cuttings, except for what shelters the green ones, and there is no cutting in any of the livestock, except for what shelters the marahs."
"29179","(29179) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: Omar said: It should not be cut off on a single stalk, nor on a year old."
"29180","(29180) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, and Al-Sari bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a man who had stolen food, but he did not cut it. (Abu Dawud 2451; Abd al-Razzaq 18915)"
"29181","(29181) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik, and Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a man who had stolen food, but he did not cut it."
"29182","(29182) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who steals food, or a donkey from the desert? He said: He does not have to cut it off."
"29183","(29183) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz was cut off at a time of Or supplies of food."
"29184","(29184) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Hassan bin Zahir, on the authority of Husayn bin Hudayr said: I heard Omar saying: There is no cutting of the stem, nor of a year of tooth."
"29185","(29185) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said: There is no cutting of the fruit, nor of the shepherd’s livestock, but there is punishment and double the debt, so if Awāha al-Marāh, or al-Jarīn, shall be cut off if he steals the value of a quarter of a dinar."
"29186","(29186) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hanif, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Murah Al-Zarqi; Ali was cut off by a thief from the waist, the waist of the foot."
"29187","(29187) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail al-Hanafi, on the authority of Umm Razin, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Is he unable? These princes of ours should cut off as this Bedouin did, meaning we find you. He cut off, but he did not make a mistake. The man, and he forgoes its consequences."
"29188","(29188) Ali bin Hashim and Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, he said: He was asked about The pieces? He said: As for the man, his offspring should be left to him."
"29189","(29189) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The foot is cut off from the middle of the foot. Detailed"
"29190","(29190) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Ja’far; In the same way"
"29191","(29191) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah; Omar ibn al-Khattab cut off the hand at the joint, and Ali cut off the foot, and Amr pointed to its two halves."
"29192","(29192) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Masra ibn Ma`abad al-Lakhmiy, who said: I heard Uday ibn Udayy speaking, on the authority of Raja` ibn Live; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cut a man’s joint. (270)"
"29193","(29193) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Samurah Abi Abd al-Rahman, who said: I saw with confusion a piece cut from the joint, so I said: Who? He cut you off? He said: The righteous man Ali cut me off, but he did not wrong me."
"29194","(29194) Abu Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah; Omar cut off the hand at the joint."
"29195","(29195) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, on the authority of Ibn Thawban; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off a man’s hand, then cut it off."
"29196","(29196) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, it was narrated on the authority of; Like him"
"29197","(29197) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Sufyan; Ibn al-Zubayr brought a thief and cut him off, so Aban bin Uthman said to him: Kill him. He said: Indeed, you are merciful to him. He said: No. But it is from the Sunnah."
"29198","(29198) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is part of the Sunnah to punish the thief."
"29199","(29199) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, on the authority of Salma ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Hajjiya; That Ali used to cut off thieves, destroy them, imprison them, and treat them. When they were healed, he said: Remove Your hands, and they raise them as if they were red lions, then he will say: Who cut you off? They say: Ali, and he says: Why? They say: We have stolen. He says: O God, bear witness. O God, bear witness. Go."
"29200","(29200) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zuhair bin Muhammad, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, he said: Omar came Ibn Abd al-Aziz was informed of a man who had stolen a bird. Al-Sa’ib Ibn Yazid asked a fatwa about that, and he said: I have not seen anyone cut a bird’s throat. The bird, and he did not have to cut it off, so Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz left it, but he did not cut it."
"29201","(29201) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz was brought. Concerning a man who stole his chickens and wanted to cut them, so Abu Salma bin Abdul Rahman said to him: Uthman said: No cutting them. The bird"
"29202","(29202) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Khaled, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali; He did not kill birds."
"29203","(29203) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard someone from my land say: There is no cutting in a falcon that has been stolen. Even if its price is a dinar, or more than that."
"29204","(29204) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, he said: He used to say it."
"29205","(29205) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Marwan bin Al-Hakam was brought to a people who were hiding themselves. Graves, meaning they are being exhumed, so he struck them and exiled them, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were there."
"29206","(29206) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Nabash was captured in the time of Muawiyah, in the time when Marwan Ali was Medina, so he asked who was in your presence among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Medina and the jurists? They did not find anyone to cut him off. He said: So they were unanimously agreed that he should be beaten and taken around him."
"29207","(29207) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: I was informed that Omar bin Abdul Aziz killed a scavenger."
"29208","(29208) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’abi, who said: A thief will be cut off. Our dead, just as the thief of our living cuts the pieces."
"29209","(29209) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about Al-Nabash? He said: It is cut off."
"29210","(29210) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning Al-Nabash, he said: He is in the same position as a thief, he will be cut off."
"29211","(29211) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about Al-Nabash? He said: It should be cut off, and I asked Al-Shaabi? He said: It will be cut off."
"29212","(29212) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In Al-Nabash, he said: It is cut off."
"29213","(29213) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad and his companions, who said: The scavenger is to be cut down because he entered upon the dead. Her home"
"29214","(29214) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: It should not be cut off, unless there is a door to the grave."
"29215","(29215) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said: The thief is a thief, so cut him off."
"29216","(29216) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj; Masruq, Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i, Al-Sha’bi, Zazan, and Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir used to say about Al-Nabash: to cut."
"29217","(29217) A sheikh whom I met in Mina told us, on the authority of Ruh bin al-Qasim, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The scavenger does not have to cut off, but he has something similar to cutting."
"29218","(29218) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Musab Ata bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father; That Ali brought the Negus drunk with alcohol during Ramadan, so he left him until he recovered, then he beat him eighty times, then ordered him to be killed. To prison, then he took him out the next day and gave him twenty strikes, saying: Eighty for the wine, and twenty for your boldness against God. Ramadan."
"29219","(29219) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majid Al-Hanafi, who said: I was with Abdullah bin Masoud was sitting, when a Muslim man came to him with his brother’s son, and said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman, did you find your brother’s son? He was drunk, so Abdullah said: Tartruh, and psalms, and disavow it, so he falters, and psalms, and disstracts, and he was found drunk, So he was taken to prison, and when the next day came, I came and brought him. (Bayhaqi 318)"
"29220","(29220) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a person becomes intoxicated, he is left until he recovers, then he is flogged."
"29221","(29221) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the imam becomes drunk, he will be flogged even though he is not of sound mind. Reason to abstain."
"29222","(29222) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid; Omar was blowing in the wind."
"29223","(29223) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: Abdullah recited Surah Yusuf In Homs, a man said: This is not how it was revealed. Abdullah approached him and smelled the scent of wine, so he said to him: You deny the truth. And you drink uncleanness. By God, this is how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught it. I will not leave you until I punish you. So he was flogged by the punishment. (Bukhari 5001, Muslim 552)"
"29224","(29224) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam; Someone related to Maimunah entered upon her, and she smelled the scent of drink from him, so she said: If you do not go out to the Muslims. Then they will attack you or purify you. Do not ever enter my house again."
"29225","(29225) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaiki, he said: I wrote to Ibn Al-Zubair, may I ask him about a man who smells like alcohol? He said: If he is an addict, limit him."
"29226","(29226) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: I brought a man and I found him The smell of wine, and I was the judge of Al-Taif, so I wanted to beat him, so he said: I only ate fruit, so I wrote to Ibn Al-Zubair. So he wrote to me: If there is any of the fruit that smells like wine, then remove it."
"29227","(29227) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, and Amr ibn Dinar, who said: There is no punishment for smell."
"29228","(29228) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any limit to the wind."
"29229","(29229) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Malik bin Umayr al-Hanafi, who said: Omar was brought Ibn Maazun drank wine and said: Who is your witness? He said: So-and-so and so-and-so, and Attab bin Salamah, and his name was Attab Sheikh Al-Saduq, and he said: I saw him vomiting, but I did not see him vomiting. If he drinks it, he will be flogged for the life of punishment."
"29230","(29230) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Attab bin Salama; Omar struck him with the hadd, and set him up for the people, except that he said: Hafs bin Omar has been brought."
"29231","(29231) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He was asked about shaving? He said: God Almighty made it a ritual and a sunnah, and the people made it a punishment."
"29232","(29232) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ruh ibn Yazid, on the authority of Bishr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umar ibn Abd Al-Aziz, he said: Beware of shaving your head and beard."
"29233","(29233) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, he said: Al-Ridha narrated to me, meaning A peacock. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever mutilates with poetry is not one of us. (Tabarani 10977)"
"29234","(29234) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: May God make it a bird. And you made him a punishment."
"29235","(29235) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Shaving the head as a punishment for heresy."
"29236","(29236) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Khalas, who said: A man was brought with him. Four, so three of them testified to adultery, but the fourth did not proceed, so Ali flogged the three and beheaded the witness. Aliyah"
"29237","(29237) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, and Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik; Omar wrote about the false witness: He will be struck with forty lashes, his face will be blackened, his head will be shaved, and he will be prolonged. imprison him"
"29238","(29238) Othman bin Othman narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Musab, who said: A man from Banu Tamim was brought to Abdullah bin Al-Zubair. So he ordered it to be shaved."
"29239","(29239) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal; A man came to Ali and he walked with him and said: O Qunbar, take him out of the mosque, and perform the punishment on him."
"29240","(29240) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab; Omar brought a man about something, and he said: Take him out of the mosque, so they took him out."
"29241","(29241) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hakim bin Hizam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Punishments should not be imposed in mosques, nor should anyone be led into them.\n(Ibn Majah 748)"
"29242","(29242) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Dhabyan ibn Subayh, who said: Ibn Masoud said: Punishment punishments shall not be established in Mosques"
"29243","(29243) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (H), and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: They hated to establish Punishments in mosques."
"29244","(29244) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He hated it, or he hated being flogged in the mosque."
"29245","(29245) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawoos, who raised him and said: No. Punishments are established in mosques. (Tirmidhi 1401 and Ibn Majah 2599)"
"29246","(29246) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I saw him, and he struck. A man slandered a man in a shirt, but he did not beat him in the mosque."
"29247","(29247) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Khaled Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Avoid your mosques and establish your borders. (Ibn Majah 750. Tabarani 136)"
"29248","(29248) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The mosque is sacred."
"29249","(29249) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha; He hated being beaten in the mosque."
"29250","(29250) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Punishments are carried out in all mosques, except for murder."
"29251","(29251) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih; He used to establish punishments in the mosques."
"29252","(29252) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who said to another man: Your wife does not have sexual intercourse with anything except forbidden. He said: He lied, there is no punishment for him."
"29253","(29253) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Not the embezzler, Neither the usurper nor the traitor shall be cut off."
"29254","(29254) Abu Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who narrated it, with something similar to it.\n(Abu Dawud 4391, Tirmidhi 1448)"
"29255","(29255) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That Marwan asked Zayd bin Thabit about the khulsa? He definitely did not see it."
"29256","(29256) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali said: The embezzler does not have to cut off any money."
"29257","(29257) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas; That Ali did not interrupt in private."
"29258","(29258) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; That a boy stole a collar, and it was brought to Adi bin Arta, and he asked Al-Hasan about that? He said: No, he was cut off from it, and he asked Iyas bin Muawiyah about that? So he ordered him to cut it off, and when they disagreed, he wrote about that to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so Omar wrote to him: The Arabs She used to call her enemy outwardly, not to cut her off, but it hurt his back and prolonged her imprisonment."
"29259","(29259) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham; A man was brought to Udayyah who had been secretly stealing, so Iyas said: He must cut it off, and Al-Hasan said: He must not cut it off, so Udayyy wrote To Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he said: He does not have to cut it off. He said: The Arabs used to call her adwa al-Dhahirah."
"29260","(29260) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no interruption in the khulsa."
"29261","(29261) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The traitor does not have to be cut off."
"29262","(29262) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The traitor is not subject to punishment."
"29263","(29263) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man came to Shuraih and said: This man stole from me. He said: Who is this? He said: A worker. He said: He who is entrusted with your household is not a thief."
"29264","(29264) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no severance in betrayal."
"29265","(29265) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a boy who was with some people in the market, and he stole some of their belongings, and he said: He is a traitor, and there is no severance against him."
"29266","(29266) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar was brought to a man for punishment, so he was brought with a whip. He said: I want something softer than this, so he was brought with a whip that was softer. He said: I want it softer than this, so he was brought with a whip that was softer. The two whips, and he said: Strike, and let your armpit not be seen, and give every member his due."
"29267","(29267) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majid, on the authority of Abdullah; He called an executioner, and he said: Flog, raise your hand, and give every member his due rights. He said: The punishment beat him severely, not severely."
"29268","(29268) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Al-Muhajir ibn Umayrah, on the authority of Ali, He said: A man was brought who was drunk, or in a state of distress, and he said: Strike, and give every member his due, and beware of shame and gossip."
"29269","(29269) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Abu Barzah carrying out the punishment on me. His mother was in Delhi, and a group of his companions were with him, so he said: Flog her between two skins, not by rubbing. And not by easing it."
"29270","(29270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: The executioner does not pull out his armpits."
"29271","(29271) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I witnessed Al-Sha’bi attack a Christian who had slandered a Muslim, so he said: Strike. And give every member his due, and do not let them see your armpit."
"29272","(29272) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The punishment for slander is punishment, and the punishment for alcohol is flogging. And do not raise your hand."
"29273","(29273) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The adulterer shall be severely beaten, and the beating shall be divided between His organs"
"29274","(29274) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The punishment for adultery is more severe than the punishment for alcohol, and the punishment for alcohol And the lie is one."
"29275","(29275) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The adulterer will be beaten more severely than the drinker, and he will be beaten The one who drinks is more severe than the one who slanders him."
"29276","(29276) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali Al-Sadusi, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: He was commanded With a whip, its fruit was cut, then it was struck between two stones, then beaten with it. I said to Anas: In whose time was this? He said: In the time of Omar bin Al-Khattab."
"29277","(29277) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majid, on the authority of Abdullah; He called for a whip and cracked his fruit until it filled his mouth. He called for an executioner and said: Flog."
"29278","(29278) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a man who had injured someone, and a new, strong whip was brought to him, and he said: Without this, He was brought with a broken, spread whip, and he said: Above this. Then he was brought with a whip that had become damaged, meaning it had become soft, and he said: This. (Malik 12)"
"29279","(29279) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: If the deceit is found in a man, He was taken and flogged, his head and beard were shaved, and everything he had on his journey except animals was taken and burned. He departed, and he never took any stock from the Muslims. He said: And he informed me; That Abu Bakr and Omar used to do it."
"29280","(29280) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no cut in the ghouls."
"29281","(29281) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no definiteness in the deception."
"29282","(29282) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning deception, if it is found with a man: his saddlebags will be burned."
"29283","(29283) Dawud bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Muhammad bin Zaydah, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever you find has committed adultery, burn his belongings. (Abu Dawud 2706. Tirmidhi 1461)"
"29284","(29284) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali was given About a man who drank wine during Ramadan. He was subjected to eighty lashes and twenty punishments."
"29285","(29285) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Sinan al-Bakri, who said: A man was brought to Umar who drank wine during Ramadan. So he struck him eighty times, and comforted him twenty."
"29286","(29286) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah, the same as him."
"29287","(29287) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the Jew and the Christian: If he was chaste in his company, then he converted to Islam, then he committed an indecent act before he was chaste in it. Islam, he said: He will be stoned."
"29288","(29288) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Jew and the Christian are distinguished in their polytheism. Ihsan, and the Magians are not Ihsan."
"29289","(29289) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; There were four witnesses against a woman committing adultery, one of whom was her husband. He said: He curses the husband, and all three are beaten."
"29290","(29290) Ibn Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, similar to him."
"29291","(29291) Ali bin Musir and Abdou told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When they come all together, The husband is the most rewarded witness."
"29292","(29292) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The punishment will be carried out on her."
"29293","(29293) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The husband is cursed and beaten. The three"
"29294","(29294) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who sells his wife, they said: They will be punished and they will be disgraced."
"29295","(29295) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man who sold a woman while they were free, so they were taken at the bridge, with dinars among them, so he wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote about them, saying: They will be punished and be kept in prison."
"29296","(29296) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning two men, one of whom sold to the other, he said: The sale will be returned, and they will be punished, and neither of them will be cut off from it."
"29297","(29297) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, who said: It should be cut off. His hand"
"29298","(29298) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab; Concerning a man who sold a free man, he said: Both the one who sold him and the one who acknowledged the sale will be punished with a painful punishment."
"29299","(29299) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muammar informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab; Concerning a man who sold his daughter, and the one who bought it fell on her, and her father said: They forced me to sell her the need. He said: They will be flogged, the father. And his daughter, one hundred, one hundred, if she has reached puberty, and the price shall be returned to the purchaser, and the purchaser must pay a dowry for what he took from her. Then the father fines the dowry, unless the purchaser knows that she is free, in which case he must pay the dowry, and the father does not fine him. He will be flogged a hundred times, and if it is an unreasonable slave girl, then the father must be punished."
"29300","(29300) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a woman who sold her sister out of her will, and a man bought her and had intercourse with her. He said: The man’s money will be returned to him, and she will be punished. The woman and her sister, and he submits to her in any way."
"29301","(29301) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A false witness strikes something, and people recognize it. And it is said: This one bore false witness."
"29302","(29302) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A false witness strikes someone who is under forty; Thirty-five, thirty-six, and thirty-seven."
"29303","(29303) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The witness of falsehood will be punished."
"29304","(29304) Abd al-Rahman al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Ja`d Abu Uthman, who said: He was afflicted when a false witness was brought. Beats, beats."
"29305","(29305) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed; Omar bin Abdul Aziz flogged the false witness with seventy lashes."
"29306","(29306) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, and Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, they said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab wrote In false witness; He will be struck with forty lashes, his face will be blackened, his head will be shaved, he will be paraded around, and he will be imprisoned for a long time."
"29307","(29307) Hafs and Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Sunnah passed from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him and the two Caliphs after him, that it is not permissible for women to bear witness within the borders."
"29308","(29308) Jarir told us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about three people who witnessed a man committing adultery, and two women? He said: It is not permissible until there are four of them."
"29309","(29309) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: It is not permissible for women to be witnesses in divorce. And the limits."
"29310","(29310) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, who said: It is not permissible for women to be witnesses within the border limits."
"29311","(29311) Ali bin Hashim and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible for a woman to be a witness in There is no limit, and there is no witness."
"29312","(29312) Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible for women to be witnesses within the border limits."
"29313","(29313) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak, who said: It is not permissible for women to witness blood, and there is no punishment. Blood"
"29314","(29314) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Hammad saying: It is not permissible for women to witness within the border limits."
"29315","(29315) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Sa’id bin Wahhab saying: It is not permissible Testimony of women regarding the punishments."
"29316","(29316) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He should not be flogged in any case of punishment. Except with the testimony of two men."
"29317","(29317) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {And that a group of the believers will witness their torment}. He said: A man was next to him, and Ata’ said: Two men."
"29318","(29318) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {And a group of the believers will witness their torment}. He said: ten."
"29319","(29319) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Three and above."
"29320","(29320) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Abu Barzah beating his mother, and she became unrighteous, and he blamed her for it. She was wrapped in a blanket, and a group of people were with him. Then he said: {And a group of believers will witness their torment}"
"29321","(29321) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, who said: I heard him say: (If He will pardon a group of you. He said: He was a man."
"29322","(29322) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; They both said: Whoever slanders a minor, there is no punishment for him."
"29323","(29323) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no punishment for a boy who has been slandered. He is small, to the point that punishments are imposed on him."
"29324","(29324) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He who prays for someone other than his mother is not obligated to limit"
"29325","(29325) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man who said to another man: You are not the wife of so-and-so, his mother. He said: He did not impose a hadd punishment on him, but it was a lie."
"29326","(29326) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Hammad; Like him"
"29327","(29327) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no punishment for him."
"29328","(29328) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Concerning beating."
"29329","(29329) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Concerning beating."
"29330","(29330) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abi Majlaz; In the Almighty’s saying: {And do not take you for anything that He has shown compassion in the religion of God}, He said: Establishing the limits when they are submitted to the authority."
"29331","(29331) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; In the Almighty’s saying: {And do not take you for anything that He has shown compassion in the religion of God}, they said: Not by killing, but by establishing Him. The limit"
"29332","(29332) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The punishment is to be carried out, but it is not as strong as flogging."
"29333","(29333) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {And do not let it take you for anything He has shown compassion in the religion of God}. He said: Concerning the implementation of the punishment, it shall be carried out, and it shall not be suspended."
"29334","(29334) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, And Suleiman bin Yassar; Concerning a man who marries a slave woman, and he had not married a free woman before her, and then commits suicide. Sulayman bin Saar said: He will be stoned. Ikrimah said: He will be flogged."
"29335","(29335) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He was asked about a man who committed adultery while he had concubines? He said: He will be flogged, not stoned."
"29336","(29336) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A free man should not be protected by a Jew. Not a Christian, not a mother."
"29337","(29337) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, or Abd Allah bin Utba; That Marwan asked him about the heat under which the mother was under, and then he was struck by an obscene person? He said: He will be stoned. He said: Who are you taking this from? He said: We found the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying the same thing. (Bayhaqi 216)"
"29338","(29338) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: A free mother shall not be married, nor a free slave."
"29339","(29339) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and this is the saying of his leaders; They used to say, “With regard to the free woman under the slave, you commit adultery.” The Sunnah is that she should be stoned, but regarding the free woman under the slave woman: No. He will be stoned."
"29340","(29340) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Al-Fadl, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; That Suleiman bin Yassar said: He made her a horse and she made him a horse."
"29341","(29341) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: I made her a horse and I made him a horse. He said: The free man will now be stoned."
"29342","(29342) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I came to Medina, and they had agreed upon a chaste servant. He is free to stone, except for Ikrimah, for he said: He is entitled to half the punishment."
"29343","(29343) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the case of a male slave, you are under a free woman, and a free person is under a female slave, and one of them commits adultery. He said: It is not against either of them. Stoning until they are both free and Muslim."
"29344","(29344) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The marriage of a slave woman is to marry a free woman, and the marriage of a slave woman is to marry a free man. A slave may marry a free woman."
"29345","(29345) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’abi; When he is free, he marries a Jewish woman and a Christian woman, then he commits immoral acts. They said: He should be flogged, not stoned."
"29346","(29346) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zamma, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He did not think that a free woman should be protected, except a Muslim free woman."
"29347","(29347) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha , on the authority of Kaab; That he wanted to marry a Jew or a Christian, so he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that? So he forbade her and said: She is not your protection. (Abu Dawud 206. Tabarani 205)"
"29348","(29348) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not see any polytheist as pure."
"29349","(29349) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Who Whoever associates anything with God is not immune."
"29350","(29350) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If he marries her while she is not a Muslim, she will not be married to him until he has intercourse with her in Islam."
"29351","(29351) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Bashir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, and Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; In Judaism and Christianity, you are under a Muslim, and then he commits an evil deed. They said: He will be stoned."
"29352","(29352) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: The woman should be fortified. And the Muslim Christian."
"29353","(29353) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who marries a woman from the People of the Book, she protects him."
"29354","(29354) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Salem, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about a man who marries Judaism, Christianity, and mothers. Should he be protected from them? He said: Yes, even if it is not."
"29355","(29355) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Bakr, who said: A woman married a slave, and was it said to her? She said: Doesn’t God say: {And as long as your right hands possess it} then this is the property of my right hand, and a woman married someone else It is clear, and there is no guardian, so it was said to her? She said: I am Thayb, and I have taken control of my affairs. So they were brought to Omar, and he gathered the people and asked them? They said: They have disputed with you according to the Book of God, glory be to Him. And Ali said: They have disputed with you according to the Book of God, so each one of them was flogged for a hundred lashes. He flogged him, then he wrote to the Egyptians: Any woman who marries her slave, or who marries without a guardian, is... In the position of an adulteress."
"29356","(29356) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Omar wrote about a woman who married her slave that a separation should be made between them and the punishment should be imposed on her."
"29357","(29357) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, who said: I asked Ata’ and Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, And Mujahid on the authority of a woman who had a slave, and she wanted to free him on the condition that he marry her? Ata’ and Abdullah bin Ubaid said: Free him, but do not join him. Mujahid said: This is a punishment from God and the Sultan. She will leave her, and the punishment will be imposed on her."
"29358","(29358) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Shayban, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, who said: A woman came to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and she said: O Commander of the Faithful, I am a woman as you see, and other women are more beautiful than me, and I am A slave whose religion and honesty pleased me, and I wanted to marry him. So he called for the boy and beat them both severely, and ordered that... The slave was sold in a foreign land."
"29359","(29359) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he says: O son of adulterers, he says: He will be flogged. Hadina"
"29360","(29360) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Makhoul; Concerning a man who said to another man: O adulterer, son of an adulterer. He said: He strikes two hard-edged men."
"29361","(29361) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Ma’iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: He had committed adultery, so he said: Is there no one for this? He turned him away, then he came three times, and said: As for this one, he turned him away. When it was the fourth time, he said: Stone him, so he stoned him. We threw him away, and he fled and we followed him. Amer said: Then Jabir said to him: Here we killed him. (Bukhari 5270 and Muslim 1318)"
"29362","(29362) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, he said: Yazeed bin Nu’aym bin Hazzal narrated to me, on the authority of his father, He said: Ma'iz bin Malik was in my father's room, and he injured a living maid, and my father said to him: Come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So tell him what you did, and he will ask forgiveness for you. He only wanted to do that to make a way out for himself, so he came to him. He said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so perform the Book of God upon me. So he turned away from it, then came to him, until he mentioned it four times. Then he came to him the fourth time and said: O Messenger of God, you have committed adultery, so perform the Book of God upon me. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Haven’t you said it four times, so by whom? He said: With so-and-so. He said: Did you have sex with her? He said: Yes, he said: Did you have sex with her? He said: Yes, he said: Did you have intercourse with her? He said: Yes, he said: So he ordered him to be stoned, so he was taken out to the heat. When he found that he was touching the stones, he went out and was terrified, and Abdul met him. Allah ibn Unais had defeated his companions, so he grabbed him with the help of a camel and threw it at him, killing him. Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So he mentioned that to him, and he said: Why don’t you leave him alone? Perhaps he will repent, so God will turn to him? (Abu Dawud 4418 and Ahmed 217)"
"29363","(29363) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A goat came Ibn Malik went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You have committed adultery, so he turned away from it until he came to him four times, so he ordered He was to be stoned. When the stones hit him, he turned back and ran hard, and a man met him with a camel’s jaw in his hand. He struck him and knocked him down. Then it was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his escape when the stones touched him. He said: Why not leave him behind? (Bukhari 5272, Muslim 16)"
"29364","(29364) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: He came Ma'iz bin Malik, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he confirmed with him three times, so I said: If you confirmed with him the fourth time, so he ordered Because of it, he was imprisoned, meaning he was stoned. (Ahmad 8 and Abu Ali 36)"
"29365","(29365) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A goat testified against himself four times that he had committed adultery. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to be stoned."
"29366","(29366) Shababah bin Suwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: I saw the Messenger of When Ma'iz bin Malik was brought, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hairy, muscular man was brought in his garment, and he straightened him. Twice, then he ordered her to be stoned. (Muslim 1320, Abu Dawud 4422)"
"29367","(29367) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Bashir bin Al-Muhajir narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of His father; That Ma'iz bin Malik Al-Aslami came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Indeed, I have wronged myself and committed adultery, and I “I want you to purify me.” He sent him back, and the next day he came to him again and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery. He sent him back. The second: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to his people and said: Do you know that there is harm to his intellect? Do you deny any of it? They said: We do not know him except in the mind of those who are righteous to us, as we see. He said: So the third came to him, so he sent to them also, and he asked About him? So they told him that there was nothing wrong with him or his mind, so when it was the fourth time, he dug a pit for him, then ordered him to be stoned. (Muslim 1323. Abu Dawud 4432)"
"29368","(29368) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: Ma’iz bin Malik came and confessed to adultery three times, so he asked about it? Then he ordered that he be stoned, so we threw clay, sandalwood, and bones at him, and we did not dig for him, nor did we bind him, so we preceded him. To Al-Harrah and we followed him, so he rose up to us, and we attacked him until he remained silent, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not ask forgiveness for him, nor did he He cursed him (Muslim 1321, Abu Dawud 4429)"
"29369","(29369) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Taifi, on the authority of Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and a man came and confessed that he had committed adultery, so the Prophet turned him away. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him three times, and when it was the fourth time and he descended, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered that he be stoned and cut to pieces. That was the case with him until I recognized him in his face. Then when the anger passed from him, he said: O Abu Dharr, your companion has been forgiven. To him, he said: And it was said: His repentance is for the punishment to be carried out on him. (Ahmed 119 Tahawi 142)"
"29370","(29370) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I told him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I said: After Surah Al-Nour was revealed, or before it? He said: I don't know.\n(Bukhari 6813 and Muslim 1328)"
"29371","(29371) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar said: I feared that It will take a long time for people until the one who says: We do not find stoning in the Book of God, so they go astray by neglecting an obligation that God has sent down. And stoning is valid, if the man is chaste, or the evidence is upright, or there is a pregnancy, or he confesses, and we have read it: {Al-Sheikh And the two old men, when they commit adultery, stone them both absolutely. \n The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned and we were stoned after him.\n It was said to Sufyan: Did the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned? He said: Yes. (Bukhari 2829. Muslim 1317)"
"29372","(29372) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked him about a man who confesses to adultery, how much should he respond? He said: Once upon a time, I asked the judge? He said: Four times."
"29373","(29373) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; That Ma'iz bin Malik came to Abu Bakr and told him that he had committed adultery, so Abu Bakr said to him: Did you mention this to anyone else? He said: No. Abu Bakr said to him: Cover yourself with God’s veil, and repent to God, for people reproach, but they do not change, by God. He accepts repentance on behalf of His servants, but his soul did not accept it, until Omar came and mentioned something similar to what he mentioned to Abu Bakr, and Omar said to him: Like what Abu Bakr said, his soul was not satisfied until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that he had committed adultery. So he turned away from it, and he even said that to him several times. When he did more, he sent to his people and said to them: Did he complain? Is he a jinn? They said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, it is true. He said: Early, or Thayb? They said: Rather, Thayb, so he was ordered to be stoned. (Abdul Razzaq 13342)"
"29374","(29374) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Messenger of God was stoned. May God bless him and grant him peace. He stoned Abu Bakr, and I stoned him. (Tirmidhi 1431. Malik 10)"
"29375","(29375) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said Omar said: Stoning is one of the punishments of God, so do not deceive him, and the meaning of that is that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned. Abu Bakr was stoned, and I was stoned. (Taalisi 25. Abd al-Razzaq 13364)"
"29376","(29376) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Uthman bin Nasr, On the authority of his father, he said: I was among those who stoned a goat, and when he found it, he touched the stones and said: Return me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so I denied that, so I went to Asim bin Omar, and he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Hanafi said: He has informed me. So I denied him, so I came to Jabir and said: Al-Aslami mentioned something from Ma’iz bin Malik’s saying: They returned me, so I denied him. He said: I am among those who stoned him. He said: He found himself touching the stones. He said: Return me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. My people warned me and said: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for he is not the one who will kill you. We did not even stop him from doing so. We killed him, and when his matter was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Why don’t you leave him until I look into his matter?\n(Nasa’i 7206 and Ahmad 431)"
"29377","(29377) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Musawar bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Barza, he said: He was stoned. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man from among us, called Ma’iz bin Malik. (Ahmad 423, Bazzar 3855)"
"29378","(29378) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulaym Abi Hilal, on the authority of Najih Abi Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned, and he stoned Abu Bakr, and Omar, and their command was according to the Sunnah."
"29379","(29379) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Yazid bin Naim, on the authority of His father, he said: Ma’iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so stand up. In me is the Book of God, so he turned away from it, then said: Indeed, I have committed adultery, so uphold the Book of God in me, so he turned away from it until he mentioned Four times, he said: Go and stone him. When he touched him, he touched the stones and became intense, so Abdullah bin Anas, or Ibn Anas, came out. From his beginning, he threw at him with a camel’s back, which knocked him down, and people threw at him until they killed him. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He fled, and said: Why don’t you let him repent, so God will turn to him? O Hazal, or Hazzan, if You covered it with your dress; It was better for you than what you did. (Bayhaqi 219. Ahmad 217)"
"29380","(29380) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, And Zaid bin Khaled, and Shibl; They said:\n We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man stood up and said: I adjure you, by God, unless you judge between us according to the Book of God. He said: His opponent, and he was more understanding than him: Judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission until I say. He said: Say. He said: My son was This is difficult for him, and he committed adultery with his wife, so I ransomed him for a hundred sheep and a servant, so I asked men of knowledge. ? So I was informed that my son was to be subjected to a hundred lashes and a year of exile, and that his wife was to be stoned. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of God. A hundred sheep and a servant will be returned to you and to you.” Your son will be subjected to a hundred lashes and a year of exile, and go tomorrow, O Anis, to this woman. If she confesses, stone her. (Bukhari 2315) Ibn Majah 2549)"
"29381","(29381) Shabab bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatad, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, on the authority of `Ubad. Ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take it on his behalf. God has made a way for them, one garment for another. And the virgin for the virgin, the virgin will be flogged and exiled, and the virgin will be flogged and stoned. (Muslim 13 Abu Dawud 4415)"
"29382","(29382) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Ubayy, who said: When a virgin commits adultery They will be flogged and banished, and if they commit adultery, they will be flogged and stoned."
"29383","(29383) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ubayy; He used to see someone being flogged and stoned while naked."
"29384","(29384) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The two virgins are flogged and exiled. And the two men are flogged and stoned."
"29385","(29385) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, Al-Shaybani, and Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Ali was flogged and stoned."
"29386","(29386) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Omar was stoned and flogged, and he Ali will be stoned and flogged."
"29387","(29387) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Abu Dharr said: The two dishonest sheikhs are flogged. They will be stoned, and the virgins will be flogged and banished."
"29388","(29388) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: If the married man commits adultery, stoning is upon him. The virgin: flogging and exile."
"29389","(29389) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Amer; If a virgin commits adultery, he will be banished for a year."
"29390","(29390) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father; Ali was flogged and stoned. He was flogged on Thursday and stoned on Friday."
"29391","(29391) Shadhaan and Affan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned Ma’iz bin Malik, but he did not mention flogging. (Ahmad 92. Tabarani 1967)"
"29392","(29392) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Bakr; He flogged a man who had intercourse with his virgin slave girl, and she became pregnant with her, so he confessed. He was not impeccable, so Abu Bakr ordered him to be flogged. Then he was banished."
"29393","(29393) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father; Omar was exiled to Fadak."
"29394","(29394) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibn Yasar, a servant of Uthman, who said: Uthman flogged a woman for adultery, then He sent a servant of his, called Al-Mahri, with her to Khaybar, and he banished her to her."
"29395","(29395) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Hayy; Ali was exiled to Basra."
"29396","(29396) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Ali was brought with two of his female slaves. Hamdan, so he beat her and took her to Basra for a long time."
"29397","(29397) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I told him in the time of Ibn Hubaira: Who Where is he denied in adultery? He said: From his own work to the work of others."
"29398","(29398) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was exiled to Khaybar."
"29399","(29399) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; That Abu Bakr exiled a man and a woman who were both menstruating."
"29400","(29400) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Omar was exiled to Basra."
"29401","(29401) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria Abi Imran, who said: I heard a sheikh speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of His father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a woman, so he dug to the side. (Abu Dawud 4440, Ahmed 36)"
"29402","(29402) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer; Ali stoned a woman and dug up to her navel, and I witnessed that."
"29403","(29403) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Bashir bin Al-Muhajir narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of His father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Al-Ghamdiyya and confessed to him that she had committed adultery, so he ordered her to be dug, and a hole was dug for her. He chested it, and he ordered the people to stone it, then he ordered it to be performed and the funeral prayer was performed over it, then it was buried. (Muslim 1323. Abu Dawud 4439)"
"29404","(29404) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman came from Bariq to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: Indeed, I have committed adultery, so fulfill the punishment of God. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned her until she had committed adultery. There are testimonies on her soul. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Take you back. When she gave birth, the Prophet commanded her. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She purified herself and put on her shrouds. Then he ordered her to be stoned, and some of her blood infected Khalid ibn al-Walid. So they took her captive, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade her, saying: She has repented in a way that if a poor person had repented, it would have been accepted from him. (Abu Dawud 249)"
"29405","(29405) Ibn Numir told us, he said: Bashir bin Muhajir told us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraida told us, on the authority of his father, He said: Al-Ghamidiyyah came and said: O Messenger of God, you have committed adultery, and I want you to purify me, and this is an apostasy. When the next day came, she said: O Prophet of God, why did you want me to come? Perhaps you will send me back as you sent back Ma’iz bin Malik. By God, I am pregnant. He said: Either no, so go until you give birth. When she gave birth, she brought him the boy in a rag and said: This is what I have given birth to. He said: Go and breastfeed him until you are weaned. When she weaned him, she brought him the boy, with a piece of bread in his hand, and said: This is it, O Prophet of God. I have weaned him. He ate the food, so he handed the boy to a Muslim man, then he ordered her to be dug up to her chest, and he ordered the people to be stoned, so he accepted. Khaled bin Al-Walid hit her with a stone and threw her head, and blood swelled on Khaled bin Al-Walid’s face, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, cursed her and said: Be patient, Khaled bin Al-Walid. By the One in whose hand is my soul, she has repented. If the owner of a tax had repented, he would have been forgiven. Then he ordered that the funeral prayer be performed over her and she be buried."
"29406","(29406) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to me, on the authority of Abi Qalaba, on the authority of Abi Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; A woman from Gehenna came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: I have committed a punishment, so make it my responsibility, and... She was pregnant, so he ordered her to be treated well until she gave birth. When she gave birth, he brought her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted her and ordered her to go to her, so she tied her clothes on her, then stoned her and prayed for her. Omar said: O Prophet of God, will you pray? Ali has committed adultery? He said: She has repented to such a degree that if it were divided among seventy of the people of Medina, it would be sufficient for them. Can you find anything better than that? She was serious about herself. (Muslim 1324, Abu Dawud 4437)"
"29407","(29407) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: His companions were brought to Ali, a woman from Hamdan. She became pregnant as a result of fornication, so Ali ordered that she be imprisoned in prison, and when she gave birth to her, he took her out on the day On Thursday, he beat her with a hundred whips, and stoned her on Friday."
"29408","(29408) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of his narrators; That a woman was absent from her husband, then he came while she was pregnant, so he took her to Omar, and he ordered her to be stoned, so Muadh said: If it is You have a way over her, so you have no way over what is in her belly. So Omar said: Lock her up until she gives birth, so she gave birth to a boy for him. Two seconds, and when his father saw him, he said: My son, my son. Then he reached that age, and he said: Women are unable to give birth like Muadh. If it were not for Muadh, Omar would have perished."
"29409","(29409) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah, he said: He came. Ali told a woman who had committed adultery, so he imprisoned her until she gave birth and recovered from her postpartum bleeding."
"29410","(29410) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; Like him"
"29411","(29411) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Salih, on the authority of Simak, he said: Dhuul ibn Ka’b narrated to me, he said: Omar wanted to stone the woman who had committed sexual intercourse while she was pregnant, so Muadh said to him: So you are wronging her. Have you seen what is in her? Her stomach, what is her fault? Why do you kill two people with one person? So he left her until she gave birth, then he stoned her."
"29412","(29412) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Zazan; Ali ordered her to be wrapped in a cloak."
"29413","(29413) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sa`id al-Hamdani, on the authority of Masoud, a man from the family of Abu Darda; When Ali stoned his companions, people cursed her, and he said: O people, do not curse her, for she is the one against whom a disobedience has been made. Punishment, it is its expiation, the repayment of debt for debt."
"29414","(29414) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla; When Ali witnessed evidence of adultery, he would order the witnesses to be stoned, then he stoned, then he stoned the people. It was an acknowledgment. He started with stoning, then he stoned the people."
"29415","(29415) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, On the authority of Ali, he said: O people, adultery has two types of adultery: secret adultery, and public adultery. Secret adultery is lest witnesses bear witness. So the witnesses will be the first to throw the stone, then the imam, then the people, and the weight of publicity, whether the rope is visible, or confession, So the imam will be the first to throw. He said: And in his hand were three stones. He said: He threw a stone at her and hit her earbuds. So she turned around, and the people threw."
"29416","(29416) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; Like him"
"29417","(29417) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of the ruling, he said: I heard Amr bin Nafi’, speaking on the authority of Ali, he said: stoning. Two stonings, then the imam will be stoned, then the people, and the witnesses will be stoned, then the imam, then the people, so I said to the arbitrator: What is the stoning of the imam? He said: When she gives birth, or gives birth, and stones the witnesses if they testify."
"29418","(29418) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I said to the arbitrator: Why stone the imam? He said: When she gives birth, or gives birth, and when the witnesses testify, the witnesses begin."
"29419","(29419) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: When Abu Bakra and his two companions testified against him Al-Mughirah, Ziyad came, and Omar said to him: A man who will not bear witness, if God wills, except in truth. He said: I saw a crowd and a gathering. Bad, so Omar said: Did you see the marauder entering the kohl? He said: No, so he ordered them to be flogged."
"29420","(29420) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin ; That people bore witness to a man committing adultery. He said: Then Othman said with his hand like this: You bear witness that he did so, and he put his finger into it. The index finger on his left finger, and he made a knot with it ten times."
"29421","(29421) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, he said: What was the matter of Abu Bakra? And Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, who was, Abu Bakra said: Avoid, or stand aside from our prayer, for we do not pray behind you. He said: So he wrote to Omar regarding this matter. He said: So Omar wrote to Al-Mughirah: As for what follows, a hadith of yours has been passed down to me. If he is truthful to you, then it is better for you to die before today. He said: So he wrote to him and to the witnesses, That they come to Him.\n When they reached him, he called the witnesses and they testified. Abu Bakra, Shibl bin Ma’bad, and Abu Abdullah Nafi’ testified. He said: When these three witnessed, Omar said: Four of the Mughirah were taken away, and Omar’s situation was very difficult for him, so when Ziyad rose He said: He will not bear witness, if God wills, except in truth. Then he testified and said: As for adultery, I do not bear witness to it, but I have seen something Ugly, so Omar said: God is Great, fight them, so he flogged them. When he finished flogging Abu Bakra, Abu Bakra got up and said: I bear witness that he is an adulterer, so Omar went to perform the punishment on him, and he said to Ali: If you flog him, then stone your companion, so he left him, so he did not He will be flogged twice after that."
"29422","(29422) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khaldi, he said: Sa`id bin Artaban, the uncle of Ibn Awn, told me: He said: Do you want to go to Abu Al-Aaliyah? I said: Yes, he said: So tell him: Al-Hasan, Ibn Sirin, and Thabit Al-Bunani testified that a woman and a man had committed adultery. The woman agreed and the man denied? So I asked Aba Al-Aaliyah about that? He said: I met a man from the people of the desires. Al-Hasan will be flogged eighty times, Muhammad will be flogged eighty times, and Thabit will be flogged eighty times. The woman will be stoned with her confession, and the man who does not Something wrong with him."
"29423","(29423) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Jews said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What is the meaning of that? They mean stoning. He said: If four people bear witness that they saw him enter as one would insert an eyelid into kohl, then it may It is obligatory to stone."
"29424","(29424) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If four people bear witness to something, they are forbidden. Their appearance, and their testimonies are accepted."
"29425","(29425) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali said: I do not like to be the first of the witnesses. The four"
"29426","(29426) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man was brought to Ali and he testified against him. Two men said that he had stolen, so he was involved in some of the people’s affairs, and the false witnesses threatened him, so he said: I will not bring a false witness unless I will do it to him. Such and such. He said: Then he looked for two witnesses but did not find them, so he let him go."
"29427","(29427) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad; A woman was brought before Umar, and she confessed to adultery four times, and he said: If you go back, we will not impose the punishment on you, so she said: It is not permissible to do so. I have to do two things: He committed indecency, and the punishment cannot be imposed on him. He said: So he imposed it on her."
"29428","(29428) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar; Omar sent Abu Waqid to her, and he mentioned something similar to it."
"29429","(29429) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Ata’, who said: If he confesses to a punishment of adultery or theft Then he denied what was warded off from him."
"29430","(29430) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, he said: If he acknowledged He has denied it, meaning he who acknowledges the punishment, then takes it back."
"29431","(29431) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a man who confesses to people, then denies. He said: He will be taken into account."
"29432","(29432) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who acknowledges the punishment without authority, and then denies it when it is lifted, not wanting to abide by it."
"29433","(29433) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ismail informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Who confessed Many times he committed theft, or did something wrong and then denied it, and nothing was punished for it."
"29434","(29434) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ziyad bin Othman; That a Christian man forced a Muslim woman to take care of herself, so the matter was brought to Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, and he said: What is wrong with him? This one made peace with you, so he beheaded you."
"29435","(29435) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; A man from the people of Dhimmi, from Nabat, the people of the Levant, poked a woman on an animal, but she did not fall, so he pushed her with his hand and knocked her over. Then her clothes were revealed from her, and he sat down to have intercourse with her. Then he was taken to Omar ibn al-Khattab, and she stood up clearly, so he ordered With that, he was crucified and said: This is not what we promised you."
"29436","(29436) Aswad bin Amir told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah; That Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan was brought to a man from among the non-Muslims who had treated a Muslim woman as a woman, so he castrated him."
"29437","(29437) Al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a Muslim dhimmi asks for it He was killed"
"29438","(29438) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata bin left; Ma'iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he confessed to himself that he had committed adultery. He said: And with whom? He said: With so-and-so. His master was the son of so-and-so, so he sent for her, but she refused, so he let her go, and he took him with what he agreed upon himself, and he did not It is reported that he flogged him to the point of slandering her. (Ahmed 339)"
"29439","(29439) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said: I committed adultery with so-and-so, he said: She is subject to punishment."
"29440","(29440) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salih bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who said to a woman: I bear witness that I committed adultery with you. He said: I will strike him for what he slandered her, but I will not strike him for what he slandered. against himself, except with clear evidence."
"29441","(29441) Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, he said: He will be flogged with two lashes. I said: So if he lies? He said: One person will be flogged, and another will turn away from him."
"29442","(29442) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a woman says: So-and-so committed adultery with me, so do not flog him, nor will he be flogged."
"29443","(29443) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man slanders another man with a woman; He was flogged by two men; A punishment for a man, a punishment for a woman."
"29444","(29444) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man says to another man: So-and-so has committed adultery. Because of so-and-so, there is only one punishment against him."
"29445","(29445) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man slanders his wife with a named man, the punishment will be carried out on him. Ibn Sirin said: There is no punishment for him. The one with which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cursed was his slander against Ibn Sahmā’."
"29446","(29446) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man slanders his wife with another man Named, there was only one punishment for them. He said: Which of them took him by himself? There was no limit to the other. If a woman initiates the act and curses him, the man is not to be struck, and if he is struck by the man then he is not to curse the woman."
"29447","(29447) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who said to his wife: I saw you committing adultery before you were with me. Sa`id said: Punishment, and I will not curse you. Al-Hasan said: There is no punishment, nor curse, because he said that to her and it is with him."
"29448","(29448) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who said to his wife: You committed adultery while you were a mother. He said: He should be punished."
"29449","(29449) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awan, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who divorced his wife once, then slandered her. He said: He will be flogged, not like someone who did not divorce.\n Ibn Omar said: He will be cursed if he is the ruler of the Raj’a."
"29450","(29450) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If a man divorces his wife three times, then slanders her, he said: The young woman shall be flogged, unless she is pregnant, and if she is pregnant, he curses her."
"29451","(29451) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who divorced his wife three times while she was pregnant, then he removed anything from her womb. He said: He will be flogged, and the child will be attached to him."
"29452","(29452) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he divorced three times, then was separated from his children and he had no He is the king of the return, he is flogged, and the child is attached to him. And if he is banished from his children while he is the king of the return, he will be cursed, and he will be banished from him. The child, even if he was never acknowledged."
"29453","(29453) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who divorced his wife irrevocably, and she claimed pregnancy, but it was denied him. He said: May we curse her."
"29454","(29454) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, and she brought a pregnancy, and he was free of it? He said: He said: May the curse be upon him. He said: Then Al-Harith said: O Abu Amr, God said in His Book: (And those who slander their wives), Did he invent a wife for him? He said: Al-Sha’abi said: If I see the truth, I am ashamed not to return to it."
"29455","(29455) Abbad told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who divorces his wife irrevocably, then slanders her. He said: He strikes."
"29456","(29456) Othman bin Othman Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Othman Al-Bati, who said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad used to say about a man who divorced His wife, then he said to her: You committed adultery and you are my wife. He said: Cursed."
"29457","(29457) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who slandered, then divorced three times, he said: May we curse her as long as she was in the waiting period."
"29458","(29458) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the king of the Raj’i people is cursed, And if he cannot take it back, he will be flogged."
"29459","(29459) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Hammad saying: There is neither punishment nor curse."
"29460","(29460) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He is struck."
"29461","(29461) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Makhoul; He said: If he slanders and then divorces, he curses."
"29462","(29462) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the mortgage, he did not see any limit to it."
"29463","(29463) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If you bet your daughter-in-law, do not consent to her. Until you kill her."
"29464","(29464) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Hakim ibn Umayr, he said: Umar ibn Abi Maryam wrote Al-Khattab: Should the commander of an army or his concubines not flog anyone until the path appears, lest his fever carry him? Satan is to join the unbelievers."
"29465","(29465) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Humaid bin So-and-so bin Roman; Abu Al-Darda’ forbade any punishment to be carried out on anyone in enemy territory."
"29466","(29466) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: We invaded the land of the Romans and with us Hudhaifi, and a man from Quraysh was against us. He drank wine, so we wanted to challenge him. Hudhaifi said: Do you challenge your prince? And you have come close to your enemy, and they are seeking you? He said: We will drink it, even if it is in ihram, and we will drink it despite his will."
"29467","(29467) Muhammad bin Sawai told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; And whoever had sexual intercourse with a mahram woman, he said: He beheaded him."
"29468","(29468) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Kill all Whoever has intercourse with a mahram."
"29469","(29469) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to a man who had married his father’s wife, and he ordered him to bring him his head. (Tirmidhi 1362 and Ibn Majah 2607)"
"29470","(29470) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I met my uncle. And he has the opinion, so I said to him? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to go to a man who married his father’s wife to kill him or strike him. His neck (Abu Dawud 4451, Ahmed 290)"
"29471","(29471) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: A man who committed adultery with his daughter was brought before Al-Hajjaj, and he said: “I don’t know why I should kill this man, and he was going to crucify him.” Abdullah bin Mutarrif and Abu Burdah said to him: May God protect this nation. He loves calamity as long as it covers Islam. Kill him. He said: You have spoken the truth. So he ordered him to be killed and he was killed."
"29472","(29472) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I asked him: What did Al-Hasan say about someone who married a male mahram? And he knows? He said: The punishment is upon him."
"29473","(29473) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Araj, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Sayfi; Omar wrote to Abu Musa: “Not to pray for more than thirty ta’zir.”"
"29474","(29474) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Jami’, on the authority of Abu Wa’il; A man wrote to Umm Salama regarding a debt he had owed her, complaining about it, so Omar ibn al-Khattab ordered that she be beaten. Thirty lashes. Some of our companions said: Both of them are badha’ and hiddur."
"29475","(29475) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: The ta’zir is between a whip and forty."
"29476","(29476) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Utbah; Omar bin Abdul Aziz brought a man cursing Othman, and he said: What made you insult him? He said: I hate him. He said: And if you hate a man, you will curse him. He said: So he ordered that he be flogged with thirty lashes."
"29477","(29477) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I was sitting with Omar ibn Abdul Aziz, Then a man came to him and asked him what was the obligatory prayer? But he did not make it obligatory for him, so he said: He is a disbeliever in God if he did not make it obligatory for him. He said: So he struck him between ten and five. ten"
"29478","(29478) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukair bin Abd. God, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu Burda bin Nayar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: He shall not be flogged with more than ten lashes, except in a case of punishment. (Bukhari 6848, Abu Dawud 4485)"
"29479","(29479) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about four people who testified against a man that he was not the son of so-and-so, and four people testified that he was the son of so-and-so? He said: Stay away from these people because they are four, and I am more honest with the others."
"29480","(29480) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Omar said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf: Have you seen? If you were the judge and the governor, and then you saw a human being on the verge of punishment, would you be responsible for him? He said: No, until someone else testifies with me. He said: You are correct, and if you had said otherwise, you would not have succeeded."
"29481","(29481) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard Hammad saying: We heard that the ruler permits his statement What is recognized by him except the limits."
"29482","(29482) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a woman clinging to a man and saying: He did that to me? Al-Hasan said: She slandered a Muslim man, she must be punished. He said: And Abraham said: Your seekers are right. How do you say?"
"29483","(29483) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man to whom a woman said: This man committed adultery with me. He said: She shall flog the man with her slander, but the man shall not be flogged."
"29484","(29484) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father and uncle, and Yahya bin Abi Al-Haytham, on the authority of his grandfather; He witnessed Ali and brought a man and a woman. They were found in the ruins of Murad. Ali was brought to them, and he said: Your cousin’s daughter. And my orphan is in my care, so his companions started saying: Say my husband. She said: He is my husband. Then Ali said: Take him by the hand. Your wife"
"29485","(29485) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, who said: It will be avoided."
"29486","(29486) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It will be avoided."
"29487","(29487) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the mirror, she is with a man and says: Marry me. Abraham said: If this were true, there would be no punishment for adultery."
"29488","(29488) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a man who banished a man from his father. Shirk? He said: He is subject to punishment, because he banished him from his lineage."
"29489","(29489) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That a man from among the immigrants slandered him about the time of Omar ibn al-Khattab, and his mother had died in the pre-Islamic period. So Omar flogged him for his Muslim wife."
"29490","(29490) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a man who slandered another man, and his mother was a polytheist? He said: Have you seen that if a man had slandered Al-Ash'ath, would he not have been beaten?"
"29491","(29491) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa`id al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who says to another man: You are not your father, and his mother is mother, or a Jew, or a Christian. He said: There is no punishment for him."
"29492","(29492) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If a man slanders another man, and he has a mother. Whether he is a Jew or a Christian, there is no punishment for him."
"29493","(29493) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who is absent from his wife and does not have intercourse with her, and she brings a pregnancy or a child. He said: If it is his absence. In a far-off land, it has not been confirmed, and the punishment is imposed on it, and if it is in a nearby land, they will see that he is coming to it secretly. She believed that the child was from her husband."
"29494","(29494) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man slandered another man, and he pardoned and testified. Then he brought him to the imam after that, and he took him as he was entitled to, even if he stayed for thirty years."
"29495","(29495) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin about a man who slanders another man and he pardons them? Al-Hasan said: No, and Ibn Sirin said: I do not know."
"29496","(29496) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ruzaiq, who said: I wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz about a man who slandered his son: Then his son said: If my father is flogged, I will confess, so Omar wrote to me: To flog him, unless he pardons him."
"29497","(29497) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; He was asked about a man whose hand they wanted to cut off, meaning his right hand, so he presented his left hand and it was cut off? He said: Do not cut off the oath."
"29498","(29498) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; Ali has fulfilled that."
"29499","(29499) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning an imam, a thief was brought to him, but he was ignorant and his left hand was cut off. He said: He should be left behind."
"29500","(29500) Muhammad bin Maysar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, who said: Sa’id and I met. Ibn Al-Musayyab regarding a man who, if he was ordered to cut off his right hand, said: If he steps towards the cupper, he will go and cut it off, saying: His hand will be invalidated. And the fuel is in its place."
"29501","(29501) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I divorced a drunken neighbor of mine, so he ordered me to He asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: If the truth befalls him, he will be flogged eighty times, and he will be separated from his family."
"29502","(29502) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Anbasa; Omar bin Abdul Aziz permitted his divorce, and flogged him."
"29503","(29503) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They both said: Divorcing a drunkard is permissible, and his back should be flogged."
"29504","(29504) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: It is permissible to divorce him and flog him."
"29505","(29505) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he frees or divorces a drunkard, it is permissible He divorced him, and the punishment was imposed on him."
"29506","(29506) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Al-Sha’bi say: It is permissible to divorce him, and his back will be painful."
"29507","(29507) Ubadah bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; That Ali and Abdullah disagreed about the mother of a child who had committed adultery, so Ali said: She should be flogged, but he did not deny it, and Abdullah said: She should be flogged. And you are banished."
"29508","(29508) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the child’s mother breaking out, he said: The punishment of motherhood will be imposed on her, and it will be according to her status."
"29509","(29509) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Hammad saying: It is not permissible for one witness to another to bear witness in a limited manner."
"29510","(29510) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible for one witness over another to testify. Retaliation, there is no punishment."
"29511","(29511) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible for a man to bear witness against me. The man within the borders."
"29512","(29512) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, and Atta; They said: It is not permissible for someone to bear witness to another person."
"29513","(29513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh, and Masruq; They both said: It is not permissible for someone to bear witness over someone else’s testimony, and it is not permissible for someone to bear witness to someone else’s testimony."
"29514","(29514) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he flees to the Sacred Mosque, then he is safe. He was injured in the Sanctuary, the punishment was imposed on him in the Sanctuary."
"29515","(29515) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Al-Walid wanted to perform the punishment on a man in the Haram, so Ubaid bin Umair said to him: Do not perform the punishment unless it is He was afflicted with it."
"29516","(29516) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata, who said: If he harms someone other than the Sanctuary, Then he took refuge in the Sanctuary and was taken out of the Sanctuary until he was standing there."
"29517","(29517) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man commits a punishment in a place other than the sanctuary, and then commits The Sacred Mosque, he was taken out of the Sacred Mosque and the punishment was imposed on him, and if he happened to him in the Sacred Mosque, the punishment was imposed on him in the Sacred Mosque."
"29518","(29518) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid; That a man killed another man, then entered the sanctuary. He said: He will be taken and taken out of the sanctuary, then the punishment will be carried out on him. He says: killing."
"29519","(29519) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Saeed (h) and Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata; Concerning a man who is killed, then enters the sanctuary. He said: The people of Mecca will not sell to him, nor will they buy from him, nor will they give him water. They will not feed him, nor will they give him shelter, nor will they marry him until he comes out and is taken for him. (Ibn Jarir 13)"
"29520","(29520) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, who said: If we had found the killer of our fathers We did not kill him in the Sacred Mosque."
"29521","(29521) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who is killed and then enters the sanctuary? Hammad said: He will go out and the punishment will be imposed on him, and Al-Hakam said: He will not be sold, nor will he be eaten."
"29522","(29522) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah informed me that Khalid bin Ma`bad narrated it, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba; They were asked about a thief who steals, and he throws what he stole out of the house, and the goods in which he stole are found. Is the cut off high? They said: He must cut it off."
"29523","(29523) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muammar informed me, on the authority of Khusayf, he said: A people lost some belongings. They left their house, and they saw a breach in the house, so they went out to look, and saw two men running, so they overtook you. One of them had their belongings, and the other let them go, so they brought him and said: I did not steal anything, but this man hired me. The one who got away and gave me this baggage so I could carry it for him. I don’t know where he got it from? Khusaif said: So he wrote about it to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he wrote: That he should be tortured and put in prison, but not He cuts it off."
"29524","(29524) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who took a garment from another man and said: Did you steal it? He said: I took it as a right I owed him. Al-Sha’abi said: There is no punishment for him."
"29525","(29525) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: If you find a person stealing with a bad man, he will be orphaned. He said: I bought it, and he did not specify who he bought it from, or he said: I found it, and he was not interrupted, and he was not punished."
"29526","(29526) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote in a book that I read: If The property was found with the accused man, and he said: I bought it, but he did not carry it out, so strengthen him tightly in the prison, and do not permit him to speak to anyone until The command of God came about it. He said: So I mentioned that to Ata, but he denied it."
"29527","(29527) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr, He says: Whoever raises a weapon and then puts it down, his blood will be shed.\n He said: Tawus was also seeing that."
"29528","(29528) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muammar informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab; That a man struck another man with a sword, but Marwan bin Al-Hakam did not cut off his hand, and that Omar bin Abdul Aziz cut off a man’s hand in... This is in the book of Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik. (Abdul Razzaq 18686)"
"29529","(29529) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ziyad informed me; That Ibn Shihab told him, saying: Safwan ibn al-Mu'tall struck Hassan ibn al-Fura'i with the sword when he attacked him, but he did not The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off his hand. (Abdul Razzaq 18686)"
"29530","(29530) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever raises weapons against us is not one of us. (Bukhari 6874 and Muslim 98)"
"29531","(29531) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: Omar said: There is not one of us who brandished weapons against us."
"29532","(29532) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, or I narrated on his authority, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, In the same way"
"29533","(29533) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever draws the sword against us is not one of us. (Muslim 162; Ahmad 46)"
"29534","(29534) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever raises weapons against us is not one of us. (Bukhari 1280, Muslim 164)"
"29535","(29535) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, Sulaiman bin Hayyan, told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Asama, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us in a convoy, and we made the morning prayers from Jehanna. I met a man and he said: No. There is no god but God, so I stabbed him, and I became distressed by that, so I mentioned it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He said, “There is no god but God,” and you killed him? He said: I said: O Messenger of God, he only said it as a group of weapons. He said: Why have you not split his heart until you know whether he said it as a group, or not? He said: He kept repeating it to me, until I wished that I had converted to Islam that day. (Bukhari 4269. Muslim 185)"
"29536","(29536) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Asama, who said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he mentioned something similar to it. (Muslim 158. Tabarani 394)"
"29537","(29537) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir (h) and on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but God. Then They said, “Prevent me from killing their blood and their property except for what is due, and their account is with God.” (Abu Dawud 2433. Tirmidhi 2606)"
"29538","(29538) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: Whoever is one with God, and disbelieves in what is worshiped other than Him, his blood has been sanctified, and his reckoning is with God. (Muslim 37. Ahmad 772)"
"29539","(29539) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they say it, their blood and their property will be protected from me. Except in accordance with their rights, and their reckoning is with Allah. Then he recited: {So remember. You are only a Reminder, and you have no control over them.}\n(Muslim 52. Tirmidhi 3341)"
"29540","(29540) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, that Amr bin Aws told him, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say there is no god but God."
"29541","(29541) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Jarir, on the authority of Jarir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say there is no god but God. (Tabarani 2392)"
"29542","(29542) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I have been commanded to fight people until they say there is no god but God. If they say it, their blood is forbidden to me. And their wealth is for what it is entitled to, and their reckoning is with Allah. (Ahmad 475)"
"29543","(29543) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amră, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: It came out Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad was on a expedition, so they passed a man among his sheep, and they wanted to kill him, so he said: There is no god but Allah, so he said Al-Miqdad: He wished to flee with his family and property. He said: When they arrived, they mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was revealed: {O you who have believed, when you strike in the way of God, then investigate clearly, and do not say to him who greets you, “You are not a believer.” You seek the wealth of the worldly life. He said: spoils. Then with Allah are spoils of war, even as you were before. He said: You conceal your faith from the polytheists. {So, from God’s favor upon you} Then Islam was revealed, {So understand yourselves} a promise from God, {Indeed, God He is aware of what you do."
"29544","(29544) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He passed A man from Banu Sulaym was with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had sheep with him. He greeted them, and they said: What? He greeted you only to seek refuge from you, so they went to him, killed him, and took his sheep, and brought them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him and grant him peace, then God revealed: {O you who have believed, when you strike in the way of God, then investigate and do not say to whom he threw Peace be upon you. You are not a believer. You seek the reward of the life of this world, for with Allah are many spoils. Until the end of the verses."
"29545","(29545) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, with something similar to it, and he did not He mentioned: They brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"29546","(29546) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith ibn Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Zayd. Al-Laythi, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Adiy bin Al-Khayyar, on the authority of Al-Miqdad; He informed him that he said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if I met a man from the infidels and he fought me and struck off one of my hands? With a sword, he cut it off, then he took refuge from a tree and said: I have submitted to God. Should I kill him, O Messenger of God, after he said it? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not kill him. So I said: O Messenger of God, he cut off my hand. Then he said that after He cut it off, so I should kill him? He said: Do not kill him, and if you do kill him, he will be in your position before you killed him, and you will be in your position before he said The word he said. (Musnad 486)"
"29547","(29547) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: Abu Aliya to me and a friend of mine, and he said: Come on, for you are younger than me, and more knowledgeable in hadith than me, so we set off until We came to Bishr bin Asim Al-Laythi, and Abu Al-Aliyah said: Narrate these two hadiths of yours, and he said: Uqba bin Malik narrated to us. Al-Laythi, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a convoy, who raided the people, and a man from the people joined him and followed him. A man from the group had a sharp sword. The man from among the people said, “Indeed, I am a Muslim.” He did not consider what he said, so he struck him and killed him. Then the hadith was transmitted to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said a strong word, so the killer reached While the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering a sermon, the killer said: By God, O Prophet of God, he who said did not say anything but Seeking refuge from killing, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from it, and sought refuge among the people to distract him, and he did that twice, each That is why the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him, and he did not have patience if the third person said something like that. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to face him, the evening is known by his face, and said: Indeed, God has rejected me regarding whoever kills a believer. Three times he says that. (Abu Dawud 2420, Ahmed 288)"
"29548","(29548) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah said: When someone who reverted to the covenant of Abu Bakr apostatized, Abu Bakr wanted to fight them. Then Omar said: Should I fight them when I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Who bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, his wealth is forbidden except by right, and their reckoning is with God Almighty? Abu Bakr said: I will not fight anyone who differentiates between prayer and zakat, and by God, I will fight anyone who distinguishes between them to the point of All of them together. Omar said: So we fought with him and he was of sound mind. When he defeated whoever of them he defeated, he said: Choose two characteristics from me; Either a shameful war, or a shameful sin. They said: This is the shameful war we have known, so what is the shameful mistake? He said: You bear witness that those who killed us are in Paradise, and that those who killed you are in Hell, so they did so. (Bukhari 1399, Muslim 32)"
"29549","(29549) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, he said: Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Jarir, on the authority of Jarir, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Yemen to fight them and call upon them. They said: There is no god but Allah. Their wealth and their blood are sacred to you."
"29550","(29550) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of his maternal uncle, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: A son of his was beaten while drinking and he was treated kindly by him, so he said: I do not find it difficult for him to hit him. But I find that he circumambulated it, and this is something that the Muslims did not do."
"29551","(29551) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, who said: I heard Malik bin Umayr saying: I heard Attab bin He greeted him, saying: Omar bin Al-Khattab asked me about a man who said: I saw him drinking it? So I said: I did not see him drinking it, but I saw him vomiting it. He said: So the punishment struck him, and he set it up for the people."
"29552","(29552) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who says to another man: You committed adultery while you were a polytheist. He said: He does not punish anyone."
"29553","(29553) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan; He said: If he says: You committed adultery while you are a polytheist, the punishment will be imposed on him."
"29554","(29554) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of an infidel who commits adultery, the punishment is imposed on him and then he surrenders, but a man slanders him and says: I only meant the adultery of the one who committed adultery. Was he in disbelief? He said: The punishment will be brought upon the one who slanders him."
"29555","(29555) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a woman who committed adultery while... A Jew, a Christian, or a Magian, then she converted to Islam, and a man slandered her? Ibn Shihab said: There is no punishment for the one who slanders her, but he will be punished."
"29556","(29556) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man, he exiles a man from his thigh. He said: He should not be beaten, unless he is exiled from his father."
"29557","(29557) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: If he said: You are not from Banu Tamim, he said: He gets hit."
"29558","(29558) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, he said: I heard Shu’bi, he said about a man saying to another man: Oh He committed adultery, and he knew that he had committed adultery. Is he being punished? He said: Yes, God says: {Then they did not bring four witnesses}"
"29559","(29559) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn; That a man said to another man: O Rusbiyah, so Urwah ibn al-Mughirah al-Hadd hit him, and the people liked that."
"29560","(29560) Yahya bin Ali bin Al-Harith narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jami’, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Suleiman, he said: A man was brought to Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, who is a judge, he said: And it was testified that he said to a man: Rusbiyya, so he was flogged by the hadd."
"29561","(29561) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salih bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man saying to another man: O pardoned man. He said: He must be punished."
"29562","(29562) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Al-Walid, who said: I witnessed Ibn Ashhua bring a man who said to another man: Oh effect, so he was flogged by punishment."
"29563","(29563) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He will be flogged."
"29564","(29564) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ikrimah; Concerning a man saying to another man: O effeminate one. Ikrimah said: He must be punished. Al-Hasan said: He is not subject to punishment."
"29565","(29?? 65) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no punishment upon him."
"29566","(29566) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he says: O effeminate man, then he is not obligated to do so. limit"
"29567","(29567) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: Ali said: A man says to another man: O wicked one! He is a sinner, he said: They are immoral, and there is a punishment for them, and do not say them so you will become accustomed to them."
"29568","(29568) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Abu Bakr said about a man saying to another man: O wicked one, O immoral one. He said: He said an evil word, but it is not in it. Punishment, and there is no limit."
"29569","(29569) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, who said: I witnessed Salim and al-Qasim and Amir asked them. Al-Medina, on the authority of a man who said to another man, “You are a sinner”? So they recited these verses: “If a sinner comes to you with news, then investigate.” And they said: The sinner is a liar. He will be punished with lashes."
"29570","(29570) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah; Concerning a man saying to another man: O evil one. He said: This is a bad statement, and there is no punishment for it."
"29571","(29571) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man had said to another man: “Ashraf has summoned you,” it would not have happened. There is a limit on him."
"29572","(29572) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Raqiba, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man saying to another man: You are a supplicant, there is no punishment for him."
"29573","(29573) Abu Issam told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; About an Arab man saying to another man: “You are my master.” He said: He strikes the hadd."
"29574","(29574) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man commits adultery with a boy, he will be flogged. He was not stoned, and there is no blame on the girl. If a boy commits adultery with a woman, she will be flogged and not stoned, and the boy must be punished."
"29575","(29575) Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who lost his youth, he said: She must be barren."
"29576","(29576) Omar bin Ali bin Ata bin Muqaddam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Fadalah Ibn Ubaid, he said: I asked him about hanging the hand around the neck? He said: The Sunnah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off a man’s hand, then hung it around his neck. (Abu Dawud 4411. Tirmidhi 1447)"
"29577","(29577) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; Ali cut off the hand of a thief and I saw it hanging, meaning around his neck."
"29578","(29578) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father; That Ali cut off a man’s hand, then hung it around his neck."
"29579","(29579) Muadh bin Muadh told us, saying: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: The magician will be killed, but they will not be asked to repent."
"29580","(29580) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib; That a grasshopper killed a magician, or wanted to kill him."
"29581","(29581) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad; He killed a magician."
"29582","(29582) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya; The governor of Oman wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz about a witch who had taken her, so Omar wrote to him: If she confesses, or stands up. upon her with the clear proof, so kill her."
"29583","(29583) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; One of Hafsah’s maids witchcraft on her, and they found out that she had done so, and she confessed, so she commanded Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, so he killed her, and the news was reached. That was Uthman, but he disapproved of her and became harsh against him, so Ibn Umar came to him and told him that she had done her magic, and they found her magic. She confessed to him, and it was as if Othman had only denied it because she had been killed without his permission."
"29584","(29584) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd Abi al-Mu’alla, who said: A police officer of Sunan bin Salama narrated to me; Sinan brought a witch and ordered her to be thrown into the sea."
"29585","(29585) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr; He heard about his glory, saying: I was a writer for Juz bin Muawiyah, and the letter of Omar bin Al-Khattab came to us: Kill every sorcerer. And a sorcerer. He said: We killed three sorcerers."
"29586","(29586) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; If the magician confesses, he will be killed."
"29587","(29587) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the magician, he said: He will be killed."
"29588","(29588) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: When he came to Omar, he opened a cover-up. And cover yourself from the land of Basra. He asked them: Is there anyone from the West? They said: A man from among the Muslims joined the polytheists, so we took him. He said: What did you do with him? They said: We killed him. He said: Did you not take him into a house, close the door on him, and feed him a loaf of bread every day? Then you asked him to question him three times, and if he repented, otherwise you would kill him. Then he said: Oh God, I did not bear witness, nor did I command, nor did I approve when they reached me. Or he said: When he informed me."
"29589","(29589) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Ali said: The apostate must be asked to repent three times, and if he returns He was killed"
"29590","(29590) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jarir, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Uthman, who said: The apostate must be asked to repent three times."
"29591","(29591) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of someone who heard Ibn Umar say: The apostate should be asked to repent three times. If he repents, he will be left alone, and if he refuses, he will be killed."
"29592","(29592) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning an apostate, he must be repented. If he repents, he will be left, and if he refuses, he will be killed."
"29593","(29593) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal; That Muadh bin Jabal came to Abu Musa and had with him a Jewish man, and he said: What is this? He said: This is a Jew who converted to Islam, then he apostatized, and Abu Musa Sharin asked him to ask for forgiveness. He said: So Muadh said: I will not even sit down. I will behead him, the decree of God and the decree of His Messenger. (Bukhari 6923 and Muslim 1456)"
"29594","(29594) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hayyan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: He will be called to Islam. Three times, then my father was beheaded."
"29595","(29595) Ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: He said: A gift in a person who disbelieves after his conversion to Islam: He is called to... Islam, if he refuses, he will be killed."
"29596","(29596) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar informed me; Concerning a man who disbelieves after his belief, he said: I heard Ubaid bin Umair saying: He will be killed."
"29597","(29597) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever changes his religion, kill him. (Bukhari 6922 and Abu Dawud 4351)"
"29598","(29598) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; Concerning an apostate, you should be kept safe, and he said: You should be killed."
"29599","(29599) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: Women should not be killed if they have renounced Islam, but rather they should be imprisoned and called to Islam. And they are forced to do so."
"29600","(29600) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the apostate, he said: Do not be killed."
"29601","(29601) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Do not kill."
"29602","(29602) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Do not kill women if they turn away from Islam. Islam, but they will be called to Islam, but if they are taken captive, they will be made the slave girls of the Muslims, and they will not be killed."
"29603","(29603) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In a woman who abandons Islam, he said: Do not kill, be imprisoned."
"29604","(29604) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Do not be killed."
"29605","(29605) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning an apostate: she must be asked to be asked for repentance, if she repents, otherwise she will be killed."
"29606","(29406) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; The mother of a child of a Muslim man apostatized, so he sold her for the price of a jandal, from someone other than her religion."
"29607","(29607) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; In a woman who abandons Islam, he said: She must be asked to be asked for repentance, if she repents, otherwise she will be killed."
"29608","(29608) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: You must be asked to be repented, if you repent, otherwise She killed you"
"29609","(29609) Abd al-Samad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: You shall be killed."
"29610","(29610) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; Ali burned his heretics in the market, and when he threw fire on them, he said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He said: Then he left, so I followed him. He said: : Black? I said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful, I heard you saying something. He said: O Suwayd, I am with a ignorant people, so if you listen to me I say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, so it is true."
"29611","(29611) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ubaid, on the authority of his father, he said: There were people They took gifts and provision and prayed with the people. They used to worship idols in secret, so Ali bin Abi Talib was brought to them. So he put them in the mosque, or he said: in the prison, then he said: O people, what do you see in a people who used to take Do you not have gifts and livelihood, and do you worship these idols? The people said: Kill them. He said: No, but do to them as was done to our father Abraham, may God’s prayers be upon him. So he burned them with fire."
"29612","(29612) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Numan, who said: I witnessed Ali in Al-Rahbiyah, and a man came and said: : O Commander of the Believers, verily here is a family who has an idol in their homes and they worship Him. So Ali got up and walked. Until he came to the house, so he ordered them to enter, and they brought out a marble statue to him, so Ali invaded the house."
"29613","(29613) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos bin Mukhariq, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali sent Muhammad bin Abi Bakr was the prince of Egypt, so Muhammad wrote to Ali asking him about his heretics. Among them are those who worship the sun and the moon, and among them are those who worship other than that, and among them are those who are called to Islam?? ? So Ali wrote and ordered him to attack the heretics. To kill those who claim to be Islam, and leave the rest of them to worship whatever they want."
"29614","(29614) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; It had reached him that Ali had taken heretics and burned them. He said: Then he said: As for me, if I had been, I would not have tortured them with the punishment of God, even if I would have killed them, according to the words of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"29615","(29615) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Ubaid ibn al-Abras, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib; That a man was brought to him who was a Christian and he converted to Islam, then he converted to Christianity. He said: So he asked him about something he spoke to, and he said to him, so he stood up to him. Ali kicked him with his foot, so the people rose up to him and beat him until they killed him."
"29616","(29616) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Saeed bin Hayyan, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dhani, he said: Abu al-Tufayl told me, he said: I was in the army that Ali bin Abi Talib sent to Bani Najiya. He said: So we came to them and found them in three groups. He said: Then our prince said to a group of them: Who are you? They said: We are a Christian people. We have not seen a religion better than ours, so we adhered to it. He said: Seclude yourself, then he said to his group. Others: What are you? They said: We are a people. We were Christians, so we converted to Islam, so we remained steadfast in Islam. He said: Separate yourself. Then he said to the third: What are you? They said: We are a people. We were Christians, so we converted to Islam, then we returned, and we did not see a religion better than our first religion, so we became Christians. So he said to them: They converted to Islam, but they refused, so he said to his companions: When I wipe my head three times, they were harsh on them, so they did so, and they killed the fighter. And they took captive the offspring."
"29617","(29617) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Jews and Christians shall not live among you, except That they submit. Whoever among them submits to Islam and then backs away, do not strike him except his neck."
"29618","(29618) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla; About a man who stole from the Kaaba? He said: He does not have to cut it off."
"29619","(29619) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Mujahid (h) and Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak (h) and Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; They said about the warrior: The imam has the choice."
"29620","(29420) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The Sultan is the guardian who kills whoever fights. Religion"
"29621","(29621) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The imam has a choice regarding The warrior"
"29622","(29622) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; In the mirror, it falls on the mirror. He said: The lowest of the two edges is struck."
"29623","(29623) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Haatibi narrated to us, on the authority of Hafsa bint Zaid, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar; Concerning a woman riding another woman, he said: They will meet God while they are both adulteresses."
"29624","(29624) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: {The recompense of those who wage war is only Allah and His Messenger} He said: If he sets out and fears the path, and takes the money, his hand and foot will be cut off on opposite sides, and if he fears The way, and does not take the money, he is exiled, and if he kills, he is killed, and if he fears the way, and takes the money, and kills, he will be crucified."
"29625","(29425) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I narrated on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, he said: Whoever fights will be defeated. A warrior. Sa`id said: If he injures blood, he will be killed, and if he injures blood and property, he will be crucified, for crucifixion is more severe. If he infects money, but does not If he pours blood, his hands and feet have been cut off, according to the words of God Almighty: {Or their hands and feet should be cut off on opposite sides}, if he repents. So his repentance is between him and God, and the punishment will be imposed on him."
"29626","(29426) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In His saying: {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive through the earth to cause corruption is only that they be killed, or be crucified. Or have their hands and feet cut off on opposite sides.} Until he concluded the verse, saying: If a man fights and is killed and takes the money, then the verses will be cut off. hand and foot on the opposite sides and he was crucified, and if he killed and did not take the money, he would be killed, and if he took the money and did not kill, they would be cut off. hand and foot on opposite sides, and if he does not kill and does not take the money, he will be exiled."
"29627","(29427) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abi Majlaz; In these verses: {The recompense is only for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger}. He said: If he kills and takes the money, he is killed, and if he takes If he kills and does not do so again, he will be killed. If he takes the money and does not do that again, he will be cut off. If he spoils it, he will be cut off. banished"
"29628","(29628) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever treads a private part out of honor, the punishment will be averted from him. And within the land."
"29629","(29629) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Hajimi, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I saw Salman bin Rabi’ He took a man to sleep, laid him down, then beat him."
"29630","(29430) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father; That Ali hit a man while he was sitting, wearing an abaya with two straps."
"29631","(29631) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew and a Jewish woman."
"29632","(29432) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew and a Jewish woman."
"29633","(29633) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned two Jews. I am among those who stoned them."
"29634","(29634) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Al-Bara’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew."
"29635","(29635) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew, or a Jewish woman."
"29636","(29436) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Rashid narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul; A man entered the bathroom; So he took a garment and put it on between two shirts, and said: He will cut it off."
"29637","(29637) Zaid bin Hubab told us; He said: Muawiyah bin Saleh told me; He said: Abu Al-Zahiriyya told me, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’; He was asked about the thief of the pigeons? He said: No, he cut it off."
"29638","(29438) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: Women are beaten without beating, and with a whip without A whip, and their faces will be protected, and they will not be stretched or stripped."
"29639","(29639) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father; He said: I witnessed Abu Barza beating his mother who had committed adultery while wearing a quilt, a beating that was neither violent nor gentle."
"29640","(29440) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amer; He said: Women are not stripped, nor stretched. They are beaten rather than beaten, and lashed without whips, and their faces are protected."
"29641","(29641) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim; A man was brought to Abu Bakr who was not related to his father. Abu Bakr said: Hit the head, for the devil is in the head."
"29642","(29642) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izza, who said: I witnessed Al-Sha’abi and he forbade striking The head of a man who slandered another man, and he was being flogged."
"29643","(29443) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, who said: Ata’ was asked about a man who heard a man slander a man. Shall I inform him? He said: No, you are only sitting in trust."
"29644","(29644) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Concerning a man who slandered his wife, then called witnesses in absentia, he said: It cannot be postponed."
"29645","(29645) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ulatha Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Uqaili, who said: A man slandered another man, so he raised him to the ground. Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so the slanderer claimed clear evidence of what he told him in Armenian, meaning absent, he said: Then Omar bin Abdul Aziz: The punishment cannot be delayed, but if you bring clear evidence, their testimony will be accepted."
"29646","(29446) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr; That a man slandered another man, so he took him to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he wanted to flog him, so he said: I will establish clear evidence, so he left him."
"29647","(29647) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If a drunkard kills, he will be killed."
"29648","(29648) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He will be killed."
"29649","(29649) Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Two drunkards killed their companion, and Muawiyah killed him."
"29650","Abu Bakr said: This is what I learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he judged it and approved the judgment therein.\n Abu Abd al-Rahman Buqiy ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying:\n(29650) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Zaid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He decreed that the child should be put to bed."
"29651","(29651) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided Peace and blessings of God be upon him. In every polytheism that is not divided into a quarter or a wall, it is not permissible for him to sell it until he asks for permission. His partner, if he wishes, he can take it, and if he wishes, he can leave it. But if he sells and does not give permission, then he has more right to it. (Muslim 1229. Abu Dawud 3507)"
"29652","(29652) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled. And he granted intercession for the neighbours."
"29653","(29453) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that the oath be imposed on the defendant."
"29654","(29454) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah that he was asked, about A man married a woman and she died, but he did not have intercourse with her and did not impose a dowry on her. Abdullah said: She has the dowry and she has the inheritance. And she is required to count, and Maqil bin Sinan said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decree the splendor of his son Washiq in a similar manner. That"
"29655","(29655) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfa, who said: Two men disputed before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He gave a camel greeting, and each one of them came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with two witnesses testifying that it was a camel. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided it between them."
"29656","(29656) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, who said: We were sitting next to Sharih when he came to him. A people are disputing before Him about my life. I have assigned to a man his life, and he said to him: He has his life and his death, so he accepted. He appealed to him who had judged him, and Shurayh said: This man blamed me for a matter that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had judged. And he greeted you."
"29657","(29657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Miswar, that Omar consulted people about the The woman, and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba said: She witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he judged her case due to the jealousy of a servant, or Mother, and Omar said: Bring someone who will bear witness, so Muhammad bin Muslim testified for him."
"29658","(29658) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nadhil, On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled on her mother’s mother’s wife, and regarding the pregnancy, Ghura."
"29659","(29459) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, who said: A man came to my father. Musa and Salman bin Rabi’a asked them about his son, his son’s son, and his father’s and mother’s sister, so they said: half is for the son, and what remains. So for the sister, go to Ibn Masoud and ask him, for he will follow us. So the man came to Ibn Masoud and asked him and told him what they said: He said: Ibn Masoud: {I have gone astray then, and I am not of those who are guided} But I will judge according to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided: For the son, half, and for the son, one-sixth, you complete the two-thirds, and what remains is for the sister.\n(Bukhari 6742, Abu Dawud 2882)"
"29660","(29660) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid, Shibl, and Ubayy. They said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came to him and said: I adjure you by God, will you decide between us? By the Book of God, and his opponent, who was more knowledgeable than him, said: Yes, O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God, and permission will be given to me until I say, he said: Say, he said: Indeed, my son was ungrateful for this, and the ungrateful is the employee, and he committed adultery with his wife, so I ransomed her. Of it, a hundred sheep and a servant, so I asked men of knowledge and was informed that my son would be subjected to a hundred lashes and a general exile, and that This woman was to be stoned, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, we will decide between you. By the Book of God: A hundred sheep and a servant will be returned to you, and to your son, a hundred lashes and a general exile, and go tomorrow, O Anis, to Ali. If this woman confesses, stone her."
"29661","(29461) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Saif bin Sulaiman Al-Makki narrated to us, saying: Qais bin Saad informed me, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a decision with an oath and a witness."
"29662","(29662) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, accepted the religion before the will, and you read: {After a testament he makes a bequest or a debt} and that Notable descendants of the mother inherit from the descendants of relatives. (Ibn Majah 2715. Ahmad 131)"
"29663","(29663) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad He said: Rabah told me, on the authority of Uthman, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that the child was for the bed."
"29664","(29644) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Shaybah bin Musawar, who said: Omar bin Abd wrote Al-Aziz, so his letter was read to us, stating that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling in al-Muddahhi with five camels, but he did not He decides other than that."
"29665","(29645) Zayd bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Malik bin Tha’labiya, on the authority of his father Tha'labah ibn Abi Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided in the shrine of Wadi Banu Quraysh that It retains water up to the ankles, but does not retain the upper part over the lower part. (Tabarani 1386)"
"29666","(29666) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled on the Sunnah. With five camels."
"29667","(29667) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id and Haram bin Sa’d that a camel of Al-Bara’ entered the enclosure of a people. So it spoiled them, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled that it was the responsibility of its owners to preserve the wealth during the day, and that The people of the livestock, what happened to the livestock during the night."
"29668","(29668) Abu Asama and Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ghalib al-Tamar, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, On the authority of Masruq ibn Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judged ten fingers of Camels"
"29669","(29669) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, judged the number of fingers ten times."
"29670","(29670) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather that His parents disputed over him to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. One of them was an infidel and the other was a Muslim, so he gave him the choice, so he gave him permission. To the infidel, and he said, O God, guide him. So he turned to the Muslim, and he decided for him. (Nasa’i 6387, Ahmad 446)"
"29671","(29671) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided whether the fetus would be a slave or a mother, and the one who judged it said: Shall he be freed? He who neither drinks, nor eats, nor shouts, nor recites, nor does anything like that become invalid. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is To say the words of a poet, in which there is a delusion: a slave or a female slave. (Ibn Majah 2639)"
"29672","(29672) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, who said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz was read to us, about a bankrupt man. Then a man took possession of his possessions with his own eyes, so he has more right to it than all the other creditors, unless he borrowed something from his own money, in which case he is the worst of debtors. He decided accordingly. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"29673","(29673) Muhammad bin Sawa’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Tufayl Sa’id bin Hamal, on the authority of Ikrimah He said: The number of divorced women is menstruation. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled on the matter according to Ibn Salul."
"29674","(29674) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Aasam, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided There are two cases regarding the slave and his master. It is decided that if the slave leaves the house of war before his master, then he is free. If he leaves His master after him did not respond to him, and if the master left before the slave from the house of war, and then the slave left after he responded to him, Her master (Saeed bin Mansour 2806)"
"29675","(29675) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, Abbad bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is between them, meaning the cursed ones, and He has decreed that she has neither a home nor sustenance for They are separated without divorce, and he has died from her, and it has been decreed that her children should not be claimed by a father and that she should not be abandoned, nor should he be abandoned. Her children, and whoever throws at her, or throws away her children, will be subject to the punishment."
"29676","(29676) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money is his. To the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, this was decided by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"29677","(29677) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that his daughter, Fatima, should serve the house, and he ruled that Ali should be free from The house is part of the service."
"29678","(29678) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: He decided The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used pre-emption in everything on the earth, the house, the maidservant, and the mount. Ata’ said, “It is only Pre-emption in the land and the home, and Ibn Abi Mulkah said: You hear me say, “You have no mother”: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And you say this?"
"29679","(29679) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled for a man from The Ansar were killed by a master of Banu Adi with a blood money of twelve thousand, and about them was revealed: {And they did not resent it except that God enriched them. And His Messenger of His bounty}"
"29680","(29680) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: A man came to Ibn Masoud said: A man among us married a woman but did not fulfill the obligation for her and did not have intercourse with her until he died. Ibn Masoud said: What I was asked about something since I left the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that was more difficult for me than this. He said: So he hesitated about it for a month and said: I will say my opinion about her. If it is correct, then from God, and if it is wrong, then from me and Satan. I see that she has a dowry. Her wives are neither negligent nor extravagant, and she is entitled to the inheritance, and she is entitled to the waiting period of her husband who died. Then some of the bravest people stood up and said: We bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a ruling similar to the one you made regarding a woman from among us who was called “Bru’ of his son.”"
"29681","(29681) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Humaid, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: A man among us took the palm trees of her dead mother, and when she died, he said: I have more right to my palm trees, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made the decision. May God bless him and grant him peace, it is an inheritance. (Muslim 1247)"
"29682","(29682) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Khalid bin Salamah, who said: Muhammad bin Abi Zaydah narrated to me. Abu Dirar said: Two men disputed before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ruled on one of them. He said: So he decided as if he He denies it and thinks otherwise, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am only a human being and I judge according to what I see, so who has I judged? His brother has the right to something, so let him not take it from him."
"29683","(29683) Wakī’ narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhlid ibn Khafāf ibn Ima’ ibn Rahdha al-Ghafarī, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that the slave’s tax is guaranteed. (Abu Dawud 3502. Tirmidhi 1285)"
"29684","(29684) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab, the son of Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, who said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You dispute with me, but I am only human, and perhaps some of you will be melodious. With his evidence from some, I only judge between you in a manner similar to what I hear from you. So whoever I judge for whom I decree anything of his brother’s right, then do not He took it, I only cut off for him a piece of the Fire, and he will bring it on the Day of Resurrection."
"29685","(29685) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Burda. On the authority of Abu Musa, that two men claimed an animal, but neither of them had proof of it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled on it. And he greeted them."
"29686","(29686) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled. He greets the penis if it is cut off or its glans is cut off from the blood of a hundred camels."
"29687","(29687) Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz called me So he asked me about the Qasamah, and he said: It seemed to me that I should return it, for the Bedouin will bear witness, and the absent man will come. So he testified, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, you will not be able to return it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has decided for it. And the caliphs after him."
"29688","(29688) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that the lifespan would be for him and his successor as a test, not for the giver in it. Condition, no exception."
"29689","(29689) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judged the death of his son Hamza. To Jafar, and he said: Her aunt is with him, and the maternal aunt is his father. (Abu Dawud 2274, Ahmed 98)"
"29690","(29690) Abdul-Ala narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a ruling. He said the salaam in the clarification and onwards. In al-Muddahiyah, he ruled for five camels, in al-Manqaliyah: fifteen, in al-Muddahiyah: a third, and in al-Ja’if: a third."
"29691","(29691) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash‘ath, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling regarding the blood sacrifice."
"29692","(29692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, who said: A brother from Banu Zurayq wrote to me: To whom did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, give a ruling concerning Ibn al-Mula’anah? So I wrote to him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had judged him for his mother, and he was in the same position as his father and in the same position. His mother (Abdul Razzaq 12476)"
"29693","(29693) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Khalid bin Arara, on the authority of Ali, who said: When they wanted to remove the stone The lions, they disputed over it and said: The first man to come out of this plow will judge between us. He said: So it was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was the first to revolt against them, and He decided that they should put him in a pit, then all the tribes would raise him up. All of it (Hakim 458)"
"29694","(29694) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Omar bin Khalda Al-Ansari, He said: We came to Abu Hurairah regarding a friend of ours who had fallen into this debt, meaning he had become bankrupt, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a decision. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him regarding a man who died or was bankrupt. He said that the owner of the goods has more right to his goods if he finds them, unless the owner abandons his payment.\n(Abu Dawud 3518 and Ibn Majah 2360)"
"29695","(29695) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Omar ibn Rashid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God decided May God bless him and grant him peace."
"29696","(29696) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Yazid bin Naim, On the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab that Nadhrah ibn Aktham married a pregnant woman, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, separated between them, and he decreed for her truthfulness. (Abu Dawud 2124)"
"29697","(29697) Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that Omar said: Who knows the case of the Messenger of God? May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Al-Jadd, and he said: Ma’qil bin Yassar Al-Muzani is among us. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, judged him. He said hello and said: With what? He said: One-sixth. He said: With whom? He said: I don't know. He said: I don't know, so what do you sing then?\n(Abu Dawud 2889 and Ibn Majah 2723)"
"29698","(29698) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that two women were harmed, one of them stoned the other. So she miscarried a fetus, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided whether it was a male slave, a female slave, or a horse."
"29699","(29699) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Many, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, a client of Banu Nawfal, who said: My wife and I were slaves, so I divorced her twice. Then we were freed after that, and I wanted to take it back, so I went to Ibn Abbas and asked him about taking it back, and he said: If I take it back, that is it. You have one, and two have passed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that."
"29700","(29700) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, who said: I came to Omar, may God be pleased with him, and he With the season, I called out from behind the tent: “I am so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, the criminal, and the son of a sister of ours has suffered among the sons of so-and-so, and we have shown He had to make the case of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he refused? He said: Then Omar raised the side of Fustat and said: Do you know your friend? He said: Yes, and he said: That is it. Go with him until the case of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is fulfilled. He said: And we were talking that the case was four camels. (Abu Ali 164)"
"29701","(29701) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: A woman struck another woman, killed her, and threw her away. A dead fetus. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided to pay the blood money to the killer’s two relatives, but he did not assign her children. He did not owe anything to her husband, and he decided on the blood money for the husband of the murdered woman and her two children, and he did not assign anything to her next of kin of her."
"29702","(29702) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mujahid, they said: Two women changed to impregnate bin Malik bin Al-Nabighah. Then one of them attacked the other with a tent pole and hit her, so she threw up what was in her stomach and died. This was reported to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He spent the blood money on the woman who killed her, and he spent the blood money on the fetus, whether a male or female slave, and he said: The father of the killer, or her paternal uncle: The most detestable is the one who neither eats nor drinks, nor shouts, nor begins to speak, and the like of that is invalid. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: This is what a poet says. Yes, there is an ambiguity in it: a slave or a female slave.\n(Bukhari 67400 Muslim 1309)"
"29703","(29703) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a decree. With the witness and the plaintiff’s oath, Abu Ja’far said: And Ali judged it among you."
"29704","(29704) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling. And peace be upon him, regarding a man who killed another man and was captured by another: that the killer should be killed and the one who captured him should be imprisoned."
"29705","(29705) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi’b narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Muslim Al-Salimi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ramz al-Araj, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that: It is not permissible to say what you think, nor to love, nor to jinn.\n(Abdul Razzaq 15366 Hakim 99)"
"29706","(29706) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash ibn Al-Mu’tamir, who said: I dug a hole in the right hand for the lion, and it fell. There was a lion in it, so people started competing for the head of the well, and a man fell into it and clung to another man, then the other clung to another. There were four people there, and they were all destroyed, and the people did not know what to do. Then Ali, may God have mercy on him, came and said: If you wish. I have made a judgment between you that will be a barrier between you until you come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I will make The blood money is due on whoever is present at the head of the well, so he pays a quarter of the blood money to the first one who is in the well, and a third of the blood money to the second. The third gets half the blood money, and the fourth gets the full blood money. He said: So they agreed on that until they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and they informed him that Ali had been judged, so he permitted the judgment."
"29707","(29707) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If two men sue over you, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says, for you will see how you will judge. Ali said: I am still a judge after her."
"29708","(29708) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to the people of Yemen to judge between them. I said: O Messenger of God, I have no knowledge. With the judgment, he struck his hand on my chest and said: Oh God, guide his heart and guide his tongue. He said: I never doubted the judgment between Two until my council sat here. (Ahmad 888 Hakim 88)"
"29709","(29709) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymiy told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudhayl, on the authority of Al-Mugheerah bin Shu’ba said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, being judged by the jealousy of a male or female slave. Omar said: : To bring someone who will bear witness with you, and Muhammad ibn Muslim testified for him."
"29710","(29710) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Amr Al-Hudhali, on the authority of a man from the family of Homs was one of the companions of Muadh, on the authority of Muadh, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him, he said: How do you judge? He said: Decide by writing. God, he said: If it is not in the Book of God? He said: Adhere to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If it is not a Sunnah from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him? He said: I strive with my opinion. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Praise be to God, who has granted success to the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"29711","(29711) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of his son Hamza, Muhammad said: And this is Ibn Shaddad’s maternal sister. She said: A servant of mine died and left him. His daughter, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided his wealth between him and his daughter, giving him half and half to her.\n(Ibn Majah 2734. Tabarani 874)"
"29712","(29712) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He ruled The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the five pillars."
"29713","(29713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling. With the mind on the nerve, and parents are inheritance. (Abdul Razzaq 17768)"
"29714","(29714) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, he said: He decided The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used pre-emption in everything: the land, the house, the maidservant, and the animal. Ataa said: The pre-emption is only for the land and the house. Then Ibn Abi Mulkaki said to him: Do you not have a mother to hear me say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, and you say this?!!"
"29715","(29715) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arouba narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yasar, and he said: Al-Qasamah It is a right decreed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while the Ansar were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came out of them, then they left from the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and suddenly they saw their companion being covered in his blood, so they returned. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: The Jews killed us, and they named a man from among them, but there was no proof between them, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had two witnesses besides you until I delivered it to you in its entirety, but it was not. We have made it clear to them, and he said: You are entitled to fifty portions, which I will pay to you in full. They said: We hate to swear by someone who is absent. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to take the Jews’ share with fifty of them, so the Ansar said: Messenger of God, the Jews do not care about swearing. When we accept this from them, they will come to us against another of us. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, paid homage to him. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"29716","(29716) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He decrees what is decreed, then the Qur’an is revealed with something other than what was decreed and it is not rejected, and it resumes."
"29717","(29717) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Najrani, who said: I said to Abdullah bin Omar: Convert to Islam in a palm tree. Before he came out, he said: No, I said: Why? He said: A man converted to Islam during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a garden of palm trees before it came out, but it did not come out. Something that year, and the buyer said: It is yours until you get it, and the seller said: I only sold the palm trees to you this year, so they disputed. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the seller: Is there anything better than your palm trees? He said: No. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: For what do you make his wealth lawful? Return to him what you took from him, and do not greet a palm tree until its goodness has been demonstrated. (Abu Dawud 3461, Ahmed 15)"
"29718","(29718) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He ruled The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, concerning a man who bit a man’s hand, so the man removed his hand from his mouth and his folds were torn out, so he set off. The man went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He did not let you eat his hand. He did not pay off any of his blood money."
"29719","(29719) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decreed that if a woman is killed: her children inherit from her, and the mind rests with her female relatives."
"29720","(29720) Shababi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Prophet’s decree was May God bless him and grant him peace: The murderer of one who kills his guardian does not inherit any of the blood money intentionally or accidentally. (Abu Dawud 360, Bayhaqi 219)"
"29721","(29721) Shababi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed in the case that the oath is on the defendant."
"29722","(29722) Shababi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Abu Jabir Al-Bayyadhi, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling about a man changing his testimony. He said: The first one shall be taken into account. (Abdul Razzaq 15508)"
"29723","(29723) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who acknowledges the child, then denies him. He said: He curses the Book of God, and binds the child to the judgment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"29724","(29724) Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Brera’s husband There was a black slave named Mugheeth, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided four cases concerning her. He ruled that Her masters stipulated loyalty, so he decided that loyalty goes to the one who gave the price, gave her the choice, commanded her to observe the iddah, and gave charity to her. With his truthfulness, she gave some of it to Aisha, and she mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: She is truthful. And to us is guidance.\n(Bukhari 5280, Abu Dawud 2225)"
"29725","(29725) Shababi told us, Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Huraira said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a ruling regarding the fetus of a woman from Banu Lahyan who miscarried and died by accident. A slave, or a mother, then the woman whom he had judged unjustly died, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made the judgment. He acknowledged that her inheritance is for her husband and children, and that the mind is upon her upbringing. (Bukhari 67400 Muslim 1309)"
"29726","(29726) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Araj, on the authority of Tariq Al-Makki, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling regarding a woman from the Ansar whose son gave her a garden of palm trees, and she died. He said: Her son: She only gave her her own life, and he has brothers. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Hers. Her life and her death. He said: I had given it in charity to her. He said: That is more distant for you. (Abu Dawud 3552, Bayqa 174)"
"29727","(29727) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, or Ibn Abi Malika and Amr ibn Dinar, who said: We still We hear that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decreed that a dinar and ten dirhams should be taken out of the Sanctuary for a missing servant."
"29728","(29728) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed that the son of Zam’i said: O Sawda: hide yourself from him, and he said: If I had not done this, no man would have wanted to claim you as another man’s son. He claimed it\n(Bukhari 2053, Muslim 1080)"
"29729","(29729) Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather that Two men claimed a camel, each of them sent witnesses, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided on it. Between them."
"29730","(29730) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Juwayriyah bin Asma’ informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd. Mawla Al-Manbid’, on the authority of a man, on the authority of a theft, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling with a witness and an oath."
"29731","Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, saying:\n(29731) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: Zayd bin Thabit told us, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Seek refuge in God from the torment of the Fire three times. We said: We seek refuge in God. From the torment of the Fire. He said: “Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave.” We said, “We seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave.” He said: “Seek refuge in God from the temptations of what What is apparent from it, and what is concealed. We said, “We seek refuge in God from the temptations of what is apparent from it.” He said: “Seek refuge in Allah from the temptations of the Antichrist.” We said: We seek refuge in Allah from the temptation of the Antichrist."
"29732","(29732) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Ask God for useful knowledge, and seek refuge in God from knowledge that is of no benefit."
"29733","(29733) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his swaying, hissing, and his blowing. He said: He is swayed by death, blown by poetry, and blown by pride. (Ibn Majah 808 and Ahmad 403)"
"29734","(29734) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Uthman, and Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam He said: I do not tell you except what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from inability and laziness. And miserliness, cowardice, poverty, and the torment of the grave. Oh God, give my soul its piety. You are its guardian and its protector. You are the best of those who Pure it, O God, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is not beneficial, a soul that is not satisfied, a heart that is not humble, and supplications that are not answered."
"29735","(29735) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Farwa ibn Nawfal, on the authority of Aisha, he said: I asked her about A supplication that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray. She said: He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. And evil that I did not know. (Muslim 650 Abu Dawud 1545)"
"29736","(29736) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: One of the supplications of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: O God, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is of no benefit, from supplications that are not heard, and from a heart He is not humble, and he has a soul that is not satisfied. (Abu Dawud 1543. Ahmad 340)"
"29737","(29737) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from a heart that is not humble, knowledge that is not beneficial, and supplications that are not He listens while the soul is not satisfied, and because of hunger, it is an miserable place to sleep. (Hakim 533)"
"29738","(29738) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is not beneficial, work that is not respected, a heart that is not humble, and speech that is not heard.\n(Ahmed 1920, Abu Ali 2837)"
"29739","(29739) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was saying: O God, I seek refuge in You from leprosy, leprosy, and other bad diseases. (Abu Dawud 1549. Ahmed 192)"
"29740","(29740) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, teaches us these words: O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice. I seek refuge in You lest I be returned to the most miserable life, and I seek refuge in You from the temptations of this world and the torment of the grave."
"29741","(29741) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He prays: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, sin, and debt. (Bukhari 6368. Muslim 2078)"
"29742","(29742) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father He said to his sons: “My sons, seek refuge with words that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with, so he mentioned Like the hadith of Ubaidah, except that it did not mention: He rejected the age."
"29743","(29743) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to seek refuge from cowardice, stinginess, the torment of the grave, the disgrace of life, and temptations of the chest."
"29744","(29744) Shababi told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same."
"29745","(29745) Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to make these supplications: O God, I seek refuge in You from the temptations of the Fire and the torment of the Fire and from the temptations of the grave and the torment of the grave and from the evil of The temptation of wealth and the evil of the temptation of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the Antichrist."
"29746","(29746) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Seek refuge in God from Hell, seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave, seek refuge in God from the temptations of the Antichrist. Seek refuge in God from the temptations of life and death."
"29747","(29747) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was seeking refuge from cowardice and stinginess, from the trials of life and death, and from the torment of the grave."
"29748","(29748) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to supplicate at the end of the prayer, saying: O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave."
"29749","(29749) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Ma’rur, on the authority of Abdullah said: The mother of my beloved, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, grant me enjoyment of my husband, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and my father Abu Sufyan, and my brother Mu’awiyah. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Indeed, you asked God. For fixed terms and numbered days, and divided livelihoods, and He will not hasten anything before it is made lawful, or delay anything beyond It is permissible if you had asked God to protect you from torment in the Fire or torment in the grave, that would have been better and better."
"29750","(29750) Abu Usama narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was lost one night in bed. So I sought him, and my hand fell on the soles of his feet while he was in the mosque while they were upright, and he said: I seek refuge With Your satisfaction from Your anger, and with Your forgiveness from your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You, I cannot count your praises, You are just as You praised me. yourself (Muslim 352, Abu Dawud 875)"
"29751","(29751) Zayd bin Harun told us, Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray With this supplication: O God, I seek refuge in You from worry, sadness, inability, laziness, cowardice, and miserliness. \n(Tirmidhi 3485. Ahmad 179)"
"29752","(29752) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abbad ibn Asim, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, On the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he opened the prayer, saying: God is the Greatest of three, praise be to God. Often, three times. Glory be to God, morning and evening. Three times. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his slander and his uttering. And he blew it."
"29753","(29753) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: I narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from a supplication that is not heard, knowledge that is not beneficial, a heart that is not humble, and a soul that is not satisfied. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of these four. Oh God, I ask You for a righteous life, a pious death, and a return to You. Not shameful. (Tabarani 1435)"
"29754","(29754) Al-Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He says: O God, I seek refuge in You from doubt after certainty, and I seek refuge in You from comparisons with the devils, and I seek refuge in You from torment. On the Day of Judgment."
"29755","(29755) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Aws, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya, who said: Shutair bin Shukal narrated to me, On the authority of his father, Shakl bin Hamid, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Teach me a spell that I may seek refuge with. He said: Say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing, my sight, my tongue, and my semen. (Abu Dawud 1546; Ahmad 429)"
"29756","(29756) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, Musa bin Uqba narrated to us, he said: Umm Khalid bint Khalid narrated to me, that I heard a hadith from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about him seeking refuge from the torment of the grave."
"29757","(29757) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Umm Mubashir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon me. May God bless him and grant him peace. I am in one of the walls of Banu al-Najjar, in which there are graves. Some of them died during the pre-Islamic era. She said: So he came out and I heard him saying: Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave."
"29758","(29758) Ibn Numayr and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Seek refuge in God from the torment of the grave."
"29759","(29759) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was asked about the torment of the grave, and Anas said: The Prophet prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: O God, I seek refuge in You from laziness, senility, cowardice, miserliness, the temptation of the Antichrist, and the torment of the Antichrist. The grave"
"29760","(29760) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhudhail, on the authority of Sheikh Hasba. He said: He was praying in the Ilaa Mosque. He said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from a heart that is not humble, a soul that is not satisfied, knowledge that is not beneficial, and supplications that are not heard, Oh God. I seek refuge in You from these four. (Tirmidhi 3482 and Ahmad 167)"
"29761","(29761) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from the defeat of debt, the defeat of the enemy, and the destruction of the most faithful. (Tabarani 1354)"
"29762","(29762) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He seeks refuge from four things: O God, I seek refuge in You from being overcome by the enemy, from being overcome by religion, from the temptations of the Antichrist, and from the torment of the grave."
"29763","(29763) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to pray with this supplication: O God, I seek refuge in You from the defeat of debt and the defeat of the enemy."
"29764","(29764) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Jalil ibn Atiyya, he said: Ja`far ibn Maimun narrated to me, he said: narrated to me. Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra said: My father told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said some words to the distressed person: Oh God, I hope for your mercy, so do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye, and set all my affairs straight for me. There is no god but You.\n(Abu Dawud 5049. Ahmed 42)"
"29765","(29765) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when distressed: There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, there is no god but God, Lord. The heavens and the Lord of the Great Throne. (Bukhari 6345. Muslim 2093)"
"29766","(29766) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Omar narrated to us, saying: Hilal, the client of Omar bin Abd al-Aziz, narrated to me, On the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, that his mother Asma bint Umays said: The Messenger of God taught me some words I say to them in times of distress: God, God, my Lord, I do not associate anything with Him. (Abu Dawud 1520; Ibn Majah 3882)"
"29767","(29767) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ishaq Al-Jazari, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: Words Faraj: There is no god but God, the Most High, the Great. Glory be to God, Lord of the Noble Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. O God, forgive me. And have mercy on me and forgive me and pardon me, for You are Most Pardoning and Forgiving."
"29768","(29768) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Safwan bin Abdullah, and there was a cloak underneath her, so he went to her and found the mother of the cloak but not the father of the cloak, so she said to him: You want to perform the public Hajj. ? He said: Yes, she said: So pray to God for our good, for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: One’s supplication is He responds to his brother, apparently unseen. At his head is an angel who guarantees his prayers. Whenever he prays for him to be well, he says: Amen. And the same for you. Then I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda’, and he told me, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something like that. (Muslim 2095, Ibn Majah 2895)"
"29769","(29769) Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The best supplications are the supplications of an absent person for an absent person. (Abu Dawud 1530, Tirmidhi 1980)"
"29770","(29770) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Hamid al-Tawil, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, who said: The man’s supplication The one who greets his brother while he is absent is not rejected. He said: And she said: Next to him is an angel for whom he does not pray for good except that the angel says: Amen. But to you"
"29771","(29771) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, who said: I heard Talha ibn Ubaidullah ibn Kuraiz say: I heard Umm al-Darda’ saying: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: A man’s response to his brother is answered in the absence of his brother. Then he did not supplicate for his brother with any supplication except that the angel said: And you have the same. (Muslim 2094, Abu Dawud 1529)"
"29772","(29772) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: When one of you supplicates, let him be determined in his supplication and not say: O God, if you wish, give me, for God does not detest it.\n(Bukhari 6338, Muslim 2063)"
"29773","(29773) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Let none of you say: Forgive me if you wish, and let him resolve the issue, for there is no compulsion against him.\n(Abu Dawud 1478. Tirmidhi 3497)"
"29774","(29774) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Aisha said to Ibn Abi Al-Sa’ib, the storyteller of the people of Mecca. Avoid prostration during supplications, for I made a covenant with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions, and they do not do that. (Tabarani 54)"
"29775","(29775) Affan told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Shayban told us, Abu Nawfal bin Abi Aqrab told us, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, loved the congregational prayers, and he omitted anything in between. (Abu Dawud 1477)"
"29776","(29776) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: If you ask God, resolve For God is not averse to Him."
"29777","(29777) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Yesa’, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Supplications are worship. Then he recited: {And your Lord says: Call upon Me, I will respond to you}"
"29778","(29778) Zayd bin Harun told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever among you has prayers opened for him, the doors of answers will be opened for him. (Tirmidhi 3548)"
"29779","(29779) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever does not supplicate to God, God will be angry with him. (Bukhari 658 and Ibn Majah 3827)"
"29780","(29780) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ali, who said: I heard Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji say: Abu Sa’id said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no Muslim who supplicates with a supplication in which there is no sin or severing ties of kin but he gives it to him. God has one of three things: Either He will hasten your supplication for him, or He will store it up for him in the Hereafter, or He will reveal The worst is like it. They said: Then we will increase, O Prophet of God. He said: God is greater. (Bukhari 710, Ahmed 18)"
"29781","(29781) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, who said: It used to be said: If a man begins with the double Before the supplication, it is obligatory, and if he begins to recite the supplication before the two supplications, then he is in a state of hope."
"29782","(29782) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: I have heard that when a Muslim supplicates, his prayer is not answered. His good deeds are recorded for him."
"29783","(29783) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: They will come to me. People are in a time in which no one will be saved except those who pray with supplications like the supplications of drowning. (Hakim 507)"
"29784","(29784) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhafi, the same as it, except that he said: He who calls"
"29785","(29785) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, and Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Abu Al-Darda'i used to say: Be diligent in your supplications, for whoever knocks on the door a lot, it will soon be opened for him."
"29786","(29786) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thumama bin Uqba Al-Muhallimi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd said: Abdullah said: If there is an imam over one of you and he fears his arrogance and injustice, let him say: O God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of The Great Throne, be my neighbor against so-and-so and his parties and followers, lest they trespass against me or transgress. Honor your neighbor. Glory be to You, and there is no god but You except that Abu Muawiyah added to it: Al-Amash said: So I mentioned it to Abraham, so he narrated on the authority of Abd. God gave him the same, and added to it: from the evil of jinn and mankind. (Bukhari 707)"
"29787","(29787) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, he said: narrated to me. Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: If you come to a formidable ruler, fearing that he will rob you, then say: God is Great. God is more powerful than all of His creation. God is more powerful than what I fear and beware of. I seek refuge in God, there is no god but He who holds the seven heavens. That they fall on the ground except by His permission, from the evil of your servant so-and-so and his soldiers and followers and his associates from the jinn and mankind. Oh God, be my neighbor against their evil, glory be to you, glory be to your neighbor, and blessed be your name, and there is no god but you three times."
"29788","(29788) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir, who said: I was sitting with Ziyad bin Abi Sufyan, and he came. With a man being carried, we have no doubt that he was killed. He said: I saw him move his lips with something we don’t know what it was, so he left. On his way, some people came to him and said: We have brought you, and we have no doubt that you will be killed. I saw you move your lips. With something, we do not know what it is. He said: So leave your way. He said: I said: O God, Lord of Abraham, Lord of Isaac, Lord of Jacob, and Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, and the One who sent down the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Great Qur’an, avert from me greater evil."
"29789","(29789) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Al-Hasan, that Abdullah ibn Ja’far He married his daughter, and he was proud of her and said: If death befalls you, or some of the affairs of this world are terrible, then accept it by saying: No. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds.\n Al-Hassan bin Al-Hassan said: Al-Hajjaj sent for me, and I told them, and when I stood before him, he said: I have sent for you, and I want to I have beheaded you, and there is no one from my family who is more generous to me than you. Ask me what you need. (Nasa’i 10463)"
"29790","(29790) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, who said: If a man is from the elite of the Shu’abi Tell him this supplication: O God, to the God of Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, and to the God of Abraham, Ishmael, and Isaac. Treat me well, and do not force anyone of your creation to do anything over me that I cannot bear. And it was reported that a man came to a prince and said, So he sent him."
"29791","(29791) Zaid bin Harun told us: Imran bin Hudayr told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Whoever fears the prince Unjustly, he said: I am satisfied with God as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as prophet, and with the Qur’an as judge and imam, may God save him from it."
"29792","(29792) Yahya bin Abi Bakir narrated to me, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, On the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’i bin Rafi’ al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Abu Bakr saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said in this heat of the first year: Ask God for well-being and certainty in the hereafter and the first.\n(Tirmidhi 3558, Ahmed 3)"
"29793","(29793) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’di, who said: Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of God. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in the year of the first year, and the covenant is near. He says: Ask God for certainty and well-being."
"29794","(29794) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jalil ibn Atiyya narrated to me, saying: Ja’far ibn Maimun narrated to me, saying: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra told me, he said: I heard my father praying with this supplication: O God, grant me health in my body, O God. Grant me health in my hearing. O God, grant me health in my sight. There is no god but You in the morning and in the evening. So I said to him: O father, I heard you. And you recite this supplication morning and evening. He said: O my son, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicating And I love to follow your Sunnah."
"29795","(29795) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger God, teach me something that I will ask my Lord. He said: Ask your Lord for well-being in this world and the hereafter. (Bukhari 726 and Tirmidhi 3514)"
"29796","(29796) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin A? Bakr bin Abi Malika, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No servant of God has asked for anything more beloved to Him than To ask him for good health.\n(Tirmidhi 3548)"
"29797","(29797) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Shuraih bin Hani, on the authority of Aisha said: If I had known the meaning of Laylat al-Qadr, I would not have asked God about it except for well-being."
"29798","(29798) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i informed us, on the authority of his father, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. A man came to him and said: What shall I say when I ask my Lord? He said: Say, O God, have mercy on me, forgive me, protect me, and provide for me. He added his four fingers except the thumb, for these are added to you. Your religion and your world. (Muslim 2073. Ahmad 472)"
"29799","(29799) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Khams ibn al-Hasan informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Buraydah, he said: She said: Aisha: If I had known which night is Laylat al-Qadr, I would have supplicated most frequently in it. I ask God for forgiveness and well-being. (Tirmidhi 3513 and Ibn Majah 3850)"
"29800","(29800) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, meaning Hilal bin Yassaf said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is an hour in the Friday prayer that a Muslim man who asks God does not agree with. There was nothing in it but He gave it to him. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, what should I ask? He said: Ask God for well-being in this world and the hereafter.\n(Bukhari 9350 Muslim 13)"
"29801","(29801) Zaid bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, that Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban told him That his uncle Abu Sarmah used to narrate, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Oh God, I ask you My riches and my loyal ones’ riches. (Bukhari 662, Ahmed 453)"
"29802","(29802) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He used to say: Oh God, I ask you for guidance, piety, chastity, and wealth. \n(Muslim 2087, Tirmidhi 3389)"
"29803","(29803) Abu Khaled told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, he was one of the supplications of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Oh God, bring the morning and make the night a rest and the sun and the moon a reckoning, pay off my debt and free me from poverty. And grant me my hearing, my sight, and my strength in Your cause. (Malik 212)"
"29804","(29804) Ibn Mushar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: When a man supplicated, he would say: O God, enrich me. And enrich my master."
"29805","(29805) Ubayd Allah told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that He used to say: Oh God, I ask you for security, faith, patience, gratitude, wealth, and chastity."
"29806","(29806) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he often said: O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. They said: O Messenger of God, we believe in you and in what You brought him, so do you fear for us? He said: Yes, the hearts are between two of God’s fingers. He turns them over. (Tirmidhi 2140, Ahmad 112)"
"29807","(29807) Muadh narrated to us, Abu Ka’b, the owner of the silk, narrated to us, Shahr bin Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I said to Umm Salamah: O Umm Believers, what was the most frequent supplication of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if he was with you? She said: His most frequent supplications: O Converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. Then he said: O Umm Salama, there is not a single human being but his heart is clear. Two of the fingers of God. He remains as He pleases, and He deviates as He pleases. (Tirmidhi 3522, Ahmed 294)"
"29808","(29808) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to pray with this supplication: O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion."
"29809","(29809) Zaid told us, Hammam bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Umm Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. I said: O Messenger God, you are praying with this supplication. He said: O Aisha, or did you not know that hearts? Or he said: The heart of the son of Adam is between the two fingers of God. If He wills, His heart will be guided to the guidance of His heart, and if He wills, His heart will be led astray, His heart will go astray. (Nasa’i 7737. Ahmad 250)"
"29810","(29810) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Umm Salama said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And when he left, he said: O God, I seek refuge in You from slipping, or going astray, or being unjust, or being wronged, or being ungrateful, or being ungrateful. Ali\n(Abu Dawud 5053)"
"29811","(29811) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Umm Salama, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted in a similar way. (Tirmidhi 3427. An-Nasa’i 7923)"
"29812","(29812) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: Who said, “When he goes out to Prayer: Oh God, I ask you by the right of those who ask about you and by the right of this person. I did not take him out of evil, nor of arrogance, nor of hypocrisy, nor of hearing. I left it seeking Your pleasure and avoiding Your wrath. I ask You to save me from the Fire and to forgive me my sins. Indeed, I do not He forgives sins, except you. God will turn to him until he turns away, and He has appointed over him seventy thousand angels. They ask forgiveness for him. (Ahmed 21)"
"29813","(29813) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: If a man comes out of The devils received him from his abode, and when he said, “In the name of God,” the angels said, “You have been guided,” and when he said, “I trust in God.” She said: It is sufficient, and when he says: There is no power nor strength except in God, she says: It is preserved. Then the devils say to one another: What? Your path is upon those who are sufficient, guided, and preserved. (Abu Dawud 5054; Abd al-Razzaq 19827)"
"29814","(29814) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b al-Ahbar He said: When he left his house and said: In the name of God, I trust in God, and there is no power nor strength except in God, the devils met each other. They said: This is a servant who has been guided, protected, and sufficient, so you have no way against him, so they will depart from him."
"29815","(29815) Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to pray: Oh God, wash away my sins with water of ice and hail and purify my heart of sins as you purified the garment. white from filth, and distance me from my sins as you distanced the east from the west. (Bukhari 6368. Muslim 2078)"
"29816","(29816) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, Shu`ba told us, on the authority of Majazi bin Zahir al-Aslami, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Awfa speaking, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to pray: O God, purify me. With hail, snow and cold water, O God, purify me from sins and purify me from them as a white garment is purified from filth.\n(Muslim 346 Tirmidhi 3547)"
"29817","(29817) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Habib, who said: It was narrated that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray He says: O God, purify me with snow, hail, and cold water, and purify me from sins, just as a white garment is purified from filth. And put a distance between me and my sins as you distanced the East from the West. (Tabarani 6950)"
"29818","(29818) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he said the greatest thing, he remained silent between saying the great thing and reciting it. He said: So I said to him: May my father and mother be sacrificed. Did you see your silence? Between the takbeer and the recitation, tell me what you say? He said: I say: O God, distance me from my sins as You have distanced between the East and the West: O God, protect me from My sins are like a white garment of filth. Oh God, wash me away from my sins with water, hail, and snow. (Muslim 1498, Ibn Majah 805)"
"29819","(29819) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to us, he said: Habib bin Ubaid narrated to me, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say about the dead: O God, wash him with water, snow, and hail, and purify him from sins, just as a white garment is purified from filth."
"29820","(29820) Waki` narrated to us, Ja`far bin Burqan narrated to us, saying: We have been informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was when he heard The strong thunder said: Oh God, do not destroy us with your torment, and do not kill us with your anger, and protect us before that."
"29821","(29821) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Medi ibn Maymun, who heard it from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, When he heard thunder, he would say: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, Glory be to God the Great."
"29822","(2982) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that when he heard thunder, he would say: Glory be to Him who I glorified Him."
"29823","(29823) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zakariya, who said: Whoever heard The sound of thunder, and he said: Glory be to God, praise be to Him. You have not been struck by lightning."
"29824","(29824) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Aamir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, that if He heard the thunder, left the hadith, and said: Glory be to Him whom the thunder glorifies with His praise, and the angels in fear of Him. Then he says: This A severe threat to the people of the earth."
"29825","(29825) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, he said: I was informed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, do not kill us with your anger, and do not destroy us with your torment, and spare us before that."
"29826","(29826) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Jami’ bin Shaddad narrated to us, he said: It was the lions. Al-Nakha'i Ibn Yazid, when he heard thunder, said: Glory be to Him whom the thunder glorifies with His praise and the angels in fear of Him."
"29827","(29827) Qutayba bin Saeed narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Arta, on the authority of Abu Matar, He heard Salem bin Abdullah narrating on the authority of his father. He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard thunder and lightning bolts He said: Oh God, do not kill us with your anger, and do not destroy us with your torment, and protect us before that. (Bukhari 721, Tirmidhi 3450)"
"29828","(29828) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhari, he said: Thabit Al-Zarqi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hariri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not curse the wind, for it is from the Spirit of God, it brings you mercy. And the torment, but seek refuge in God from its evil and ask God for its good. (Ibn Majah 3727)"
"29829","(29829) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abzi, on the authority of Ubayyah, on the authority of Ubayy, who said: Do not curse the smell. When you see what you dislike, say: Oh God, we ask you for the best of this smell. The best of what is in it and the best of what it was sent with, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this smell and the evil of what is in it and the evil of what it was sent with.\n(Tirmidhi 2252. Ahmad 123)"
"29830","(29830) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Shaiban narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Did a wind blow, or did a wind blow? So they took her captive, and Ibn Abbas said: Do not take her captive, for she brings mercy and brings torment, but say: Oh God, make her Have mercy on her, and do not make her a torment."
"29831","(29831) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: When the wind blew and turned, Ibn Umar used to say: Stress the takbeer, for it is my doctrine."
"29832","(29832) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of my father, so he visited him, saying: He was a slave. Al-Rahman ibn Malik, when he saw the wind, said: O God, we ask You for its good and the best of what You have sent in it, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it is. You were destined for it."
"29833","(29833) Zaid bin Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, that he mentioned that Aisha narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would leave what was there when he saw heavy clouds from one of the horizons. In it, and if he was in prayer until he faced it, he would say: O God, we seek refuge in You from the evil with which He was sent. Then if it rains, he said : Oh God, pour out a beneficial rain twice, or three times, so if God uncovers it and it does not rain, praise be to God for that. (Bukhari 686 and Abu Dawud 5058)"
"29834","(29834) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he saw the rain, he said: O God, make it a beneficial rain. (Bukhari 1032. Ahmed 90)"
"29835","(29835) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samat He said: We said to Ka'b bin Murah, O Ka'b, tell us, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, ask God for rain for Mudar. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised He extended his hand and said: O God, give us rain, which is abundant, refreshing, hasty, non-staining, beneficial, and non-harmful. He said: They did not gather until they were brought back to life. So they came to him and complained to him about the rain, and said: O Messenger of God, the houses were destroyed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: With his hand: Oh God, be around us, or against us. He said: Then he made the clouds part, right and left. (Ibn Majah 1269. Tayalisi 1199)"
"29836","(29836) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made supplication for anyone, he would start with himself and mention it one day. Moses and he said: May God have mercy on us and on Moses. If he had been patient, God would have related to us some of His news. But he said: {If I ask you about anything after that, so do not accompany me, for you have attained an excuse from me.} (Bukhari 122 and Muslim 1847)"
"29837","(29837) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: When you call, begin. For yourself, you do not know which supplication will be answered."
"29838","(29838) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: May God have mercy on us and brother Aad. (Ibn Majah 3852)"
"29839","(29839) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yassar, who said: I sat with Ibn Umar and mentioned a man. So I had mercy on him, and he hit my chest and said: Start with yourself."
"29840","(29840) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Darda’ al-Ansari, who said: Aisha said: To her sister’s son: It is better for you to pray for yourself than for the storyteller to pray for you."
"29841","(29841) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Rishdin Kurayb The servant of Ibn Abbas said: Ibn Abbas said: I spent the night at my aunt Maimunah’s, and I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: His prostration: Oh God, put light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in front of me, and light behind me. And make light beneath me, and give me greater light."
"29842","(29842) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mus’ar, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zurr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Ali, who said: He who loves to speak to God That the servant says while prostrating: I have wronged myself, so forgive me."
"29843","(29843) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Thawair bin Abi Fakhita, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: No man has placed his jilbab prostrate before God and said: O Lord, forgive me, O Lord, forgive me, O Lord, forgive me three times, except that he raised His head has been forgiven."
"29844","(29844) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abu Wael used to say while prostrating: My Lord, if You pardon me, you will be pardoned. It is too long of you, and if you torture me, you will torture me without being unjust or unjust, then he will cry."
"29845","(29845) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad Al-Ansari, who said: Abdullah bin Yazid bin Rabi’ah narrated to us. Al-Dimashqi said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: One night she entered the mosque, and when she entered, she passed by a prostrating man, and he said: Oh God, I am afraid and seeking refuge, so protect me from your torment, and I am begging and poor, so grant me grace, I am not innocent of sin. So he apologized, and no powerful person was victorious, but a sinner asked for forgiveness, so Abu Al-Darda’ began teaching them to his companions out of admiration. With it"
"29846","(29846) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: When he prostrates Let one of you say: O Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me. Muharib said: For he is the closest thing he has to God Almighty."
"29847","(29847) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I asked for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, but I did not find him. She said: What if he had intercourse with some of his maids or wives? She said: I saw him prostrating and saying: O God, forgive me for what I have concealed and what I have declared. (Ahmad 1471 Hakim 221)"
"29848","(29848) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that he said: Whoever gets disgraced at night and says: There is no god but You, my Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, he will be free of his sins as The snake comes out of its skin."
"29849","(29849) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Zayd ibn Suhan, on the authority of Salman, when he got tired at night, he would say: Glory be to the Lord of the prophets and to Him who are the messengers."
"29850","(29850) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Huraim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Kathir, the mawlid of his mother. Salama, when Umm Salama was tired at night, she would say: My Lord, forgive and have mercy and show the right path."
"29851","(29851) Bakr bin Ubaid narrated to us, Issa bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, that when he moved in the night, he would say: O people, proof has come to you from Your Lord, and We have sent down to you a clear light."
"29852","(29852) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Saad al-Sa’idi, who said: Two hours in which it will be opened. The gates of heaven, and rarely does his supplication be answered: attending the call to prayer, and standing in line for the sake of God Almighty. (Abu Dawud 2532, Ibn Hibban 1764)"
"29853","(29853) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to order supplications. At the call to prayer of the muezzins."
"29854","(29854) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The supplications between the call to prayer and the iqamah are not rejected."
"29855","(29855) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Marara, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The best of hours Prayer times, so pray during them."
"29856","(29856) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: The hour in which the supplication is answered for the one who supplicates on the day of Friday prayer when the imam stands for prayer until he finishes."
"29857","(29857) Ubayd Allah told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Supplications are not rejected between the call to prayer and the iqamah, so pray."
"29858","(29858) Ahmad bin Abdul-Malik bin Waqid narrated to us, Al-Harith bin Murra narrated to us, Zaid Al-Raqqashi narrated to us, on the authority of Anas He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the call to prayer comes, the gates of heaven are opened and supplications are answered, and when At the time of residence, your prayer was not rejected. (Abu Ali 4095. Tayalisi 2106)"
"29859","(29859) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakim bin Abdullah bin Qais, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father Saad, that he said: Whoever says, when the muezzin says, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,” I am satisfied with Allah as my Lord. And with Islam as a religion and with Muhammad as a prophet, his sins were forgiven, and a man said to him: O Saad, what of his previous sins, and what He was late? He said: No, that is what I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say. (Muslim 290 and Abu Dawud 526)"
"29860","(29860) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Huraim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Kathir, the mawlid of his mother. Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Say at the time of the Maghrib call to prayer: Oh God, when it arrives. Forgive me during your night, and the end of your day, and the voices of your supplications, and the presence of your prayers. (Abu Dawud 531, Tirmidhi 3589)"
"29861","(29861) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd bin Muawiyah said: The words that Adam received from his Lord: Oh God, there is no god but You, Glory be to You and with Your praise, I have done evil. And I have wronged myself, so have mercy on me, and You are the Best of the Merciful. O God, there is no god but You, Glory be to You, and with Your praise, I have done evil and wronged myself. So accept my repentance, for you are the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"29862","(29862) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: They are followed by those who say them, and those who say them will not be disappointed: Glory be to God at the end of every prayer, three times And thirty-four, and praise be to thirty-three, and glorify God thirty-four. (Muslim 418, Tirmidhi 3412)"
"29863","(29863) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra. He said: Three, and those who say them will not be disappointed, or he said: They say: He glorifies God thirty-three, and He praises thirty-three, and He says Akbar four times. And thirty at the end of every prayer. Al-Hakam said: I have not left them after that. (Bukhari 622, Tayalisi 1060)"
"29864","(29864) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Continuations whose speakers will not be disappointed. Then he mentioned the example of a comprehensive hadith."
"29865","(29865) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Abu Musa, that When he finished his prayer, he would say: O God, forgive my sins, make my affairs easy for me, and bless my livelihood."
"29866","(29866) Zaid bin Harun told us, Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Taysalah, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: Whoever says at the end of every prayer and when he takes his place to rest: God is Greatest, Greatest, according to the number of Shaf’ and Witr, and the words of God. The perfect, the good, the three blessed, and there is no god but God like that. Be a light for him in his grave, and a light on the bridge. And upon the path there will be light until we admit him to Paradise, or he enters Paradise."
"29867","(29867) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, that he used to say: It was completed. Your light, so you guided, to you is praise, your forbearance was great, so you pardoned, praise is due to you, you extended your hand, so you gave, praise is to you, our Lord, your face The most honorable of faces, your reward is the best of status, and my gift to you is the best and most congratulatory of gifts. You obey our Lord and are grateful, and you disobey Our Lord, please forgive, respond to the afflicted, remove harm, heal the sick, save from distress, accept repentance, and forgive the sin of whomever. Whatever you like, no one will suffice for your blessings, nor will your blessings be counted. Someone says, meaning: each one says after the prayer. (Abu Ali 436)"
"29868","(29868) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Umair bin Saad, who said: Abdullah used to pray with these supplications after Tashhud: Oh God, I ask You for all the good that I know of, and all that I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all the evil that I know. Of it, and what I do not know, O God, I ask you for the best of what your righteous servants have asked of you, and I seek refuge in you from the evil of what your servants have sought refuge from. The righteous: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire. Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us our sins and atone forgive us our evil deeds and die with the righteous. Our Lord, grant us what You promised us upon Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, you will not break The appointed time"
"29869","(29869) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, who said: I heard Musab bin Saad narrating, on the authority of Saad, When he recited the tashahhud, he would say: Glory be to God. He filled the heavens and filled the earth, and what is between them, and what is under the earth. His people said: No. Do you know, “Allahu Akbar” (God is Greatest) before, or “Praise be to God, good and blessed praise be to Him,” “There is no god but God alone, without any partner.” To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. Oh God, I ask you of all goodness, then he greets you."
"29870","(29870) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ward, the client of Al-Mughirah, who said: He wrote Mu'awiyah to Al-Mughirah bin Shu'ba: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say when he gave the salutation during prayer? He said: So he dictated it to me. Al-Mughirah said: So I wrote it to Mu’awiyah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When he says the salutation, he says: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. Oh God, there is no one who can prevent what You have given, nor can there be a giver of what You have withheld, and no one can benefit from your earnestness from you."
"29871","(29871) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, he said: A sheikh narrated to me, on the authority of Salah ibn Zufar, he said: I heard Ibn Omar said at the end of the prayer: Oh God, you are peace and from you is peace. Blessed are you, O possessor of majesty and honor. Then she prayed beside Abdullah bin Amr heard him say it, so I said to him: I heard Ibn Omar say the same as what you say, so Abdullah bin Amr said Amr: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying these things at the end of his prayer."
"29872","(29872) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, a client of theirs, that Abdullah bin Al-Zubair At the end of every prayer, God used to say: There is no god but God alone, there is no partner with Him, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is upon Him. All things are powerful, and there is no power or strength except with God, and we worship none but Him. To Him belongs blessings, to Him is bounty, and to Him is the good reward. There is no god but God, sincere in religion to Him, even if the disbelievers hate it. Then Ibn al-Zubair says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May God’s peace and blessings be upon him. May God grant you every prayer. (Muslim 416. Abu Dawud 1502)"
"29873","(29873) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, came. Fatimah, may God be pleased with her, said, “My chest complains about what I am suffering from in the West.” She said, “And I, by God, my hands complain about what I am grinding.” He said: To her: Come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a captive has come to him. Come to him, perhaps he will serve you as a servant, so they set off. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to them and said: You have come to me so that I may serve you as a servant, and I will inform you of what It is better for you than a servant. If you wish, I will inform you of what is better for you than a servant: Glory be to You, after every prayer. thirty-three, and you praise Him thirty-three times, and you glorify Him thirty-four times, and when you take your resting places during the night, then 100. Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: I have not yet been informed of your abandonment of it. Abdullah Ibn al-Kawa’i said to him: Not even for the night of Siffin. Then Ali said to him: May God fight you, people of Iraq, or even the night of Siffin. (Ibn Majah 4152. Ahmed 79)"
"29874","(29874) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There are two characteristics that no man will keep unless he enters Paradise. They are easy, and those who do them are few. It was said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: The five prayers. A man says Subhanahu ten after each prayer, praises ten, and Takbir Ten, that is fifty and one hundred on the tongue, and one thousand and five hundred in the scale. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, counts them on his hand, says “Tasbih” thirty-three times, “praises be to Him” thirty-three times, and “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. He lies down during the night, and when he goes to bed, he glorifies, praises, and glorifies Allah a hundred times. That is a hundred on the tongue, and a thousand in the scale. Which of you commits sin on the night of two thousand and five hundred? (Ibn Majah 926. Tirmidhi 3410)"
"29875","(29875) Your youth told us, Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of the servant of Laam Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he prayed the morning prayer when he said the salutation: Oh God, I ask you for useful knowledge and good provision. And an acceptable deed. (Ahmad 3051, Abu Ali 6961)"
"29876","(29876) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Zazan, who said: A man from the Ansar narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying at the end of the prayer: O God, forgive me and accept my repentance. Indeed, You are the Most Accepting and Forgiving. bitterness (Ahmad 371. Bukhari 619)"
"29877","(29877) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abu Umar Al-Sinni, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’ heard it from Abu Umar, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, the rich went away with the reward, and they pray as We pray, and they fast as we fast, and they perform Hajj as we do, and they give in charity, but we do not find what we give in charity. He said: So he said: Shall I not guide you to Something that if you do, you will overtake those who came before you, and no one will overtake you after you except those who have done what you do: You glorify God. Allah is thirty-three times, and you praise Him thirty-three times, and you glorify Him thirty-four times at the end of every prayer.\n(Ahmad 446. An-Nasa’i 9979)"
"29878","(29878) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of his father, who said: When Omar finished his prayer He said: O God, I seek Your forgiveness for my sin, I seek Your guidance for the guidance of my affairs, and I repent to You, so accept my repentance. O God, You are my Lord, so make My desire is for You, and place my singing in my breast and bless for me what You have provided for me, and accept from me, for You are my Lord."
"29879","(29879) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Simak ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Munabbih, who said: The example of one who prays Without action, it is like one who throws stones without a string."
"29880","(2980) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, who said: There was a spring coming to Al-Qamiya on the day The crowd, he said: So he came to him, but it was not there then, then a man came and said: Don’t you marvel at the people’s many supplications and their few prayers? Their answer, and Rabi’ said: Do you know why that was? God does not accept except the palm trees of supplication. Abdul Rahman bin Yazeed said: When I came, Alqamah told me what Rabi’ had said. So I said to him: Did you not hear what Abdullah said? He said: What is that? He said: Abdullah said: By the One besides Whom there is no god, God does not hear from a listener, nor from a hypocrite, nor from a player, nor from a caller except a caller who calls. With steadfastness in his heart."
"29881","(29881) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, who said: God says whoever is occupied with remembrance, on the authority of I gave him what I asked for more than what I gave to those who asked. (Bukhari 1850, Tirmidhi 2926)"
"29882","(29882) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman Abu Umayyah bin Fadalah narrated to us, saying: Bakr bin Abd narrated to us. Allah Al-Muzani Abu Dharr said: Sufficient supplications for righteousness are as sufficient for food as salt."
"29883","(29883) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who narrated it, saying: Whoever is distracted by the remembrance of You have given me what I asked for more than what I give to those who ask, meaning the Lord, Blessed and Most High."
"29884","(29884) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, who said: I heard Amr bin Asim narrating that he heard Abu Huraira says: Abu Bakr said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Inform me of something that I should say in the morning and then. Evening, he said: Say: O God, the Knower of the Unseen and the Witnesses, the Creator of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of all things and His King, I bear witness that no There is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself, and from Satan and his partners. Say it in the evening and in the morning, and when you take it. Your bed"
"29885","(29885) Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, Abu Maudud narrated to us, saying: He who heard Aban ibn Uthman narrated to me, saying: narrated to me. Abu Uthman said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever says three times in the morning and in the evening: In the name of God With His Name nothing on earth or in the heavens can be harmed, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. Nothing has afflicted it in its day or in another. His night is something. (Abu Dawud 5047. An-Nasa’i 9844)"
"29886","(29886) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the evening: “Our evening And the kingdom belongs to God, and praise be to God. There is no god but God alone, without any partner. Oh God, I ask you of the best of this. The night and the best in it, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of it and the evil in it. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from laziness and old age. And arrogance, the temptations of this world, and the torment of the grave. Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah said: Zubaid added to me in it, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah, he narrated it, saying: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. (Muslim 2089. Abu Dawud 5032)"
"29887","(2988) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the morning: We have entered into the nature of Islam in the morning. And the word of sincerity, and the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, and the religion of our father Abraham, upright, and he was not of the polytheists."
"29888","(2988) Zayd bin Harun told us, Fa’id Abu Warqa’ told us, Abdullah bin Abi Awfa told us, he said: It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the morning: We have arrived and the kingdom belongs to God, and pride and greatness, And the creation and the matter, and the night and the day, and what is sacrificed in them belong to God alone, without any partner. O God, make the first of these The day is good, its middle is prosperity, and its end is success. I ask you for the best of this world, O Most Merciful of the Merciful. (Abdullah bin Hamid 531)"
"29889","(2989) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Ubadah bin Muslim Al-Fazari narrated to us, Jubayr bin Abi Sulayman bin Jubayr bin Mutim claimed that he was sitting with Abdullah bin Omar and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: In his supplication in the evening and in the morning, he did not abandon him until he left this world, or until he died: Oh God, I ask you Wellness in this world and the hereafter. Oh God, I ask you for forgiveness and well-being in my religion, my world, my family, and my wealth. O God, cover my private parts and secure my splendor. O God, protect me from before me and from behind me, from my right and from my left and from Above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness lest I be attacked from below. Jubayr said: It is an eclipse, and I do not know: the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, or the saying of the mighty. (Nasa’i 7971)"
"29890","(29890) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Abu Dawud 5035. Ibn Hibban 961)"
"29891","(29891) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, who said: I narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say when morning came: With you we have become, and with you we live, and with you we die, and to You is the resurrection. And when evening came, he would say: Oh God. With You we have spent the evening, with You we live, and with You we die, and to You is the return."
"29892","(29892) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqeel narrated to me on the authority of a previous person, on the authority of Abu Salam, the servant of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: There is no Muslim, or human being, or servant who says when In the evening and in the morning, three times, I am satisfied with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as prophet, unless it is a duty upon God to He will be satisfied on the Day of Resurrection."
"29893","(29893) Zaid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh narrated to us, Abu Hani narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ali al-Janabi, he said : I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says, “I am satisfied with God as my Lord and with Islam.” religion and Muhammad is a messenger, Paradise is inevitable for him. (Abu Dawud 1524, Hakim 93)"
"29894","(29894) Zaid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mujabir told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says in the evening: I am satisfied with God as my Lord and with Islam religion, and Muhammad is a messenger, he has attained the true meaning of faith."
"29895","(29895) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, who said: Whoever says, “When the evening and the morning Thirdly, O God, the morning has become a witness, and when the morning comes, he says: O God, the morning has become a witness, that we have no good health in the morning. And His blessings, they are from You alone, you have no partner, so praise be to You. He was not asked about any blessings that were on that night, nor On this day, he has paid her thanks. (Abu Dawud 5034, Ibn Hibban 861)"
"29896","(29896) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, that he used to say in the morning and evening: Oh God, I ask you, when I attend your prayers and the rise of your supplications, to forgive me. And have mercy on me."
"29897","(29897) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sakhbara, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he used to say in the morning or evening: O God, make me the best of Your servants morning or night a share of goodness. You divide, and light you guide, mercy you spread, sustenance you extend, harm you remove, affliction you remove, and evil. You repel it, and you divert it from temptation."
"29898","(29898) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who said: I said to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, “What do you say?” When you wake up in the morning and evening from what you call upon, he said: We say: I seek refuge in the Noble Face of God, the Great Name of God, and the Word of God. Complete from the evil of the Semites and the Lame, and from the evil of what you were ignorant of, O Lord, and from the evil of what You took by His forelock, and from the evil of this day and the evil of What comes after it, and the evil of this world and the hereafter."
"29899","(29899) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of a man from Nakha’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salman, who said: Whoever says in the morning and in the evening, O God, you are my Lord, you have no partner, we have risen and the kingdom is yours, you have no partner, will be forgiven. What happened between them?"
"29900","(29900) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of a man from Al-Nakh’, on the authority of Salman, who said: Who said when the morning Oh God, you are my Lord, you have no partner. He was an expiation for what happened between them."
"29901","(29901) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Al-Janni, who said: A man narrated to me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Who said Glory be to God in the evening and Glory be to God in the morning until he finishes reciting the verses three times, and he realizes what he had missed from his day."
"29902","(29902) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ayyash Al-Zarqi, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to him is the kingdom and to Him Praise be to Him, and He has power over all things. He had as many slaves from the offspring of Ishmael, and ten good deeds were recorded for him. It removed from him ten bad deeds, and raised him ten degrees because of it, and he was under protection from Satan until the evening. And if the evening is like that until the morning."
"29903","(29903) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says when morning comes: Oh God, by you we have risen in the morning and by you we have entered the evening, by you we live and by you we die. And to You is the final destination. (Abu Dawud 5029. Tirmidhi 3391)"
"29904","(29904) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr narrated to me, on the authority of a man from The companions of Muhammad said: Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone, and there is no partner with Him, to Him belongs the kingdom and to Him is praise, in His hand. Goodness, and He has power over all things ten times, He has been raised ten times in degrees, He has erased ten bad deeds, and He is exonerated. On that day he will be free from hypocrisy until the evening, and if he says in the evening it will be like that, and he will be free of hypocrisy until the morning."
"29905","(29905) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Zar’i. Ibn Amr Ibn Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: I find in the Torah: Whoever says in the morning: O God, I I seek refuge in Your Name and Your perfect words from the accursed Satan. Oh God, I seek refuge in Your Name and Your perfect words from Your torment and evil. Your servants, O God, I ask you in your perfect name and words for the best of what you ask and of the best of what you give and of the best of what you You reveal and among the best things you conceal: O God, I seek refuge in You, in Your Name and in Your perfect words, from the evil of what the day has revealed. You have not extinguished Therein are the devils, and there is nothing that he dislikes, and when he says to them in the evening, it is like that, except that he says: Of some evil. The night came in."
"29906","(29906) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He took his bed and said: O God, to You I surrender myself and direct my face, and to You I entrust my affairs: and to You I seek refuge. My desire and fear are for You. There is no refuge or refuge from You except in You. I believe in Your Book which you revealed. And by Your Prophet, or Your Messenger whom You sent."
"29907","(29907) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: O so-and-so, when you go to your bed, say: Oh God, I have surrendered myself to You, and I have turned my back to You. Then he mentioned Something like that, except that he said: If you die that night, die in the proper manner, and if you die in the morning, you will be well."
"29908","(29908) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Saad ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Aazib, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: When you go to bed, say: Oh God, I have surrendered my soul to you. I have turned my face to you, and I have entrusted my affairs to you, and I have turned my back to you out of fear and desire for you, with no refuge. There is no refuge from you except in you. I believe in your book which you sent down and in your prophet whom you sent, so if he dies, he dies according to the nature of the matter."
"29909","(29909) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to bed, he would say: O God, in your name I die and live, and when he got up, he said: Praise. To Allah is the One who brought us to life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"29910","(29910) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: It was When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept, he said: In your name I live and die, and when he woke up, he said: Praise be to God, who has given us life. After He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"29911","(29911) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfy, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, such as the suspicion of Jarir regarding Abd al-Malik or Mansour."
"29912","(29912) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting with Ammar and a man came to him. So he said: Shall I not teach you some words as if he were referring them to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When you go to bed at night, say: Oh God, I have submitted myself to You, and I have entrusted my affairs to You, and I have turned my back to You, and I have believed in Your revealed Book. And Your Prophet and Messenger, O God, You have created my soul. Yours is its life and its death. If You are sufficient for it, have mercy on it. You delay it, so guard it by preserving faith."
"29913","(29913) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, who said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa He narrates, on the authority of Al-Baraa, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, he would say: Praise be to God who has revived us after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. His people said this, or something like it, and when he slept, he said: Oh God, in your name they live and in your name. I am dying"
"29914","(29914) Zayd bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to pray: O God, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire. (Ahmad 2471 Muslim 2071)"
"29915","(29915) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu I saw that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you wants to lie on his bed, let him remove inside his garment, then to dust his bed with it, for he does not know what he left behind it, then to lie on his part. The right hand, then to say: In Your Name, my Lord, I have placed myself at my side, and in You I raise it up. If I hold my soul, have mercy on it, and if I send it So protect it with the same way you protect your righteous servants."
"29916","(29916) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, on the authority of his father, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: What brought you? He said: O Messenger of God, teach me something that I may say when I sleep. He said: When you go to bed, recite: (Say, O The disbelievers) Then sleep at the end of it, for it is free from polytheism."
"29917","(29917) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man from the Ansar: What do you say when you want to sleep? He said: I say: In your name you have placed me beside me, so forgive me. He said: You have been forgiven."
"29918","(29918) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Nawfal Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of His father said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me something that I should say to him in the morning and in the evening, and he said: Read {Say O you, the disbelievers.} Then sleep at its conclusion, for it is free from polytheism."
"29919","(29919) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Baba, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever says when he goes to his bed: There is no god but Allah alone, there is no partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is above all. A powerful thing, Glory be to God and praise be to Him, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is Great, His sins are forgiven, even if It was like sea foam."
"29920","(29920) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Afaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, who said: Whoever says when he goes to bed: I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is Able to do so four times. His sins will be forgiven, even if they are over the earth."
"29921","(29921) Zayd bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Sawa, on the authority of Hafsa, that the Messenger of God When he went to bed, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would say: My Lord, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants."
"29922","(29922) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you take Your bed, then say: In the name of God and in the way of God, and upon the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"29923","(29923) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And when he sleeps, he places his right hand under his cheek and says: Save me from your punishment on the day you resurrect your servants."
"29924","(29924) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that when he slept, he would say: Oh God, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You will raise up Your servants, and he would put His right hand is under his cheek."
"29925","(29925) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father He saw that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go to his bed, he would say: O God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earths, our Lord. And the Lord of all things, the Creator of love and intentions, the Revealer of the Torah and the Gospel and the Qur’an, I seek refuge in You from the evil of every evil You are taking. By His commandment, You are the first, so there is nothing before you, You are the last, so there is nothing after you, and You are the Manifest, so there is nothing above you. And You are the Inward One, and there is nothing without You. Pay off my debt and enrich me from poverty.\n(Muslim 2084, Abu Dawud 5012)"
"29926","(29926) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, who said: I narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he used to say when he went to bed: O God, grant me good health in my religion, good health my body, good health my sight, and make it The heir from me, there is no god but God, the Most High, the Great. Glory be to God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Noble Throne. Praise be to God, Lord. The two worlds (Tirmidhi 3480, Abu Ali 4671)"
"29927","(29927) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid bin Amr Al-Kharifi, on the authority of Ali, who said: What I see a sensible person who has embraced Islam sleeping until he recites the Kursi verse."
"29928","(29928) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Laith bin Saad bin Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that He said: Urwah informed me, on the authority of Aisha, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would blow his nose when he went to bed, His hands and recited the two Mu'awwidhayn over them, then wiped his body with them. (Bukhari 5017, Abu Dawud 5017)"
"29929","(29929) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, who said: The Messenger of Allah May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He says when he sleeps: I seek refuge in your generous face and your perfect words from the evil of what you are reckless. With his advice, O God, it is you who remove sin and debt, O God, your promise will not be broken, your soldiers will not be defeated, and this will not be of any use. The greatness of you is the greatness, Glory be to You and praise be to You. (Abu Dawud 5013. An-Nasa’i 10603)"
"29930","(29930) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Marzuq, who said: Abu Salamah Al-Janni narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Abd never said if He has been afflicted with grief or sadness: Oh God, I am Your servant, the son of Your servant, the son of Your female servant. My forelock is in Your hand. I will continue in Your judgment with justice. In Your decree, I ask You by every name with which You have named Yourself, or revealed it in Your Book, or taught it to any of you. Your creation, or You have taken control of it in the knowledge of the unseen with You, to make the Qur’an the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, and the remover of my sorrow and the go-away. My concern is that God will take away his worry and replace the place of his sadness with joy. They said: O Messenger of God, we must learn These words? He said: Yes, whoever hears them should learn them. (Ahmad 391, Abu Ali 5276)"
"29931","(29931) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, who said: Ali said to me: Shall I not teach you words that I did not teach you, Hasan or Hussein? If you ask for a need and would like it to succeed, then say: There is no god but Allah. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, the Most High, the Great, and there is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, the Most Forbearing, the Most Generous. Then ask I need you (Nasa’i 10469)"
"29932","(29932) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: I entered the mosque and I saw that It was morning and suddenly it was a long night and there was no one in it except me. I got up and heard movement behind me and I was frightened. He said: O you, whose heart is full of divisions, do not be divided, or do not be afraid, and say: O God, you are the King, Able to do whatever you wish. It is, then ask whatever you want. Sa`id said: I never asked God for anything but He answered it."
"29933","(29933) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, who said: I looked for a ruling on a matter and did not find it, then I looked for it and found it. And he said: Al-Hakam: Khaythama said: If one of you seeks a pilgrim and finds it, let him ask God for the Garden, perhaps his Day of Resurrection. He will be answered in it."
"29934","(29934) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: Talq bin Habib used to say: Oh God, grant us peace. This nation has a wise matter in which you honor your guardian, humiliate your enemy, and do it in obedience to you."
"29935","(29935) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abdul-Malik, who said: Tell me who saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz. He is standing with his finger, making supplication, and he is saying with his finger in this way and pointing with it: O God, increase the benefactor of his mother Muhammad in favor and restore With their wrongdoing until repentance, then He says thus, then He turns with His finger: And bring down those behind them by Your mercy."
"29936","(29936) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abdul-Malik, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to say, Oh God The most righteous is he whose righteousness is righteous to his mother Muhammad. And he greeted you."
"29937","(29937) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he wanted to get up from the gathering: Glory be to God, O God. And by Your praise I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. (Abu Ali 7389)"
"29938","(29938) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Omar, who said: Whoever says, “Glory be to you” when he gets up from his gathering O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. He said: May God atone for every sin in that. The Council"
"29939","(29939) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, on the authority of Ziyad ibn al-Husayn, who said: I entered upon my father. Aliya, and when I wanted to leave him, he said: Shall I not provide you with some words that Gabriel taught Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I said: Yes? He said: When he was at the end of the night, when he got up from his seat, he said: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise I bear witness that there is no god but You, I ask your forgiveness and I repent to you. He said: Then it was said: O Messenger of God, what are these words that you say? He said: These are words that Gabriel taught me as expiations for what happened in the assembly. (Nasa’i 10264)"
"29940","(29940) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas regarding his saying: And glorify with the praise of your Lord When you stand up, he said: When you stand up, say: Glory be to God and praise be to Him."
"29941","(29941) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: We used to consider Al-Awaab to be the All-Knowing, the All-Knowing, when he got up from his seat and said: O God, forgive me for what I have befallen in this assembly."
"29942","(29942) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’diyah, who said: The expiation of the assembly, Glory be to You. And with Your praise, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."
"29943","(29943) Abu Asama and Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, who said: I heard Aisha saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying while leaning on my chest: O God, forgive me. And have mercy on me and join me with the Companion. (Bukhari 4440, Muslim 85)"
"29944","(29944) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace, he often says before he dies: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. She said: So I said: O Messenger of God, what are these words that you said? He said: I have made a sign for my nation when you see it and say it when God’s victory and conquest come. (Bukhari 794, Muslim 351)"
"29945","(29945) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Musa bin Sarjis, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, On the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was dying, he had a cup of water in it and he put it in his hand. In the cup, and wipes his face with water, then says: Oh God, help me in the throes of death.\n(Tirmidhi 978 and Ahmad 1423)"
"29946","(29946) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: O God, forgive me, and join me with a companion. She said: This was the last I heard of his words."
"29947","(29947) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up at night, he would say: O God, praise be to You. You are the light of the heavens and the earth, and to You is praise. You are the foundation of the heavens and the earth, and praise be to You. You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and those in them. You are the truth and your words are the truth and the jinn is the truth. And the Fire is true and the Hour is true. O God, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed, and in You I have put my trust, and in You I have disputed, and to You I have judged, so forgive. What you have put forward, what you have delayed, what you have concealed, what you have announced, and what you know better than me, you are the one who brings forward and the one who delays, there is no god but You (Bukhari 1120, Muslim 534)"
"29948","(29948) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, who said: Azhar bin Saeed narrated to me, on the authority of Asim bin Hamid. He said: I asked Aisha: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to start his night prayers with? She said: You asked me about something that no one had asked me about before you. He used to say “Allahu Akbar” ten times, “praise be to Allah” ten times, and “Allahu Akbar” ten times. He will ask for forgiveness ten times and say: O God, forgive me, guide me, provide for me, and protect me. And he will seek refuge from the distress of his situation on the Day of Resurrection. The Resurrection (Abu Dawud 762, Ibn Hibban 2602)"
"29949","(29949) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: We were with Abu Musa, so we went to sleep at night. A ruined orchard. He said: So he got up during the night and prayed and recited the Qur’an beautifully, then he said: Oh God, you are a believer. You love a believer, and you are a believer. You love the dominant, you love peace, you love the truthful, you love the truthful."
"29950","(29950) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, Rabi’a ibn Ka’b told him that he was spending the night at the door of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was listening The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during the night: Glory be to God, Lord of the Worlds, the Divine, then he said: Glory be to God. And praise be to Him.\n(Bukhari 1218 and Tirmidhi 3416)"
"29951","(29951) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Thabit, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He prays: Oh God, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire."
"29952","(29952) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon a man as if he were a chick. Exhausted from effort, he said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Have you been praying to God for anything? He said: I used to say, O God, if you are punishing me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world, then he said to him: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. Did you not say: Oh God, give us good in this world and good in the hereafter and protect us from the torment of the Fire. He said: So he called upon God and He healed him.\n(Bukhari 728 and Muslim 2068)"
"29953","(29953) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Habib bin Saban, who said: I heard Omar going around The House, and there is no reward for it except these words: {Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment. Fire}"
"29954","(29954) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Musayyab, on the authority of Habib ibn Saban, on the authority of Umar with a similar story."
"29955","(29955) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of my father Hariri said: Fatima came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask a servant, and he said to her: I do not have what I can give you. So she came back and he came to her after that and said: Is the one you asked more beloved to you or something better than that? So he said: I have to say: No. Rather, nothing is better than it. So she said, and he said: Say: O God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Great Throne, our Lord and Lord of all things. You are the first, and there is nothing before you, and you are the last, and there is nothing after you. The Outward One, for there is nothing above You, and You are the Inward One, for there is nothing below You. Pay off our debt and enrich us from poverty. (Muslim 63 Tirmidhi 3481)"
"29956","(29956) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali, that Fatima complained to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her hands being kneaded and rough. He said: So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him because of a curse. She came to him to ask for a servant but did not find him. She found Aisha and told her. Ali said: So we came. After we had gone to bed, we went to get up and he said: Your place. He said: Then he came and sat between me and her until his feet felt cold. He said: Shall I not guide you to something better for you than a servant: Glory be to Him thirty-three times, and praise be to Him thirty-three times. And you say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-three times. (Bukhari 2023 and Muslim 2091)"
"29957","(29957) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Jabr bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, on the authority of Aisha, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught her this supplication. O God, I ask you of all goodness, urgently. And for the sake of it, what I knew of it, and what I did not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I knew of it, and what I did not know, O God. I ask you for the best of what your servant and your Prophet asked you, and I seek refuge in you from the evil of what your servant and your Prophet sought refuge from. Oh God, I ask you Paradise, and whatever brings it near to it in words or deeds, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire, and whatever brings it closer to it in words or deeds. I ask you to make every decree you decree good for me. (Ahmad 134. Ibn Hibban 869)"
"29958","(29958) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays bin Abbad. He said: Ammar prayed a prayer as if they had denied it, so he was told about that and he said: Didn’t he complete the bowing and prostration? They said: Yes, he said: Indeed, I have invoked God with a supplication that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Oh God, with your knowledge of the unseen. And by Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as you know life is good for me, and cause me to die when you know death is good for me, O God. I ask you to speak words of sincerity in anger and contentment, purposefulness in wealth and poverty, and your fear in the unseen and the present. And I ask you to be content with destiny, and I ask you for bliss that never ends, and comfort for an eye that never ceases, and the pleasure of life after death. And that is why I look at your face and longing to meet you, and I seek refuge in you from harmful adversities and misleading trials. Oh God, adorn us. Beautify your faith and make us guided and guided. (Bazzar 1392. Tabarani 625)"
"29959","(29959) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Let none of you wish for death because of harm that has befallen him in this world, but rather say: O God, grant me life as long as life is good. And let me die if death is better for me. (Bukhari 5671, Muslim 2064)"
"29960","(29960) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, who said: It was one of Ammar’s supplications, O God, I ask you By Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, You grant me life as long as You know life is good for me, and cause me to die as long as You know death. It is better for me. Oh God, I ask you for your fear in the unseen and the seen, and I ask you for your purpose in wealth and poverty. And I ask you for justice in contentment and anger. Oh God, make me love to meet you and long for you in anything other than misleading temptation or harm. Harmful"
"29961","(29961) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Rashid, who said: Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’ narrated to me, on the authority of his father. He said: I have never heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, begin a supplication without him opening it with Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, the Most High. Al-Wahhab (Ahmed 54)"
"29962","(29962) Ali bin Musir and Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father He said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, teach me something that I may say. He said: Say: There is no god. There is no partner but God alone. To Him belongs the kingdom. God is great, great, and praise be to God abundantly. Glory be to God, Lord. The worlds, there is no power nor strength except in God, the Mighty, the Wise. He said: Then the Bedouins said: This is for my Lord, so what is mine? He said: Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me. (Muslim 2072. Ibn Hibban 946)"
"29963","(29963) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Adbas, on the authority of Abu Marzuq, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and it was as if we longed for him to pray for us, and he said: O God, forgive us and have mercy on us and be pleased with us and accept from us and admit us to Paradise and save us from Hell and make all our affairs right for us. It is as if we longed for him to add more to us, so he said: I have gathered the matter for you. (احمد ۲۵۳)"
"29964","(29964) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Zakaria bin Abi Zayed narrated to us, Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, he said: narrated to me. Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that he said: Husayn came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before he He greeted him and said: O Muhammad, what do you command me to say? He said: You say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, and I ask You to guide me in the right direction in my affairs. He said: Then I am fortified. He converted to Islam after that, then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I asked you the first time, and now I say: What Do you command me to say? He said: Say: O God, forgive me for what I concealed, and what I declared, and what I did wrong, and what I deliberately did, and what I was ignorant of, and what I taught. (Tirmidhi 3483 and Ahmad 444)"
"29965","(29965) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Dawud Al-Awdi, on the authority of Buraidah, who said: The Messenger of God said to me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Shall I not teach you the words of someone whom God intended good for, He taught them to them and then did not forget them? Never, he said: Say: O God, I am weak, so strengthen my weakness in Your satisfaction, and take me to goodness by my forelock, and make Islam its ultimate destination. My satisfaction, O God, I am weak, so strengthen me, I am humble, so comfort me, and I am poor, so provide for me. (Hakim 527)"
"29966","(29966) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Bakr, that he said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Teach me a supplication that I will pray with, He said: Say: O God, I have wronged myself greatly, and no one can forgive sins except You, so grant me forgiveness from You. And have mercy on me, for You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. (Bukhari 834, Muslim 2078)"
"29967","(29967) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Shall I not teach you some words that if you say them you will be forgiven? Although you are forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens. And the Lord of the Great Throne, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. (Tirmidhi 3504, Ibn Hibban 6928)"
"29968","(29968) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ward bin Thumama, on the authority of Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of Muadh, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man and he was saying: Oh God, I ask you for patience. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I ask God for calamity, so I ask for well-being. A man passed by and he said: Oh God, I ask you for the perfect blessing. He said: O son of Adam, do you know the completion of the blessing? He said: O Messenger of God, a supplication with which you invoked the hope of goodness. He said: Among the completion of blessings is entry into Paradise and seeking refuge from Hell, and he passed. On a man who was saying: O Possessor of Majesty and Honour, and he said: Your request has been answered, so ask of him. (Ahmed 231)"
"29969","(29969) Abu Muawiyah told us on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They pronounced: O Possessor of glory and honor. (Tirmidhi 3524, Ahmad 177)"
"29970","(29970) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hasan, that Abdullah Ibn Jafar came to see his sick son, who was called Salih, and he said to him: Say there is no god but Allah, the All-Merciful, the Most Generous. Glory be to my Lord. The Great Throne, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. O God, forgive me, O God, have mercy on me, O God, forgive me, O God, forgive me. On his authority, for You are pardoning and forgiving. Then he said: These are the words that my uncle taught me. He mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught them. Oh, oh (Nasa’i 10477)"
"29971","(29971) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, that he said: Preserve from me what I tell you. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: When people hoard gold and silver So treasure these words. Oh God, I ask you for steadfastness in the matter, and determination to follow the right path, and I ask you for gratitude for your blessings. And I ask You to worship You well, and I ask You for a sound heart and a sincere tongue, and I ask You for the best of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from The evil of what you know, and I ask forgiveness for what you know. Indeed, you are the Knower of the unseen. (Ahmad 123. Ibn Hibban 1974)"
"29972","(29972) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He teaches his companions, saying: Say: O God, forgive us our transgressions, reduce our transgressions, and cover our faults."
"29973","(29973) Waki’ narrated to us, saying Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He heard a man saying: Oh God, I ask you that you are God, the One and Only, the Eternal, the One who does not give birth and is not begotten. And there was no one equal to him, so he said: He has asked God by His greatest name, which when called upon, He answers, and when asked by it, I gave you\n(Abu Dawud 1488. Tirmidhi 3475)"
"29974","(29974) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khuzaymah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: He heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace, a man says: Oh God, I ask you that to you is praise, there is no god but you alone, you have no partner, Al-Mannan, the Splendor of the heavens and the earth, the Possessor of majesty and honor. He said: He has asked God in His greatest name. When asked, He gives. He was called upon and answered. (Tirmidhi 3544, Ahmed 265)"
"29975","(29975) Abu Usama narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, that a caller called In the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Oh God, I ask you in your name, God, there is no god but You, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Creator of the heavens and the earth, and when you want something, you just say to it: Be, and it is. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed. I almost, or he almost called, by His Greatest, Greatest Name."
"29976","(29976) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Asma’ Bint Zaid said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The greatest name of God in these two verses is: {And your God is God. One, there is no god but Him, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. And the opener of Surah Al Imran: {Allah belongs to Him, there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting}"
"29977","(29977) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: A man recited Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran, and he said Ka'b: He has recited two surahs. In them is the name by which when he is called, he responds."
"29978","(29978) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Al-Hasan bin Thawban narrated to me, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Ruqayya, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’ and Ibn Abbas, that they used to say: The greatest name of God is Lord, Lord."
"29979","(29979) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Hayyan al-Araj, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd who said: The greatest name of God is Allah."
"29980","(29980) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of someone who heard Al-Sha’bi say: The greatest name of God is God, then he recited, or she recited. He is God, the Creator until the end."
"29981","(29981) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq, who said: Abu Sa’id said: If you ask God Almighty, then ask In the matter, for what is with God you cannot escape."
"29982","(29982) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If any of you wishes Let him increase, for he is only asking his Lord. (Ibn Hibban 889 and Abd bin Hamid 1496)"
"29983","(29983) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Raja’ bin Hiyawah, on the authority of Abu Darda’ He said: Beware of calling upon the oppressed, for it ascends to the heavens like sparks of fire until the gates of heaven are opened for it."
"29984","(29984) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Sayfi narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ma`bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Beware of calling on the oppressed, for he There is no veil between her and God."
"29985","(29985) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who narrated it: Avoid the supplications of the oppressed. (Bukhari 624, Abu Ali 1332)"
"29986","(29986) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ma’n, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: There are four things that cannot be withheld from God: The supplication of a contented father and a just imam, the supplication of the oppressed, and the supplication of a man praying for his brother in the apparent absence."
"29987","(29987) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Abu Ma’shar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Huraira. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The prayer of the oppressed will be answered, and if he is an immoral person, then his immorality is against himself.\n(Ibn Hibban 875, Ahmed 367)"
"29988","(29988) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn al-Habnai, on the authority of Ali, who said: There are three whose supplications are not rejected: The Imam is just over his subjects, the father of his children, and the oppressed."
"29989","(29989) Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr’s statement, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Darda’, who said: Beware of And they called the oppressed."
"29990","(29990) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salama, that a man came to Mu’adh He said: Advise me, and he said: Beware of calling upon the oppressed."
"29991","(29991) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Yunus bin Saad, on the authority of Ali Al-Azdi, who said: I narrated that David, peace be upon him, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from wealth that overwhelms, from poverty that forgets, and from poverty that destroys. And from a deed that disgraces you."
"29992","(29992) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Dawud was Peace be upon him, he says: O God, save me from every calamity that the night has descended from the heavens on earth three times, and he says: O God, make for me An arrow in every good deed the night descended from the heavens to the earth."
"29993","(29993) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Musab, who was Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Whenever he broke his fast, he would face the Qiblah and say: O God, save me from every calamity. Three nights descended from the heavens, and when he rose The visor of the sun said: Oh God, make for me an arrow in every good deed that the night descends from the heavens to the earth three times. He said: So it was said to him, He said: The supplication of David, so soften your tongues with it and make your hearts aware of it."
"29994","(29994) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abbas Al-Ammi, who said: I was informed that David the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say in his supplications: Glory be to You, O God, You are my Lord, You have exalted above Your throne, and You have placed above those in the heavens And the earth fears you, so the closest of your creation to you in station is the most fearful of you, and no one knows who does not fear you, or The wisdom of one who does not obey your command. (Dharmi 4602)"
"29995","(29995) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that David the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, no Illness makes me sad, and good health makes me forget, but it's in between."
"29996","(2996) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, who said: It was one of David’s supplications upon him. Peace: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from evil."
"29997","(29997) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Habib bin Shahid informed me, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, that Dawud The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from work that disgraces me, desire that drives me back, and poverty that makes me forget. And the rich overwhelm you."
"29998","(29998) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, who said: Umm Hani’ came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: O Messenger of God, I have grown old and weak, so teach me something that I may do, while I am sitting. So the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, if you glorify God a hundred times, it will be better than the hundred of a glorified body coming forward. And indeed, if you glorify God a hundred times, it will be better than a hundred slaves that you will free. And indeed, if you praise God a hundred times Praise be to Him, which is better than a hundred saddled and bridled horses being carried for the sake of God Almighty.\n(Nasa’i 10680 and Ibn Majah 3810)"
"29999","(2999) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: A man from the people of the mosques narrated to me who kissed the skulls. He said: : I was informed that Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him, used to say: Oh God, I have no power for myself what I hope for, nor am I able to do with it. I pay what I hate, and the good becomes in the hands of others, and I become dependent on what I earned, and there is no poor person poorer than me, so do not make My affliction is in my religion, and do not make this world your greatest concern, and do not impose authority over me who does not have mercy on me."
"30000","(30,000) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to me, he said: It was mentioned on the authority of some of the prophets that he said: Oh God, do not burden me. Ask for what You have not decreed for me, and whatever provision You have decreed for me, then bring it to me with ease and well-being from You, and reconcile me with what you have reconciled. With it are the righteous, for only you are the most righteous of the righteous."
"30001","(30001) Zaid bin Harun told us, Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala bin Al-Shakhir, that Noah and those after him They were seeking refuge from the temptations of the Antichrist."
"30002","(30002) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, on the authority of Suhaim ibn Nawfal, who said: While we were at Abdullah, when a Bedouin child came to her master while we were showing a Qur’an, and she said: Why should you sit when so-and-so has fallen asleep? With his eyes, so he left him tossing around in the house as if he were in a pot. Get up and seek a sorcerer. Abdullah said: Do not seek a sorcerer and blow into it. His right nostril four, and three in his left nostril, and say: There is no problem, there is no problem. Take away the tragedy, Lord of people. Heal, You are the healer. No. No one removes harm except you. He said: So he left, then returned to us. He said: I said, “I did not command me,” and I did not come until he had urinated, urinated, and eaten."
"30003","(30003) Wakī’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murā narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Taliq ibn Qais al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his supplications: O Lord, help me, and do not Help me, and help me, and do not support me, and plot against me, and do not plot against me, and guide me and facilitate guidance for me, and help me against Whoever transgresses against me, my Lord, make me thankful to you, remembrance of you, fearful of you, obedient to you, hiding to you, seeking refuge in you. Repenting, my Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sins, answer my supplication, guide my heart, establish my proof, and guide my tongue. And the generosity of my heart flows. (Abu Dawud 15051 Tirmidhi 3551)"
"30004","(30004) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Abbad, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: I came to the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he performed ablution and prayed, then he said: O God, forgive me my sins, expand my abode and bless me. I have a livelihood. (Nasa’i 9908. Ahmad 375)"
"30005","(30005) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make these supplications: O God, forgive me my sin, my ignorance, and my extravagance. Concerning my matter, and you are more knowledgeable about it than I am, O God, forgive me my seriousness and my jest, my mistakes and my intentionality, and all of that is with me.\n(Bukhari 6398 and Ahmad 417)"
"30006","(30006) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, benefit me with what you have taught me, and teach me what will benefit me, and increase me in knowledge, and praise be to Him. To God in every condition, and I seek refuge in God from the torment of the Fire. (Tirmidhi 3599, Ibn Majah 251)"
"30007","(30007) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Othman bin Abu Al-Aas and a woman from Qais said that they heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of them said: I heard him saying: O God, forgive. I have my sins, my sins, and my will, and the other said: I heard him say: O God, I seek Your guidance to guide my affairs, and I seek refuge in You. From the evil of myself. (Ahmad 21. Ibn Hibban 901)"
"30008","(30008) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Rushdin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Juwayriyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by her during the lunch prayer, or after the lunch prayer. And he remembered God, so he returned when the day had risen, or he said: The day was halfway through, and he was like that, so he said: I have said since I got up Four words from you, three times, that are more and more likely, or more weighty, than what you said: Glory be to God, according to the number of His creation, Glory be to God, satisfied. Himself, Glory be to God, the adornment of His throne, Glory be to God, the ink of His words. (Muslim 79 Tirmidhi 3555)"
"30009","(30009) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Basri, who said: He used to say: The Prophet used to pray. May God bless him and grant him peace. He prays: O God, forgive me, O God, have mercy on me, O God, guide me, O God, guide me, O God, protect me, O God. Bless me"
"30010","(30010) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, provide us with Your bounty, and do not deprive us of Your provision, and bless for us what You have provided for us. And put our desire in what is with You, and put our wealth in ourselves. (Abu Naim 66)"
"30011","(30011) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mus’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Musab, on the authority of Ali bin Husayn and others, who said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: O God, remove my stumbling, cover my faults, secure my splendor, and suffice me. Whoever wrongs me, and help me from those who wronged me, and show me my revenge for it."
"30012","(30012) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Abdullah bin Amir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say: Oh God, I ask you because you are the first, so nothing. before you, and the last, there is nothing after you, and the apparent, there is nothing above you, and the hidden, there is nothing below you, that you may pay off our debt. And to free us from poverty."
"30013","(30013) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to say: O God, help me in remembering You, thanking You, and worshiping You well, and I seek refuge in You from I am overcome by religion or an enemy, and I seek refuge in You from being overcome by men. (Abu Dawud 1517, Ahmed 244)"
"30014","(30014) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’i, who said: They made me Ali. Behind him, then he walked towards the heat, then he raised his head to the sky and said: Forgive me my sins, for no one forgives sins. Other than you, why did he turn to me and make you laugh? I said: O Commander of the Faithful, do you ask for forgiveness from your Lord and make you laugh when you turn to me? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, carried me behind him, then walked with me to the side of the heat, then he raised his head to the heavens. He said: O God, forgive me my sins, for no one forgives sins except you. Then he turned to me and laughed, so I said: O Messenger of God. Do you seek forgiveness from your Lord and do you turn to me to make you laugh? He said: I laughed because of the laughter of my Lord, because of His amazement towards His servant, because he knows that no one forgives sins except Him. (Abu Dawud 2595. Tirmidhi 3446)"
"30015","(30015) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: If one of you wants to perform a pilgrimage, let him say: Oh God, I ask You for help through Your knowledge and I seek authority from You through Your ability, and I ask You of Your bounty, for You are able, and I am not able and You know. And I do not know, and You are the Knower of the Unseen. Oh God, if this matter that You have intended is good for me in my religion and my livelihood and good My end, make it easy for me and bless me in it, and if other than that is good, then decree good for me wherever it may be, then Satisfy me with what you have decreed. (Bazzar 1583)"
"30016","(30016) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to me, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir. Abdullah bin Al-Hasan narrates, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us istikharah as He teaches us a surah from the Qur’an. He said: If one of you intends to do a matter, let him pray two rak’ahs other than the obligatory ones, and then name the matter. And he says: Oh God, I ask You for guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek guidance from You through Your ability, and I ask You of Your great bounty, for You are You are able, and I am not able, and You know, and I am not aware, and You are the Knower of the unseen. Oh God, if this matter is good for me in my religion And the outcome of my affair, ordain it for me, and make it easy for me, and bless me in it, even if it is evil in my religion and the outcome of my affair So turn it away from me, and turn me away from it, and ordain for me what is good wherever it is, then be pleased with it. (Bukhari 1162 and Abu Dawud 1533)"
"30017","(30017) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: If one of you wants to meet the pilgrim, let him say: Oh God, I ask You for guidance by Your knowledge and I seek guidance from You by Your ability and I ask You of Your grace, for You are able, and I am not able and You know. And I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. Oh God, if this matter which You have intended is good for me in my religion and my livelihood and good Then make it easy for me and bless me therein, and if other than that is good, then decree the good for me wherever it is and He has satisfied me. With it"
"30018","(30018) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When you ask God, ask Him with the insides of your palms, and do not ask Him with the outward appearance."
"30019","(30019) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shehr, who said: The matter is like this, and he extended his palm towards his face, and seeking refuge Thus, the heart suffices."
"30020","(30020) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salama narrated to us, Bishr bin Harb narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to supplicate with knowledge and raise his hand in this way, making a clear appearance of what Its face, and its interior is from what is next to the earth. (Ahmad 85. Tayalisi 2174)"
"30021","(30021) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Sincerity This is how he pointed with his finger, and the supplications are like this, meaning he gestures with the inside of his palms, and the Istikhara is like this and he raised His hands and his backs are his face."
"30022","(30022) Affan narrated to us, Wahib narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ajlan narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad Ibn Malik, on the authority of her maternal uncle Bint Hakim, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If When one of you stays in a house, he says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created. It will not harm him in that house in the slightest. He leaves from there. (Muslim 2080, Ahmed 409)"
"30023","(30023) Ubaid bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Mikhraq, who said: I heard Qais bin Abaya, on the authority of A servant of Saad, on the authority of Saad, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There will be a people who will attack... Prayers (Abu Dawud 1475. Ahmed 183)"
"30024","(30024) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Saeed Al-Jariri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Naama, that Abdullah bin Mughaffal heard his son saying: Oh God, I ask you about the white palace on the right side of Paradise when you enter it, so he said: My son, ask God for the Garden and seek refuge with him from the Fire, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There will be A people who resort to supplication. (Abu Dawud 97 Ahmed 55)"
"30025","(30025) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Because I say, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greater, more beloved to me than anything upon which the sun rises. (Muslim 2072. Tirmidhi 3597)"
"30026","(30026) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Huraira, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Two words that are light on the tongue and heavy in the scale, two words that are beloved to the Most Gracious: Glory be to Him. God and praise be to Him, Glory be to God the Great. (Bukhari 6406. Muslim 2072)"
"30027","(30027) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Hani ibn Uthman narrating, on the authority of his mother Humaidah bint Yasir, on the authority of Her grandmother, Yusira, who was one of the female emigrants, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: May you be With glorification, greatness, and sanctification, and hold them together with your fingertips. Indeed, they will come on the Day of Resurrection as being asked to speak, and not You neglect and forget mercy."
"30028","(30028) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Salem, on the authority of Awn bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, or on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Those who are mentioned from the majesty of God from His glorification. And the praise, the greatness, and the night, they coincide around the throne, for they have a sound like the sound of bees. They are mentioned. With their companions, or does not one of you like that there should not cease to be something with the Most Merciful that reminds him of him? (Ibn Majah 3809. Ahmad 271)"
"30029","(30029) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj Al-Sawaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever says, Glory be to God, the Great, a palm tree or a tree will be planted for him in Paradise.\n(Tirmidhi 3464 and Ibn Hibban 826)"
"30030","(30030) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, Malik ibn Anas told us, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says a hundred times on a day, Glory be to God and with praise be to Him, his sins will be forgiven. Even if it were like sea foam. (Bukhari 64050 Muslim 2071)"
"30031","(30031) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri. On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Shall I not tell you that I love speech? To God? I said: O Messenger of God, tell me the most beloved speech to God. He said: The most beloved speech to God is: Glory be to God and praise be to Him.\n(Muslim 2093. Tirmidhi 3593)"
"30032","(30032) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, who said: He came A man of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned that he was not able to learn from the Qur’an, and he asked him something that would suffice. With the Qur’an, and he said to him: Say, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greatest, and there is no power but By God\n(Abu Dawud 828, Ahmed 353)"
"30033","(30033) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Mahdi bin Maimun narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Yahya bin Aqeel, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Du’ali, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: With all Your praise is sincere. \n(Muslim 498 and Ahmad 168)"
"30034","(30034) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah He said: Because I say: Glory be to God and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greater, more beloved to me than to give dinars in charity."
"30035","(30035) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Misra, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: Abdullah said: Because I recite glorifications that are dearer to me than spending dinars in the name of God Almighty."
"30036","(30036) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: Because What I say means: Glory be to God and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greater, more beloved to me than carrying on her Iddah of Horses with their horses."
"30037","(30037) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, who said: If he said The servant said: Glory be to God, the angels said: And with praise be to Him. So when he said: Glory be to God and with praise be to Him, send blessings upon him, and Abu Asama, peace be upon him."
"30038","(30038) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Shall I not teach you what Noah taught his son? They said: Yes, he said: I command you to say: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is above all. A mighty thing, for if the heavens were in a cup, they would swing it, and if they were a ring, they would break it, and your command glorifies God. And you praise Him, for it is the prayer of creation and the glorification of creation, and by it the creation is provided. (Bukhari 548, Ahmed 169)"
"30039","(30039) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Praise be to God, praise be to God in A believer’s newspaper is better than letting it flow, or having the mountains of the world move with it."
"30040","(30040) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Al-Izar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: He said, I heard him say: Saying “Tasbiha” at the request of a pilgrim is better than saying “Tasbih” at the request of a pilgrim, rather than saying “Tasbih” to a pure man in a single year, or to a housewife."
"30041","(30041) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Afaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Is any of you unable to recite the tasbih with water? Glory be to Him and there will be a thousand praises to Him."
"30042","(30042) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, who said: A man from Muhammad’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Whoever says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, I ask forgiveness from God and I repent to Him, it will be recorded for him. On a piece of parchment, then a musk seal was printed on it, and it was not broken until He brought it to Him on the Day of Resurrection."
"30043","(30043) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Hisham Abi Abdullah informed me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: It is more beloved to me to say “Tasbeeh” a hundred times than to give a hundred dinars in charity to the poor."
"30044","(30044) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata’. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Sawda: Glory be to God every morning ten, and Akbar ten, and praise be to Him ten. And you said: Forgive me ten times, for he is saying: I have done, I have done."
"30045","(30045) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Al-Janni, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us: Is any of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds a day? A questioner asked him: How can one of us earn a thousand good deeds? He said: He glorifies God a hundred times, then a thousand good deeds are recorded for him, or A thousand sins will be removed from him. (Muslim 2073. Ahmad 180)"
"30046","(30046) Zaid bin Harun told us, Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: The best saying is Subhanahu al-Hadith. He said: I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman. And the hadith did not Subhanahu. He said: The man and the people glorify Him. They talk to you."
"30047","(30047) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: We were With Saad bin Malik, he became silent and said: You have become silent like this, like the Nile and the Euphrates were watered. He said: We said: What happened to you? He said: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest."
"30048","(30048) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: If the servant says: Praise Thank God very much. The king said: How should I write? He said: He says: Write down for him My mercy, abundantly, and when the servant says: Allah is the Greatest, the Greatest, the angel says: How do I write? He said: Write my mercy abundantly. And when he said: Glory be to God abundantly, the angel said: How shall I write? He said: Write down My mercy upon him abundantly."
"30049","(30049) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Abi Yahnus, on the authority of Abu Darda’, who said: Bakh, Bakh. For five: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, God is greatest, and a righteous son dies."
"30050","(30050) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’ Al-Jashmi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah bin Masoud says: Glory be to God, the number of pebbles."
"30051","(30051) Abu Dawud narrated to us Omar bin Saad, on the authority of Yunus bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: Whoever says, Glory be to God, the Great, and with praise be to Him, palm trees will be planted for him in Paradise."
"30052","(30052) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka’b, On the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The master of seeking forgiveness is to say: O God, you are my Lord and I am Your servant, there is no god but You. You created me and I am your servant. I have adhered to Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your blessing upon me and I acknowledge Your sins, so forgive me. No one can forgive sins except You."
"30053","(30053) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, saying: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to me, saying: Al-Mughirah ibn Sa’id ibn narrated to me. Nawfal, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Shall I direct you to the master of seeking forgiveness? To say: Oh God, You are his God, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I adhere to Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge Beware of the evil of what I have done, and I acknowledge your blessing upon me, and I acknowledge my sins, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You, there is no servant who says it and his destiny comes to him in his day before the evening, or in his evening before the morning. Unless he is one of the people of Paradise. (Tabarani 7189)"
"30054","(30054) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I complained to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, my tongue moved and he said: Where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? Indeed, I seek forgiveness from God a hundred times every day.\n(Ahmad 394, Darmi 2723)"
"30055","(30055) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him a hundred times today. (Ibn Majah 3815. An-Nasa’i 10268)"
"30056","(30056) Abdullah bin Narrated to us, Nimir Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If we were to count the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the assembly, he would say: My Lord, forgive me and turn to me in repentance. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Forgiving. A hundred times (Abu Dawud 1511, Ahmed 21)"
"30057","(30057) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: I heard Al-Aghar and he was one of the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to Ibn Umar. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him a hundred times today. (Muslim 2075, Abu Dawud 1510)"
"30058","(30058) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Mughirah bin Abi Al-Hurr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Burda, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came while we were sitting and said: I never woke up in the morning without asking God’s forgiveness for me. A hundred times (Ahmad 410 and Ibn Majah 3816)"
"30059","(30059) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: Abu Darda’ used to say: Blessed is he who A summary of asking for forgiveness was found in his newspaper. (Nasa’i 10289)"
"30060","(30060) Affan narrated to us, Bukair bin Abi Al-Sumait narrated to us, Mansour bin Zazan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: Whoever says: I ask forgiveness from God, there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting, and I repent to Him five times, will be forgiven. For him, even if there is something like sea foam on him."
